{"parentUuid":"0e26801f-afdb-4ec2-9dec-607d1b339b5f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtEACh1UqvchQVJoNURt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3501,"cache_read_input_tokens":328172,"output_tokens":1815,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1004},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3501,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1815,"cache_read_input_tokens":328172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3501},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13349,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"66a5ec24-2d75-4d76-9e3b-25ddfd8a11d9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgtEACR935TZe8rn8zukn","requestRef":"abbb9c0b-4d18-474b-bb35-09788059da87","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"04f7727c-4d1f-4e63-bfc4-80913f5c097d","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:32:58.544Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"04f7727c-4d1f-4e63-bfc4-80913f5c097d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtEACh1UqvchQVJoNURt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not terrible. It gets the audience right, but its shape conflicts with what you just described, so it needs changes. I read `courier:changeset-analyzer` 3.0.3 as installed. I haven't run it on our diffs yet, so this is a read of its instructions, not a test.\n\n**What it gets right**\n- It writes for a consumer deciding whether the change affects them, and bans engineering language (\"refactored X\") in summaries.\n- It tells internal-only changes apart from user-visible ones.\n- Breaking changes must say old behavior, new behavior and what the caller does.\n- It warns against both bundling unrelated topics and fragmenting one effort.\n\n**What conflicts with your direction**\n- **Hard length caps.** The summary is capped at 200 characters, \"one sentence for minor\", \"one clause for patch\". That is the prescriptive target you don't want, and it would crush a feature like the release PR into one sentence.\n- **Flat output.** The summary is a single string, so it can't produce a lead with sections, bullets and sub-bullets.\n- **Per diff, not per outcome.** It splits a diff into topics, but one feature spans several PRs. It has no way to say \"update the existing entry\" or \"this doesn't need a changeset\".\n- **No audience sections.** Nothing asks whether the entry matters to someone upgrading, scripting or setting up.\n- **No required \"why it matters\".** The agent's own backstory complains about release notes that say what changed but not why, yet the output rules don't require the why.\n\n**One thing to verify.** The agent says to load `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` first, and I didn't find it in the 3.0.3 install. I saw a path that looks like it is under a codex copy of the plugin. If it's missing from the installed one, the agent runs without its decision table.\n\n**What I'd change**\n1. Replace the length caps with a principle: detail proportional to what a reader needs.\n2. Let the summary carry a lead plus optional sections and bullets.\n3. Add outcome-level granularity: update an existing entry, or recommend no changeset.\n4. Add the \"why it matters\" and \"who needs to act\" requirements, and a few before and after examples.\n5. Check that the shared reference ships with the plugin.\n\nI'd run it once on #483's diff first, so we change it based on evidence. That plugin is outside this repo, so editing it is your call.\n\nneeds input: should I run the courier changeset agent on #483 as a test, and do you want me to propose the plugin edits?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3501,"cache_read_input_tokens":328172,"output_tokens":1815,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1004},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3501,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1815,"cache_read_input_tokens":328172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3501},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"66a5ec24-2d75-4d76-9e3b-25ddfd8a11d9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgtEACR935TZe8rn8zukn","requestRef":"abbb9c0b-4d18-474b-bb35-09788059da87","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e38fb00-78e8-40b4-bf48-5c1ab0fa99e0","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:32:59.607Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"exter