ull_request_that_added_it\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptance_criteria_met\": [\"unlinked\"],\n      \"breaking_changes\": [],\n      \"commits\": [],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Semver guide row: 'New optional schema field -> minor' (ReleasePreview ChangeKind::Changeset gains optional `pr`, serde default, skipped when None, so old preview files still load) plus a new consumer-visible capability in the release PR body; chosen new-capability over behavior-change because no existing output is altered for changes without a PR (those render unchanged). One topic: the changeset-to-PR lookup, preview field, PR body rendering and docs all exist because of the single PR-link feature (check 3; no spec/plan linked). Docs/spec edits (docs/architecture/versioning.md, docs/specs/release.json) are the same topic's self-description, not separate. Not attributed or unresolved: none. Limitations a user may hit: changesets pushed directly (no merge commit or trailing (#N) subject) get no link; only first-parent history is read. Diff has no commit SHAs, so commits is empty. The existing .changeset/change-pr-links.md in the diff is two sentences; this summary is held to one.\"\n    }\n  ]\n  \n  Instruction friction (3 lines):\n  1. The load_first path `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` did not resolve in the worktree; I had to search the plugins directory for it. A resolvable path would help.\n  2. The semver table is plugin/schema-oriented (agents, skills, schemas) with no rows for a CLI's flags, output formats or serialized files. I mapped the new optional preview field to \"new optional schema field -> minor\" by analogy, and the guide has no row for CLI output changes.\n  3. The \"one sentence for minor\" cap plus the 200-char limit forced me to choose between the visible PR-body change and the preview-file field, and to omit the direct-push limitation (put in `reasoning`, which is not forwarded). That limitation is arguably what a user needs to know.\n</agent-message>"}
