{"parentUuid":"7feed946-0742-4895-bd71-aebab3b995b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtEKZJGA5AfnPdsg43Zo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The courier agent is better than I was on one point, and its own rules got in its way on the rest. Its output for #483:\n\n> The release PR now shows `#N` beside each change, linking the pull request that added its changeset; the `--emit-preview` file gains an optional `pr` field.\n\n**Where it did well**\n- It named the link and where it appears, which my versions never did.\n- It found a limit users will hit: changesets pushed directly with no pull request get no link.\n- It classed the change as a minor new capability, which is right.\n\n**Where its instructions hurt it**\n- **Length cap:** \"one sentence for minor\" plus the 200-character limit forced it to squeeze a user-facing change and a scripting detail into one line. It then left the direct-push limitation in a scratchpad that is never forwarded.\n- **Missing why:** it never says why the link helps.\n- **Missing reference:** the shared reference it is told to load first didn't resolve, so it had to search for it.\n- **Wrong semver table:** the table is built for agents and schemas, with no rows for a CLI's flags, output or serialized files, so it had to map by analogy.\n\nThat matches my read: the plugin needs changes. It was written for per-diff, one-line summaries, not the layered, audience-aware entries you described.\n\n**A draft for #483's changeset, not written to a file:**\n\n```\nLinks each change in the release PR to the pull request that added it.\n\n- Shown as `#123` next to the change, so you can open the review and discussion behind it\n- A changeset added without a pull request (a direct push) gets no link\n- For scripts: the `--emit-preview` file has an optional `pr` for each change\n```\n\n**Next steps, if you agree**\n1. Change the plugin: drop the caps, allow a lead plus bullets and sections, add \"why it matters\" and \"who must act\", add CLI rows to the semver table, and fix the reference path. This is outside this repo, so it's your call.\n2. Write the changeset set (#483 and #486) using the agent with the new rules, so the text comes from the agent rather than me.\n\nneeds input: should I propose the plugin edits as a diff for you to review, and does the draft above read right for #483?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1572,"cache_read_input_tokens":335834,"output_tokens":1135,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":437},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1135,"cache_read_input_tokens":335834,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1572},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dfa73a0b-cbdb-41c0-9dfd-67fe4bbd01fe","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgtEKYvSPdcArMTwaH4LH","requestRef":"bb59bad8-64e0-4865-b773-222c0a661608","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"96343d3e-4b74-4666-8161-328497deb774","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:35:00.723Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
