{"parentUuid":"3e98942d-f7bc-44a9-b75d-663e10f7d2cc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01XjEutgQVDah67ip17ogmic","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/gabe/projects/wisp-plugins && rtk read 'shared/schemas/changeset@2.json'; echo; rtk ls plugins/courier/skills; sed -n 1,50p plugins/courier/skills/changeset/SKILL.md; cat shared/references/authoring/voice.md | head -60\",\"dangerouslyDisableSandbox\":true}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":22},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0e9e180b-1bed-4ef2-9734-860874671371","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:54:12.217Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"3e98942d-f7bc-44a9-b75d-663e10f7d2cc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"015887c6-8c9e-46c8-a166-f9ca109a581f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjEutgQVDah67ip17ogmic","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"$id\": \"changeset@2\",\n  \"title\": \"Changeset\",\n  \"description\": \"Describes what was changed in an implementation and why, classified from a consumer's perspective. Supersedes changeset@1 — adds required consumer_impact and semver_impact, set once at authoring time rather than re-derived at release time. Produced by courier's changeset-analyzer, consumed by courier's release-summarizer and by sentinel.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"summary\", \"consumer_impact\", \"semver_impact\", \"files_changed\", \"acceptance_criteria_met\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"maxLength\": 200,\n      \"description\": \"Description of what changed, from the consumer's perspective. Length and detail scale with semver_impact: one clause for patch/internal-only, one sentence for minor, full detail for major. Under 200 characters.\"\n    },\n    \"consumer_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"behavior-change\", \"new-capability\", \"internal-only\"],\n      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\n    },\n    \"semver_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"major\", \"minor\", \"patch\", \"none\"],\n      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n    },\n    \"files_changed\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"Paths of files added, modified, or deleted\"\n    },\n    \"tests_added\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"Paths of test files added or modified\"\n    },\n    \"acceptance_criteria_met\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"IDs from spec@1.acceptance_criteria that this changeset satisfies\"\n    },\n    \"criteria_evidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"criterion_id\", \"test_file\", \"implementation_file\"],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"criterion_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"test_file\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"test_line\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n          \"implementation_file\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"implementation_line\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }\n        }\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Per-criterion evidence trail: exactly where each acceptance_criteria_met ID is tested and implemented. When sourced from implementer's own build, test_line and implementation_line are exact. When reconstructed from a diff with no smith run behind it, file-level entries without line numbers are acceptable rather than fabricating precision that was never observed. A criterion may have more than one entry when it is proven in more than one place.\"\n    },\n    \"breaking_changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"Public API or behavior changes that break existing callers. Each entry states old behavior, new behavior, and what the caller does about it.\"\n    },\n    \"commits\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"Git SHAs of commits in this changeset\"\n    },\n    \"linked_spec\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"linked_plan\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"linked_requirement\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"ID of the requirement@1 this change ultimately traces back to. Propagated from spec@1.linked_requirement via plan@1.linked_requirement when available.\"\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Agent scratchpad — not consumed downstream\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nchangeset/\ncommit/\npost-review/\npr/\nreceive-feedback/\nrelease/\n---\nname: changeset\ndescription: >-\n  Trigger when the user asks to add a changeset or document a change: \"add a changeset\", \"document this change\", \"what changed here\". Extracts the consumer-facing meaning of a diff: classifies consumer_impact (behavior-change, new-capability, internal-only) and semver_impact (major, minor, patch, none) per shared/references/delivery/changesets.md's decision table, then writes a summary scaled to that classification. A diff spanning multiple independent topics — common on a backlog/catch-up run, not just a single PR — produces one changeset per topic, not one bundled entry. When the change came via smith, pass along implementer's criteria_evidence — changeset-analyzer uses those exact locations instead of reconstructing approximate ones from the diff.\nversion: 2.1.0\n---\n\n# Courier — Changeset\n\n<overview>\nA changeset is the changelog entry, written once at authoring time and later aggregated — not rewritten — into a release. `changeset-analyzer` first checks how many independent topics the diff actually contains, then classifies consumer_impact and semver_impact per topic before writing anything, and scales each summary's detail to match: terse for a patch, one sentence for a minor, full old-behavior-to-new-behavior-to-required-action detail for a major. Delegates entirely to `changeset-analyzer`.\n</overview>\n\n<dispatch>\n| Agent | Model / Effort | Delegate When |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **changeset-analyzer** | sonnet / medium | A git diff needs one or more structured `changeset@2` entries with consumer/semver classification and acceptance criteria mapping. |\n</dispatch>\n\n<references>\n`shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, the Consumer Impact Classification table, the Semver Decision Guide, and the voice standard for this artifact.\n</references>\n\n<io>\n**Consumes**: git diff (a single PR's, or a larger backlog/catch-up diff since the last release), optionally a linked `spec@1`, optionally smith's aggregated `criteria_evidence`\n**Produces**: one or more `changeset@2` entries conforming to `shared/schemas/changeset@2.json` — one per independent topic found in the diff, never one entry bundling unrelated topics together. Route to `courier/pr` or `courier/release` depending on the next stage.\n</io>\n# Documentation Voice\n\nWrite for the person who must use, review, or maintain the artifact. Be succinct, friendly, direct, and technically honest.\n\n## Choose the reader\n\n| Artifact | Lead with | Include when relevant |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| User guide or README | What the user can do and when to use it | Prerequisites, examples, limits, recovery |\n| Contributor or architecture doc | System responsibility and decision | Boundaries, invariants, tradeoffs, evidence |\n| PR or review | Outcome and approval-relevant risk | Verification, gaps, migration, follow-up |\n| Changeset or release note | Observable consumer impact | Old behavior, new behavior, required action |\n| Decision record | The decision and the alternative rejected | Context, the causal because, consequences, enforcement, supersession |\n| Reference | Decision the guidance supports | Applicability, evidence, refutation, disposition |\n\nUse the reader's language. User-facing docs describe tasks and outcomes before internal agents, schemas, or implementation details. Contributor docs may use precise engineering terms when those terms help the reader act.\n\n## Voice\n\n- Lead with the outcome. Add context only when it changes understanding or action.\n- Use active voice, present tense, and second person for instructions.\n- Prefer familiar, concrete words. Define unavoidable domain terms once.\n- Keep one main idea per sentence and one actionable rule per list item.\n- Be friendly without ceremony: respectful, calm, and helpful; no praise, apology, or enthusiasm added as padding.\n- Practice radical candor: state the concern, evidence, consequence, and confidence. Label blockers plainly. Do not manufacture praise, hide impact behind soft language, or imply certainty the evidence does not support.\n- State mechanisms, behavior, and observed results instead of promotional adjectives.\n- Let length follow the reader's need. Preserve non-obvious rationale, constraints, migration steps, and risks.\n\n## Structure\n\n- Use the smallest form that makes the relationship clear: prose for one connected idea, bullets for short parallel items, tables for repeated fields, and diagrams for structure or flow.\n- Split a bullet when it contains independently actionable rules. Convert it to prose when its explanation is more important than enumeration.\n- Use numbered steps only when order affects correctness.\n- State a rationale once, next to the decision it changes.\n- Link to authoritative detail instead of copying it.\n\n## Cut\n\n- Conversational preambles, scene-setting, and process narration.\n- Restatements of a title, signature, diff, table, or preceding sentence.\n- Synonymous claims that add emphasis but no information.\n- Hedge phrases such as “essentially,” “basically,” “in order to,” and “it is worth noting.”\n- Empty quality claims such as “robust,” “seamless,” “powerful,” or “comprehensive” without the mechanism or evidence that earns them.\n- Rhetorical hooks, inflated contrasts, and adjective clusters.\n\nWords are warning signs, not a substitute for judgment. Keep a word when it is the clearest accurate term; remove it when it stands in for evidence.\n\n## Self-check\n\n- Can the intended reader find the outcome first?\n- Does each sentence change what the reader knows or does?\n- Are material concerns direct, evidenced, and calibrated?\n- Can any paragraph, bullet, heading, or example be removed without loss?\n- Does user-facing text explain user impact before internal machinery?\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"86f4f160-c5ac-42e0-b6c3-f6dcfeec4038","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:54:15.492Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"$id\": \"changeset@2\",\n  \"title\": \"Changeset\",\n  \"description\": \"Describes what was changed in an implementation and why, classified from a consumer's perspective. Supersedes changeset@1 — adds required consumer_impact and semver_impact, set once at authoring time rather than re-derived at release time. Produced by courier's changeset-analyzer, consumed by courier's release-summarizer and by sentinel.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"summary\", \"consumer_impact\", \"semver_impact\", \"files_changed\", \"acceptance_criteria_met\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"maxLength\": 200,\n      \"description\": \"Description of what changed, from the consumer's perspective. Length and detail scale with semver_impact: one clause for patch/internal-only, one sentence for minor, full detail for major. Under 200 characters.\"\n    },\n    \"consumer_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"behavior-change\", \"new-capability\", \"internal-only\"],\n      \"description\": \"Whether this change is observable to someone outside this repo. See shared/references/changesets.md for classification rules.\"\n    },\n    \"semver_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"major\", \"minor\", \"patch\", \"none\"],\n      \"description\": \"Version bump this change requires, per the Semver Decision Guide in shared/references/changesets.md. release-summarizer takes max(semver_impact) across a release's changesets rather than re-deriving it.\"\n    },\n    \"files_changed\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"Paths of files added, modified, or deleted\"\n    },\n    \"tests_added\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"Paths of test files added or modified\"\n    },\n    \"acceptance_criteria_met\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"IDs from spec@1.acceptance_criteria that this changeset satisfies\"\n    },\n    \"criteria_evidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"criterion_id\", \"test_file\", \"implementation_file\"],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"criterion_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"test_file\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"test_line\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n          \"implementation_file\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"implementation_line\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }\n        }\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Per-criterion evidence trail: exactly where each acceptance_criteria_met ID is tested and implemented. When sourced from implementer's own build, test_line and implementation_line are exact. When reconstructed from a diff with no smith run behind it, file-level entries without line numbers are acceptable rather than fabricating precision that was never observed. A criterion may have more than one entry when it is proven in more than one place.\"\n    },\n    \"breaking_changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"Public API or behavior changes that break existing callers. Each entry states old behavior, new behavior, and what the caller does about it.\"\n    },\n    \"commits\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"description\": \"Git SHAs of commits in this changeset\"\n    },\n    \"linked_spec\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"linked_plan\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"linked_requirement\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"ID of the requirement@1 this change ultimately traces back to. Propagated from spec@1.linked_requirement via plan@1.linked_requirement when available.\"\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Agent scratchpad — not consumed downstream\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nchangeset/\ncommit/\npost-review/\npr/\nreceive-feedback/\nrelease/\n---\nname: changeset\ndescription: >-\n  Trigger when the user asks to add a changeset or document a change: \"add a changeset\", \"document this change\", \"what changed here\". Extracts the consumer-facing meaning of a diff: classifies consumer_impact (behavior-change, new-capability, internal-only) and semver_impact (major, minor, patch, none) per shared/references/delivery/changesets.md's decision table, then writes a summary scaled to that classification. A diff spanning multiple independent topics — common on a backlog/catch-up run, not just a single PR — produces one changeset per topic, not one bundled entry. When the change came via smith, pass along implementer's criteria_evidence — changeset-analyzer uses those exact locations instead of reconstructing approximate ones from the diff.\nversion: 2.1.0\n---\n\n# Courier — Changeset\n\n<overview>\nA changeset is the changelog entry, written once at authoring time and later aggregated — not rewritten — into a release. `changeset-analyzer` first checks how many independent topics the diff actually contains, then classifies consumer_impact and semver_impact per topic before writing anything, and scales each summary's detail to match: terse for a patch, one sentence for a minor, full old-behavior-to-new-behavior-to-required-action detail for a major. Delegates entirely to `changeset-analyzer`.\n</overview>\n\n<dispatch>\n| Agent | Model / Effort | Delegate When |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **changeset-analyzer** | sonnet / medium | A git diff needs one or more structured `changeset@2` entries with consumer/semver classification and acceptance criteria mapping. |\n</dispatch>\n\n<references>\n`shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` — changeset format, the Consumer Impact Classification table, the Semver Decision Guide, and the voice standard for this artifact.\n</references>\n\n<io>\n**Consumes**: git diff (a single PR's, or a larger backlog/catch-up diff since the last release), optionally a linked `spec@1`, optionally smith's aggregated `criteria_evidence`\n**Produces**: one or more `changeset@2` entries conforming to `shared/schemas/changeset@2.json` — one per independent topic found in the diff, never one entry bundling unrelated topics together. Route to `courier/pr` or `courier/release` depending on the next stage.\n</io>\n# Documentation Voice\n\nWrite for the person who must use, review, or maintain the artifact. Be succinct, friendly, direct, and technically honest.\n\n## Choose the reader\n\n| Artifact | Lead with | Include when relevant |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| User guide or README | What the user can do and when to use it | Prerequisites, examples, limits, recovery |\n| Contributor or architecture doc | System responsibility and decision | Boundaries, invariants, tradeoffs, evidence |\n| PR or review | Outcome and approval-relevant risk | Verification, gaps, migration, follow-up |\n| Changeset or release note | Observable consumer impact | Old behavior, new behavior, required action |\n| Decision record | The decision and the alternative rejected | Context, the causal because, consequences, enforcement, supersession |\n| Reference | Decision the guidance supports | Applicability, evidence, refutation, disposition |\n\nUse the reader's language. User-facing docs describe tasks and outcomes before internal agents, schemas, or implementation details. Contributor docs may use precise engineering terms when those terms help the reader act.\n\n## Voice\n\n- Lead with the outcome. Add context only when it changes understanding or action.\n- Use active voice, present tense, and second person for instructions.\n- Prefer familiar, concrete words. Define unavoidable domain terms once.\n- Keep one main idea per sentence and one actionable rule per list item.\n- Be friendly without ceremony: respectful, calm, and helpful; no praise, apology, or enthusiasm added as padding.\n- Practice radical candor: state the concern, evidence, consequence, and confidence. Label blockers plainly. Do not manufacture praise, hide impact behind soft language, or imply certainty the evidence does not support.\n- State mechanisms, behavior, and observed results instead of promotional adjectives.\n- Let length follow the reader's need. Preserve non-obvious rationale, constraints, migration steps, and risks.\n\n## Structure\n\n- Use the smallest form that makes the relationship clear: prose for one connected idea, bullets for short parallel items, tables for repeated fields, and diagrams for structure or flow.\n- Split a bullet when it contains independently actionable rules. Convert it to prose when its explanation is more important than enumeration.\n- Use numbered steps only when order affects correctness.\n- State a rationale once, next to the decision it changes.\n- Link to authoritative detail instead of copying it.\n\n## Cut\n\n- Conversational preambles, scene-setting, and process narration.\n- Restatements of a title, signature, diff, table, or preceding sentence.\n- Synonymous claims that add emphasis but no information.\n- Hedge phrases such as “essentially,” “basically,” “in order to,” and “it is worth noting.”\n- Empty quality claims such as “robust,” “seamless,” “powerful,” or “comprehensive” without the mechanism or evidence that earns them.\n- Rhetorical hooks, inflated contrasts, and adjective clusters.\n\nWords are warning signs, not a substitute for judgment. Keep a word when it is the clearest accurate term; remove it when it stands in for evidence.\n\n## Self-check\n\n- Can the intended reader find the outcome first?\n- Does each sentence change what the reader knows or does?\n- Are material concerns direct, evidenced, and calibrated?\n- Can any paragraph, bullet, heading, or example be removed without loss?\n- Does user-facing text explain user impact before internal machinery?","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"77f27ee6-5aee-4628-ae1b-bde8ea9389ab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","branch":"docs/changeset-set","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3e98942d-f7bc-44a9-b75d-663e10f7d2cc","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config"