{"parentUuid":"bdbbe233-1c43-4bbe-b287-22a03eb99782","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtFvsDbtT1GXyeehuhcv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":352320,"output_tokens":2751,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":321},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2751,"cache_read_input_tokens":352320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7245,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"cacafd1b-6f86-48a4-8328-9ae4e385ff6e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgtFvrgs6smsi4SxFsa8V","requestRef":"70594f36-7699-48a2-b6d8-cfa0cf2740c1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a2bb8cb-8665-4dc5-aaa7-6c25d893e8fd","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:56:05.052Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"3a2bb8cb-8665-4dc5-aaa7-6c25d893e8fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtFvsDbtT1GXyeehuhcv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is a prompt you can paste to the other agent. I created one worktree for it at `~/projects/wisp-plugins/.claude/worktrees/layered-changesets` on branch `feat/layered-changesets`, and I have made no edits there. Reuse it or delete it.\n\n````markdown\n# Task: make courier's changeset guidance produce layered, user-valuable entries\n\nRepo: `~/projects/wisp-plugins` (orin-dx/wisp-plugins). Work in a git worktree off `origin/main`, not in the main checkout, which has the owner's uncommitted changes. Commits must be signed (never override signing). Read `AGENTS.md`, `shared/constitution.md` and `docs/adr/README.md` first. Edit authored sources only (generated Codex output is built with `just marketplace-sync`). Finish with `just check` passing and judge it by exit code.\n\n## Why this exists\n\nA Callisto maintainer (Callisto is a release tool) kept writing poor changesets. We tried `courier:changeset-analyzer` on a real diff (a feature that links each change in a release PR to the pull request that added it) and the agent's own rules got in its way:\n\n- **Hard length caps.** The `changeset@2` schema has `summary.maxLength: 200` with \"one clause for patch, one sentence for minor\". The agent and `courier/changeset` skill repeat it. The agent had to choose between the visible change and a scripting detail, and left a real user-facing limitation (changesets pushed directly get no link) in `reasoning`, which is never forwarded.\n- **Flat output.** `summary` is one string, so it cannot carry a lead line plus sections, bullets and sub-bullets.\n- **Per-diff granularity.** The agent splits a diff into topics. Real features span several PRs, and some PRs need no changeset at all. Nothing lets it say \"update the existing entry\" or \"no changeset needed\".\n- **No \"why it matters\".** The agent's own backstory complains about notes that say what changed but not why, but the output contract doesn't require it.\n- **Semver table gaps.** `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md` has rows for agents, skills and schemas only. It has none for a CLI's flags, output formats or serialized files, so the agent mapped by analogy.\n- **Reference not loading.** `load_first` names `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`. In source this resolves through a `plugins/courier/shared -> ../../shared` symlink. The installed Claude copy (`~/.claude/plugins/cache/orin-dx-agent-plugins/courier/3.0.3/`) has no `shared/` at all, so the reference may never load.\n\n## What the maintainer wants (use these as the design goals)\n\nChangelog entries communicate value clearly to users who are upgrading, scripting or setting up. They are easy to scan and still give depth for readers who want it.\n\n- **No hard length targets.** Prescriptive limits don't produce value with LLMs. Replace them with judgment: detail proportional to what the reader needs.\n- **Layered structure when there is enough to say:** a lead line stating the value, then bullets, with sub-bullets for depth, grouped under audience sections where useful (for example what you see, scripting, upgrading). A one-line entry is fine when that is all there is.\n- **Say what it is, why it helps, and what to do.** Name the visible thing (a \"link\", a \"label\", a \"flag\"), where it appears, and the action if any. Vague verbs like \"identifies\" or \"says\" fail this test.\n- **State limits that users will hit.** They belong in the entry, not in a scratchpad.\n- **One entry per user-visible outcome, not per PR.** A feature across several PRs updates one entry. A change that is not user-visible, or fixes something not yet released, gets no changeset. The agent should be able to recommend this.\n- **Consistent voice** across entries, following `shared/references/authoring/voice.md`.\n\n## Outcomes (definition of done)\n\n1. `changeset@2` (or a new `changeset@3` if the change is breaking for consumers; follow the repo's schema-versioning rules) allows a layered summary without a length cap, and its description matches the new behavior. Decide with the ADR/constitution rules whether this is a new schema version, and justify it.\n2. `agents/changeset-analyzer.md` and `skills/changeset/SKILL.md`: remove the \"one clause / one sentence / 200 chars\" rules. Add the audience, why-it-matters and action requirements, the outcome-level granularity (update an entry, or recommend none), and \"limits belong in the entry\". Keep the 5-part agent structure and byte-identical constitution block. Follow instruction economy: one actionable rule per item, no repeated rationale.\n3. `shared/references/delivery/changesets.md`: add semver rows for CLI surface (new flag or command, changed output or exit code, new or changed serialized file) and a short worked example of a layered entry plus a bad-versus-good pair. Keep it under the reference size cap (`just reference-size`).\n4. Downstream consumers (`release-summarizer`, `pr-narrator`, sentinel, anything that reads `changeset@2`) still work with the new summary shape; update them and their tests.\n5. Add or update tests in `tests/` so the new schema and contract are covered.\n6. Bump versions and CHANGELOG for the affected plugins per repo rules (`just versions`).\n\n## Separate investigation, report only, do not fix in this change\n\nConfirm whether Claude installs lose the `shared/` symlink: compare the source plugin dir with `~/.claude/plugins/cache/orin-dx-agent-plugins/courier/3.0.3/`. If `shared/` is missing there, every agent's `load_first` references and schemas fail to load in installed plugins, which affects all plugins. Describe the evidence, the likely cause (ARCHITECTURE.md says Codex bundles dereference symlinks but nothing is said for Claude), and options. Return it as a finding.\n\n## Reinforcing use of the plugins (design, then implement what fits)\n\nIn practice, Claude sessions wrote changesets, commit messages and PR text freehand instead of calling the courier agents. Propose and implement, within this repo, the lightest way to make the right agent the default: sharper trigger wording in the `changeset`, `commit` and `pr` skill descriptions, and a short note in the courier README on when to use each. Do not add Claude hooks (the owner finds them too heavy). Anything that needs changes in the Callisto repo, such as its AGENTS.md or PR template, goes in your report as a recommendation, not a change.\n\n## How to work\n\n- Use mason's agents (`mason:scaffolder` and `mason:auditor`) or the repo's own checks to validate structure; do not invent your own format.\n- Test the result: run `courier:changeset-analyzer` on this diff, a real Callisto PR diff (`gh pr diff 483 --repo orin-dx/callisto`) and confirm the entry names the link, where it appears, why it helps, and the direct-push limit.\n- Report what you changed, evidence for each outcome (commands and exit codes), what you did not do, and any decision you made that the owner should review.\n````\n\nI can also write a shorter version, or a second prompt for the symlink and packaging finding, if you want it handled separately."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":352320,"output_tokens":2751,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":321},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2751,"cache_read_input_tokens":352320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cacafd1b-6f86-48a4-8328-9ae4e385ff6e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgtFvrgs6smsi4SxFsa8V","requestRef":"70594f36-7699-48a2-b6d8-cfa0cf2740c1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf9aee09-5b51-4e1f-81ba-a867a3763fb8","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:56:17.955Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
