{"parentUuid":"f0d228fa-a78b-45e0-bcfb-440672ffdfa1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"50fd4777-05e9-4a02-99bc-1274a388e428","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:57:52.190Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"1914be4b748f180bed10da2b5234290daa819552c8cbda416c2537fb1396264b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll rewrite the set in the agreed shape: a lead line, audience sections, bullets and sub-bullets. The courier agent can't write these yet, because its 200-character cap would flatten them, so I'll draft them and then have a fresh agent with no context read them as a user would."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NUAZCymZGwgbejm2i8s8Yp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/changeset_set2.py","content":"import os\n\nrepo = \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set/\"\ncs = repo + \".changeset/\"\n\nfor name in [\n    \"pr-body-headlines\",\n    \"pr-body-attention\",\n    \"pr-body-publish-plan\",\n    \"pr-labels\",\n    \"version-emit-preview\",\n]:\n    os.remove(cs + name + \".md\")\n\nentries = {\n    \"release-pr-overview\": (\n        \"minor\",\n        \"\"\"The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.\n\n**What you see**\n- Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes folded away\n- A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n- Where merging will publish each package, with a warning if the release would be refused\n- Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n  - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n\n**Scripting**\n- `callisto version --emit-preview <path>` writes the release as JSON\n- `compose-pr-body --preview <path>` builds the PR body from that file\n  - Relative paths resolve against `--cwd`\n- `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` adds the publish section; the release PR action already passes it\n\n**Upgrading**\n- Nothing to change. Start a changeset paragraph with `Breaking:` or `Action:` to have it listed.\"\"\",\n    ),\n    \"changelog-grouped-layout\": (\n        \"minor\",\n        \"\"\"Changelogs group each release's changes by bump, so they are easier to scan.\n\n- Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n- The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n- A package that only released with its group gets one line saying so\n\n**Upgrading**\n- To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\"\"\",\n    ),\n    \"cli-io-consolidation\": (\n        \"patch\",\n        \"\"\"`callisto release` and `release-pr` resolve relative file flags against `--cwd`, so `--cwd` works the same for every flag.\n\n- Before, they resolved against the directory you ran from.\n- If a script passes relative paths together with `--cwd`, make them relative to that directory or absolute.\"\"\",\n    ),\n}\nfor name, (bump, text) in entries.items():\n    with open(cs + name + \".md\", \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(f\"---\\ncallisto-cli: {bump}\\n---\\n\\n{text}\\n\")\nprint(sorted(os.listdir(cs)))\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C6PUZsNc7beiju9wDiLqSj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/changeset_set2.py","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
