{"parentUuid":"b05f8189-89ac-4ef9-b745-34dd69b9dcc0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bee458e7-2ab9-4117-89c2-fe1e13836a84","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\nversion exit 0\ncompose exit 0\n       0\n### 📦 What's Changing\n\n_Also bumped with no direct change of their own (released together via a fixed/linked group): `callisto-fixtures`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-model`._\n\n**3 change(s) across 5 package(s):**\n\n#### 🟡 Minor\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Changelogs group each release's changes by bump, so they are easier to scan.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n- The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n- A package that only released with its group gets one line saying so\n\n**Upgrading**\n- To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\n\nPull request #474\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n**What you see**\n- Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes folded away\n- A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n- Where merging will publish each package, with a warning if the release would be refused\n- Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n  - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n\n**Scripting**\n- `callisto version --emit-preview <path>` writes the release as JSON\n- `compose-pr-body --preview <path>` builds the PR body from that file\n  - Relative paths resolve against `--cwd`\n- `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` adds the publish section; the release PR action already passes it\n\n**Upgrading**\n- Nothing to change. Start a changeset paragraph with `Breaking:` or `Action:` to have it listed.\n\n</details>\n\n#### 🟢 Patch\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>callisto release</code> and <code>release-pr</code> resolve relative file flags against <code>--cwd</code>, so <code>--cwd</code> works the same for every fl…</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n`callisto release` and `release-pr` resolve relative file flags against `--cwd`, so `--cwd` works the same for every flag.\n\n- Before, they resolved against the directory you ran from.\n- If a script passes relative paths together with `--cwd`, make them relative to that directory or absolute.\n\nPull request #475\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Release Workflow Instructions</b></summary>\n(eval):1: ===== not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WybkjSJyA2Yr6pfyEXVSYD"}]},"uuid":"1719f809-8338-4903-8df1-307bbae16e53","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:58:16.260Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\nversion exit 0\ncompose exit 0\n       0\n### 📦 What's Changing\n\n_Also bumped with no direct change of their own (released together via a fixed/linked group): `callisto-fixtures`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-model`._\n\n**3 change(s) across 5 package(s):**\n\n#### 🟡 Minor\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Changelogs group each release's changes by bump, so they are easier to scan.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n- The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n- A package that only released with its group gets one line saying so\n\n**Upgrading**\n- To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\n\nPull request #474\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n**What you see**\n- Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes folded away\n- A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n- Where merging will publish each package, with a warning if the release would be refused\n- Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n  - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n\n**Scripting**\n- `callisto version --emit-preview <path>` writes the release as JSON\n- `compose-pr-body --preview <path>` builds the PR body from that file\n  - Relative paths resolve against `--cwd`\n- `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` adds the publish section; the release PR action already passes it\n\n**Upgrading**\n- Nothing to change. Start a changeset paragraph with `Breaking:` or `Action:` to have it listed.\n\n</details>\n\n#### 🟢 Patch\n\n<details>\n<summary><b><code>callisto release</code> and <code>release-pr</code> resolve relative file flags against <code>--cwd</code>, so <code>--cwd</code> works the same for every fl…</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n`callisto release` and `release-pr` resolve relative file flags against `--cwd`, so `--cwd` works the same for every flag.\n\n- Before, they resolved against the directory you ran from.\n- If a script passes relative paths together with `--cwd`, make them relative to that directory or absolute.\n\nPull request #475\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Release Workflow Instructions</b></summary>\n(eval):1: ===== not found","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ccd90778-d0b0-4acd-8210-69f699338efb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set