{"parentUuid":"34483c96-ce05-433c-bf4f-1dd4967b0ff7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01DSuqo9AGcmn54cCPo5bUym","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"git add -A && git commit -S -q -m \\\"docs: shorten the cwd changeset lead\\\" && sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/render_set.sh; rtk grep -n \\\"Patch\\\" -A12 /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/render_set/body.md | head -20; sed -n 1,42p /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/render_set/CHANGELOG.md\",\"timeout\":300000,\"dangerouslyDisableSandbox\":true}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":19},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cd655004-d567-4df1-9366-72f89373f89f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:58:24.653Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"572aea0c-281b-4a74-a186-f46bc8a4678d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bee458e7-2ab9-4117-89c2-fe1e13836a84","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DSuqo9AGcmn54cCPo5bUym","type":"tool_result","content":"moon run :format-check\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-manifests:format-check (cached, 9b8538e4)\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-fixtures:format-check (cached, a7347515)\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-model:format-check (cached, 1a1faa1e)\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-graph:format-check (cached, fc924409)\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-cli:format-check (cached, cfeb94df)\n\nTasks: 5 completed (5 cached)\n Time: 33ms ❯❯❯❯ to the moon\n\nversion exit 0\ncompose exit 0\n       0\n29:- Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n30-- The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n31-- A package that only released with its group gets one line saying so\n32-\n33-**Upgrading**\n34-- To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\n35-\n36-Pull request #474\n37-\n38-</details>\n39-\n40-<details>\n41-<summary><b>The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n--\n44:- Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes folded away\n45-- A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n46-- Where merging will publish each package, with a warning if the release would be refused\n47-- Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n48-  - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n49-\n# callisto-cli\n\n## 0.19.0\n\n_2026-11-09 · [compare](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/compare/callisto@0.18.0...callisto@0.19.0)_\n\n### Minor Changes\n\n- Changelogs group each release's changes by bump, so they are easier to scan.\n\n  - Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n  - The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n  - A package that only released with its group gets one line saying so\n\n  **Upgrading**\n  - To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\n- The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.\n\n  **What you see**\n  - Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes folded away\n  - A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n  - Where merging will publish each package, with a warning if the release would be refused\n  - Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n    - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n\n  **Scripting**\n  - `callisto version --emit-preview <path>` writes the release as JSON\n  - `compose-pr-body --preview <path>` builds the PR body from that file\n    - Relative paths resolve against `--cwd`\n  - `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` adds the publish section; the release PR action already passes it\n\n  **Upgrading**\n  - Nothing to change. Start a changeset paragraph with `Breaking:` or `Action:` to have it listed.\n\n### Patch Changes\n\n- Relative file flags of `release` and `release-pr` now follow `--cwd`.\n\n  - Before, they resolved against the directory you ran from.\n  - If a script passes relative paths together with `--cwd`, make them relative to that directory or absolute.\n\n## 0.18.0","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"173521da-bd5a-4074-92c6-cb1f6a07befc","timestamp":"2026-11-09T23:58:35.710Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"moon run :format-check\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-manifests:format-check (cached, 9b8538e4)\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-fixtures:format-check (cached, a7347515)\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-model:format-check (cached, 1a1faa1e)\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-graph:format-check (cached, fc924409)\n▮▮▮▮ callisto-cli:format-check (cached, cfeb94df)\n\nTasks: 5 completed (5 cached)\n Time: 33ms ❯❯❯❯ to the moon\n\nversion exit 0\ncompose exit 0\n       0\n29:- Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n30-- The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n31-- A package that only released with its group gets one line saying so\n32-\n33-**Upgrading**\n34-- To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\n35-\n36-Pull request #474\n37-\n38-</details>\n39-\n40-<details>\n41-<summary><b>The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n--\n44:- Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes folded away\n45-- A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n46-- Where merging will publish each package, with a warning if the release would be refused\n47-- Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n48-  - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n49-\n# callisto-cli\n\n## 0.19.0\n\n_2026-11-09 · [compare](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/compare/callisto@0.18.0...callisto@0.19.0)_\n\n### Minor Changes\n\n- Changelogs group each release's changes by bump, so they are easier to scan.\n\n  - Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n  - The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n  - A package that only released with its group gets one line saying so\n\n  **Upgrading**\n  - To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\n- The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.\n\n  **What you see**\n  - Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes folded away\n  - A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n  - Where merging will publish each package, with a warning if the release would be refused\n  - Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n    - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n\n  **Scripting**\n  - `callisto version --emit-preview <path>` writes the release as JSON\n  - `compose-pr-body --preview <path>` builds the PR body from that file\n    - Relative paths resolve against `--cwd`\n  - `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` adds the publish section; the release PR action already passes it\n\n  **Upgrading**\n  - Nothing to change. Start a changeset paragraph with `Breaking:` or `Action:` to have it listed.\n\n### Patch Changes\n\n- Relative file flags of `release` and `release-pr` now follow `--cwd`.\n\n  - Before, they resolved against the directory you ran from.\n  - If a script passes relative paths together with `--cwd`, make them relative to that directory or absolute.\n\n## 0.18.0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b513575d-c0fc-46a6-8be7-e0064944ed48","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","branch":"docs/changeset-set","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"572aea0c-281b-4a74-a186-f46bc8a4678d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
