{"parentUuid":"9b8e29dc-937e-4985-8e39-9da92425cc8e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtGGmc5V2ZoQtkM9FcuB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PjrCGzX9HWS863Q5Pz1i6i","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr486.md","content":"## Summary\n\nThe 0.19.0 changelog had 13 entries, mostly fix-ups to release PR features that have not shipped, and several described how it works instead of what a user gets. This rewrites them as 3 layered entries.\n\n- **The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge**: one entry with What you see, Scripting and Upgrading sections, replacing five.\n- **Changelog grouped layout** and **`--cwd` for relative file flags**: reworded with the action to take on upgrade.\n- Fix-ups to unreleased features are folded in or dropped. Bumps are unchanged: still a minor release.\n- `AGENTS.md` now asks for why it matters to the user, and says a fix to something not yet released gets no changeset.\n\n## Verify\n\n- Rendered the real release PR body and 0.19.0 changelog from these files in a scratch worktree: sections, bullets and sub-bullets display as intended.\n- A reader with no context was given only the 0.19.0 changelog. They described each change, why it matters and the upgrade action correctly, and flagged three vague phrases, which are now reworded.\n- `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0.\n\nNot run: CI. #483 keeps its own small entry for the pull request link, so this entry makes no claim about it before it merges.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2135,"cache_read_input_tokens":366155,"output_tokens":839,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"servi