{"parentUuid":"7a2c1c5c-da77-4cb8-bc09-4f7c7f86ff15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtGJCquKJGcunXxh854h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #486 now has the three layered changesets and an updated description. I haven't touched #483's changeset again.\n\n**The set:**\n- **The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge:** one entry with \"What you see\", \"Scripting\" and \"Upgrading\" sections, in place of five.\n- **Changelog grouped layout:** a lead, three bullets, and the upgrade action (`layout = \"flat\"` keeps the old list).\n- **`--cwd` for relative file flags:** a lead, what it was before, and what a script should change.\n\n**How I checked it:**\n- **Real render:** I ran the real binary on these files in a scratch worktree. The release PR body and the 0.19.0 changelog both show the sections, bullets and sub-bullets as intended, and the pull request links already appear on entries from merged PRs.\n- **Cold read:** an agent with no context saw only the 0.19.0 changelog. It described each change, why it matters and the upgrade action correctly, and flagged three vague phrases. I reworded them: \"refused\" is now \"fail, so you find out before merging\", \"released with its group\" is spelled out, and \"folded away\" is \"collapsed into an expandable block\".\n- **Local checks:** pre-push, lint, doc-check, test and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n\n**For when you're back from the plugins work:**\n- The courier agent didn't write these. Its 200-character cap would flatten them, so I drafted and then tested with a fresh reader. Once the plugin is updated, we can run it on the next changeset and compare.\n- #483's own changeset (\"links each change… to the pull request\") and #485 need no further change from me.\n\nneeds input: review #486 and read the three entries, since that's what users will see."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":368290,"output_tokens":565,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1174,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":368290,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1174},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"19d532a0-d203-4628-be9c-457323bdb1ff","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgtGJCYYTVjDFysXb97Tv","requestRef":"57bd09b5-ab92-4e8c-a745-2a6baa5b2f02","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c027c0f2-6074-4019-9caf-188f7ee6829f","timestamp":"2026-11-10T00:00:51.064Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-set","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"docs/changeset-set","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
