78     Every spec criterion has a test that asserts it\n179     Packages and fixed groups appear and release the way they are configured\n180     The release PR says why it is held\n193     chore(release): version packages\n194     Comments say why, never history\n195     Delete what nothing uses, and tests that assert nothing\n196     The release PR scripts and their tests share one helper\n197     Names and values live in one place\n198     Failures are loud and contracts are pinned to real output\n199     Copies of the same list agree, and a test says so\n212     fix(ci): run the problem matcher test in the Test job, not on the release path\n213     fix(release): classify a failed npm publish as already published only on npm's conflict signals\n214     test(release): prove the npm confirmation passes the publish config to view\n215     test(release): build the pending-contract fixture with the shared release harness\n225     chore(deps): bump taiki-e/install-action from 2.87.30 to 2.88.0 in the routine-actions group\n226     chore(deps): bump the routine-crates group with 5 updates\n233     Generated release workflows run in a downstream repo\n237     Cleanup: dead code, stale docs and narration\n245     Version writes keep what they should\n246     A configured registry destination is honored or refused\n247     The release pipeline runs verification alongside planning and building\n250     Release notes: structured model for the release PR and changelog\n256     chore(release): version packages","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cdf026fc-8099-43d2-bc6c-e04b74465cdc","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:10:01.934Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"page:    \n40     ci(release): find unfinished releases with callisto release pending\n71     chore(release): version packages\n94     ci(release): run one release at a time\n110     chore(deps): bump taiki-e/install-action from 2.87.28 to 2.87.30 in the routine-actions group\n111     chore(deps): bump the routine-crates group with 2 update