{"parentUuid":"b4a53078-57af-49b3-9da6-df6212485ca5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01WYdepMumhNouAoxEpLdY7W","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk gh release list --limit 2; gh run list --workflow callisto-release.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion --jq '.[0]|\\\"\\\\(.status) \\\\(.conclusion)\\\"'; gh release view callisto@0.19.0 --json body,assets --jq '\\\"assets: \\\\(.assets|length)\\\", .body' | head -50\",\"dangerouslyDisableSandbox\":true}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":21},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7b53b6dc-f40b-42c8-ad6c-9755dd536ac2","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:42:21.251Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"b4a53078-57af-49b3-9da6-df6212485ca5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6e6805a2-5d38-4f7a-be02-83ade9cfd23d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WYdepMumhNouAoxEpLdY7W","type":"tool_result","content":"callisto@0.19.0\tLatest\tcallisto@0.19.0\t2026-11-10T15:21:01Z\ncallisto@0.18.0\t\tcallisto@0.18.0\t2026-11-07T01:18:46Z\ncompleted success\nassets: 5\n_2026-11-10 · [compare](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/compare/callisto@0.18.0...callisto@0.19.0)_\n\n### Minor Changes\n\n- The release PR now links each change to the pull request that introduced it. The link, such as `#123`, sits next to the change, so you can open the discussion and review behind a line without searching for it.\n- Changelogs group each release's changes by bump, so they are easier to scan.\n\n  - Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n  - The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n  - A package with no changes of its own, released only because its fixed or linked group was, gets one line saying so\n\n  **Upgrading**\n  - To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\n- The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.\n\n  **What you see**\n  - Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes collapsed into an expandable block\n  - A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n  - Where merging will publish each package, with a warning up front if the release would fail, so you find out before merging\n  - Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n    - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n\n  **Scripting**\n  - `callisto version --emit-preview <path>` writes the release as JSON\n  - `compose-pr-body --preview <path>` builds the PR body from that file\n    - Relative paths resolve against `--cwd`\n  - `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` adds the publish section; the release PR action already passes it\n\n  **Upgrading**\n  - Nothing to change. Start a changeset paragraph with `Breaking:` or `Action:` to have it listed.\n\n### Patch Changes\n\n- Relative file flags of `release` and `release-pr` now follow `--cwd`.\n\n  - Before, they resolved against the directory you ran from.\n  - If a script passes relative paths together with `--cwd`, make them relative to that directory or absolute.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"15c100ea-9cab-4cdd-a0c6-085afce034c4","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:42:26.487Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"callisto@0.19.0\tLatest\tcallisto@0.19.0\t2026-11-10T15:21:01Z\ncallisto@0.18.0\t\tcallisto@0.18.0\t2026-11-07T01:18:46Z\ncompleted success\nassets: 5\n_2026-11-10 · [compare](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/compare/callisto@0.18.0...callisto@0.19.0)_\n\n### Minor Changes\n\n- The release PR now links each change to the pull request that introduced it. The link, such as `#123`, sits next to the change, so you can open the discussion and review behind a line without searching for it.\n- Changelogs group each release's changes by bump, so they are easier to scan.\n\n  - Major, Minor and Patch Changes headings\n  - The release date, plus a link to compare with the previous version when the GitHub repository is known\n  - A package with no changes of its own, released only because its fixed or linked group was, gets one line saying so\n\n  **Upgrading**\n  - To keep the old single list, set `layout = \"flat\"` under `[changelog]` in `callisto.toml`.\n- The release PR tells you what to expect before you merge.\n\n  **What you see**\n  - Changes grouped under Major, Minor and Patch, each titled by its first line instead of its file name, with long notes collapsed into an expandable block\n  - A \"Read before merging\" block listing `Breaking:` and `Action:` notes, a `Breaking:` note whose bump is too low, and packages that changed but are not in this release\n  - Where merging will publish each package, with a warning up front if the release would fail, so you find out before merging\n  - Labels such as `callisto: ready`, `blocked` and `bump: minor`, so you can triage without opening the PR\n    - Missing labels are created, and labels that stop applying are removed\n\n  **Scripting**\n  - `callisto version --emit-preview <path>` writes the release as JSON\n  - `compose-pr-body --preview <path>` builds the PR body from that file\n    - Relative paths resolve against `--cwd`\n  - `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` adds the publish section; the release PR action already passes it\n\n  **Upgrading**\n  - Nothing to change. Start a changeset paragraph with `Breaking:` or `Action:` to have it listed.\n\n### Patch Changes\n\n- Relative file flags of `release` and `release-pr` now follow `--cwd`.\n\n  - Before, they resolved against the directory you ran from.\n  - If a script passes relative paths together with `--cwd`, make them relative to that directory or absolute.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ea2f36f1-4507-4db5-8427-75264cfc8534","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","branch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility