{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"1cff9838-fa8f-4bb8-99f6-28c713063c63","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:42:26.536Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"3d38bda41afeaa80a7569742499e219aed533aeca653499439fd60bb5adbc429","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"ea7441f4-69cf-4ba5-b46e-e878c8f233d7","keep":714,"tail":["bb329bfbaf8b9aae1104ba5e3fcbb9e1583ab04060c75ab04ee863b268aca30b","6dfa91fdd4b150e45cc2e2aab773c30773dbcb2b885eee140f593fbca5ae0bec","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",716,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"5882e6e367886d6597b15b1d28a72d783ea079822dc17d48a73270824cca67f2"}
{"parentUuid":"1956cb92-84ab-4753-85d3-987956ff2626","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguW73zfLDt1PxXrED4Qt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"0.19.0 is published and verified. The release run succeeded, GitHub marks `callisto@0.19.0` as Latest, and it has 5 assets. The release notes show the new layered entries, with the compare link and date. Nothing in the notes mentions the fixes to unreleased features, so users see only what they can use.\n\nOne thing to check. The notes list #483's PR-link entry in the old two-sentence style, before the changeset rewrite landed on main. It still says what the feature is and why it helps, and the line is accurate, so I'd leave it.\n\n**What this confirms about the process:**\n- One entry per outcome kept the changelog short.\n- The upgrade action is where a user would look for it.\n- The real render matched what I'd tested in a scratch worktree.\n\n**Next, in the order I proposed.** Item 1, checking the release, is now done.\n2. **Private workspace root listed as a package (#179).** It needs one yes or no from you on adding an explicit `ignore = true` for a package.\n3. **Changelog checks in Callisto (#152).** This is the soft lint on changeset summaries and where the rendered changelog is shown before merge. We've effectively answered where, since the release PR shows it, so the lint is the one open call.\n4. **Did-you-mean for mistyped package names.** Small and self-contained.\n5. **Close the stale trails** after a done-when check.\n\nSay go on any of these. Without a decision from you, I'd start item 4, since it needs none.\n\nneeds input: a yes or no on `ignore = true` for #179, and whether you want the soft changeset lint for #152."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":393505,"output_tokens":517,"output_tokens_detai