{"parentUuid":"d3f4c4fc-f374-49b3-ad7a-710862e7bb2c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguWAMk66Y1Pvi3FTH2ti","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My recommendations, in the order I'd do them:\n\n1. **Did-you-mean for mistyped package names: do it now.** It needs no decision from you. A typo in a monorepo today costs a rerun plus a `status` call to find the right name, and the fix is small. It's one PR, off `origin/main`.\n2. **`ignore = true` for a private workspace root (#179): yes.** Every npm monorepo with a private, versioned root sees a fake package in `status`, and `publish-to = [\"none\"]` doesn't hide it.\n   - **Why this option:** it changes nothing for existing users and adds one key.\n   - **Why not the alternatives:** dropping private roots by default would silently remove a deliberately versioned root. Documenting `publish-to = [\"none\"]` leaves the package listed.\n   - **How:** write the spec text first (the package is removed from the graph after discovery), then code and tests in one PR. I'd start it after the did-you-mean PR merges, to keep one PR open at a time.\n3. **Soft changeset lint (#152): no, not now.**\n   - **Why not:** heuristics about length or wording are brittle, and you said prescriptive rules aren't the way to get value. The real fix was the shape in AGENTS.md, the courier plugin update, and showing the rendered changelog in the release PR, which we now do.\n   - **What I'd do:** close #152 with that recorded as the decision. If users' changesets turn out poor, revisit with evidence.\n4. **Close the stale trails: yes, after a done-when check.** About 35 are bookkeeping (merged auto-trails, old release PRs, Dependabot). I'd check the outcome trails with merged work first. Closing is reversible.\n5. **#247 (read the release timings): low priority.** It's a cheap read now that 0.18 and 0.19 are out, but it only matters if you want the faster release.\n6. **ADR 12 (shared tag across a group): leave it.** It needs a design decision, and no user is asking for it yet.\n\nI'd start with 1, and do 3 and 4 as trail housekeeping alongside it, since those are status changes, not PRs.\n\nneeds input: a go on 2 and 3, and on closing the stale trails."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50,"cache_read_input_tokens":395169,"output_tokens":1172,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":444},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1172,"cache_read_input_tokens":395169,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c8f9f705-1aa8-45bd-b9ff-c3c278fe6b45","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CguWAMHpDyCqZJTF8PYG7","requestRef":"ba1c973c-ade6-4724-ad17-05e8d282e975","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d2d62b7-2e47-402a-9652-72282767ebac","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:43:20.966Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
