{"parentUuid":"54a420b7-f61f-44be-ba7b-8a3469061cea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguWJz197yTjLw5xQjgPq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SZt5chCRaKrCTNGENSyZ5i","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"release-please monorepo root package versioning \".\" component root package manifest when to version the root","mode":"standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_read_input_tokens":402102,"output_tokens":289,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":402102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SZt5chCRaKrCTNGENSyZ5i":{"query":"release-please monorepo root package versioning \".\" component root package manifest when to version the root","mode":"standard"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f87d275e-ef9d-4bcf-aaac-3e70dac1faca","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CguWJyfoUkH5h3hrYZVJ3","requestRef":"f2577508-550f-410a-a6ab-bf5a0ffe0d38","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"73345d2d-89e7-4448-ad85-95466014b8b1","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:45:10.647Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"54a420b7-f61f-44be-ba7b-8a3469061cea","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5bd368-c9d8-4a9d-9f73-b1c8a7a184a6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015u7fwKjTCKbtJxoKZWv9YG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Lerna Nx release monorepo workspace root package.json private excluded from versioning and publishing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"versioning and releasing packages in a monorepo\",\"url\":\"https://nx.dev/blog/versioning-and-releasing-packages-in-a-monorepo\"},{\"title\":\"Versioning and Releasing Packages in a Monorepo\",\"url\":\"https://juri.dev/articles/nx-versioning-packages\"},{\"title\":\"DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/nx/versioning-and-releasing-packages-in-a-monorepo-31pk\"},{\"title\":\"# Publishing Packages to npm\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@AgiFlow/aicode-toolkit/blob/63ac95f2cfd63ccb7fffd3690209391508410b73/PUBLISHING.md\"},{\"title\":\"Versioning and Publishing Packages with Nx Release\",\"url\":\"https://gitnation.com/contents/versioning-and-publishing-packages-with-nx-release\"},{\"title\":\"local library development with nx release and verdaccio 019af5c5bec0\",\"url\":\"https://itnext.io/local-library-development-with-nx-release-and-verdaccio-019af5c5bec0\"},{\"title\":\"# Publishing Packages to npm\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@AgiFlow/aicode-toolkit/blob/d050cc7f3fa004d8b36608cbd2be10003354e9ae/docs/PUBLISHING.md\"},{\"title\":\"Updating Version References in Manifest Files (e.g. package.json)\",\"url\":\"https://20.nx.dev/recipes/nx-release/updating-version-references\"},{\"title\":\"updating version references\",\"url\":\"https://nx.dev/docs/guides/nx-release/updating-version-references.md\"},{\"title\":\"Get Started with Nx Release\",\"url\":\"https://nx.dev:443/recipes/nx-release/get-started-with-nx-release\"},{\"title\":\"Get Started with Nx Release\",\"url\":\"https://19.nx.dev/recipes/nx-release/get-started-with-nx-release\"},{\"title\":\"updating version references\",\"url\":\"https://nx.dev/docs/guides/nx-release/updating-version-references\"},{\"title\":\"release publishing\",\"url\":\"https://nx.dev/docs/core-features/release-publishing\"},{\"title\":\"release npm packages\",\"url\":\"https://nx.dev/docs/guides/nx-release/release-npm-packages\"},{\"title\":\"Get Started with Nx Release\",\"url\":\"https://20.nx.dev/recipes/nx-release/get-started-with-nx-release\"},{\"title\":\"Nx Release\",\"url\":\"https://canary.nx.dev/recipes/nx-release\"}]\n\nThe search didn't find a source that says Nx Release automatically skips a private root `package.json`. The closest guidance is about excluding private packages with a project filter, which you can apply to the root project.\n\n- **Excluding a private package:** An Nx blog post shows a `projects` setting that includes all projects with `*` and then removes one with a `!` negation. It notes that you can include all (*) and exclude the private package. (\"projects\": [\"*\", \"!@tuskdesign/demo\"] is the example config.)\n- **Root project in a monorepo:** An ITNext article notes that Nx's Verdaccio setup results in a root project.json, so the root can appear as a project. Excluding it by name with a `!` filter would follow the same pattern as above, though I didn't find a source confirming that exact setup.\n- **Per-project versioning:** Nx Release can version packages independently. One source says each package can have a different version and not all packages need to be released at once, and it requires additional configuration options.\n- **Manifest root:** Nx's docs describe a configurable \"manifest root,\" which is the directory from which the project is versioned. By default this is the project root, so a root `package.json` would be versioned only if the root is treated as a project.\n\nFor a definitive answer on whether the root `package.json` is skipped, check the Nx docs for the `release.projects` option and whether the root project is included by default. Running `nx release --dry-run` will also show which projects it plans to version.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"42faee8e-2c61-42aa-b9a7-6541fb520dc6","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:45:17.215Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Lerna Nx release monorepo workspace root package.json private excluded from versioning and publishing","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LG1UgunAhupZt4j8njfNyh","content":[{"title":"versioning and releasing packages in a monorepo","url":"https://nx.dev/blog/versioning-and-releasing-packages-in-a-monorepo"},{"title":"Versioning and Releasing Packages in a Monorepo","url":"https://juri.dev/articles/nx-versioning-packages"},{"title":"DEV Community","url":"https://dev.to/nx/versioning-and-releasing-packages-in-a-monorepo-31pk"},{"title":"# Publishing Packages to npm","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@AgiFlow/aicode-toolkit/blob/63ac95f2cfd63ccb7fffd3690209391508410b73/PUBLISHING.md"},{"title":"Versioning and Publishing Packages with Nx Release","url":"https://gitnation.com/contents/versioning-and-publishing-packages-with-nx-release"},{"title":"local library development with nx release and verdaccio 019af5c5bec0","url":"https://itnext.io/local-library-development-with-nx-release-and-verdaccio-019af5c5bec0"},{"title":"# Publishing Packages to npm","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@AgiFlow/aicode-toolkit/blob/d050cc7f3fa004d8b36608cbd2be10003354e9ae/docs/PUBLISHING.md"},{"title":"Updating Version References in Manifest Files (e.g. package.json)","url":"https://20.nx.dev/recipes/nx-release/updating-version-references"},{"title":"updating version references","url":"https://nx.dev/docs/guides/nx-release/updating-version-references.md"},{"title":"Get Started with Nx Release","url":"https://nx.dev:443/recipes/nx-release/get-started-with-nx-release"},{"title":"Get Started with Nx Release","url":"https://19.nx.dev/recipes/nx-release/get-started-with-nx-release"},{"title":"updating version references","url":"https://nx.dev/docs/guides/nx-release/updating-version-references"},{"title":"release publishing","url":"https://nx.dev/docs/core-features/release-publishing"},{"title":"release npm packages","url":"https://nx.dev/docs/guides/nx-release/release-npm-packages"},{"title":"Get Started with Nx Release","url":"https://20.nx.dev/recipes/nx-release/get-started-with-nx-release"},{"title":"Nx Release","url":"https://canary.nx.dev/recipes/nx-release"}]},"The search didn't find a source that says Nx Release automatically skips a private root `package.json`. The closest guidance is about excluding private packages with a project filter, which you can apply to the root project.\n\n- **Excluding a private package:** An Nx blog post shows a `projects` setting that includes all projects with `*` and then removes one with a `!` negation. It notes that you can include all (*) and exclude the private package. (\"projects\": [\"*\", \"!@tuskdesign/demo\"] is the example config.)\n- **Root project in a monorepo:** An ITNext article notes that Nx's Verdaccio setup results in a root project.json, so the root can appear as a project. Excluding it by name with a `!` filter would follow the same pattern as above, though I didn't find a source confirming that exact setup.\n- **Per-project versioning:** Nx Release can version packages independently. One source says each package can have a different version and not all packages need to be released at once, and it requires additional configuration options.\n- **Manifest root:** Nx's docs describe a configurable \"manifest root,\" which is the directory from which the project is versioned. By default this is the project root, so a root `package.json` would be versioned only if the root is treated as a project.\n\nFor a definitive answer on whether the root `package.json` is skipped, check the Nx docs for the `release.projects` option and whether the root project is included by default. Running `nx release --dry-run` will also show which projects it plans to version."],"durationSeconds":5.218047999992967,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f87d275e-ef9d-4bcf-aaac-3e70dac1faca","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","branch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"54a420b7-f61f-44be-ba7b-8a3469061cea","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"42faee8e-2c61-42aa-b9a7-6541fb520dc6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebSearch","toolUseID":"toolu_015u7fwKjTCKbtJxoKZWv9YG","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"unreleased-needs-tag\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebSearch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":54},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d3224438-a74a-458f-8d2b-0973cbd7b20b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:45:17.215Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"df3b81a2-b779-4f49-844e-35fe991ea645","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5bd368-c9d8-4a9d-9f73-b1c8a7a184a6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y23Htxgk8Hjaj4KyEVbcn2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Changesets monorepo private packages version workspace root package not included; privatePackages config\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"🦋 Changesets is a game changer\",\"url\":\"https://levelup.gitconnected.com/changesets-is-a-game-changer-fe752af6a8cc\"},{\"title\":\"github-redirect.dependabot.com\",\"url\":\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/changesets/changesets/issues/1325\"},{\"title\":\"Stuck on an issue?\",\"url\":\"https://lightrun.com/answers/changesets-changesets-omit-private-packages-from-lists-of-changed-and-unchanged-packages-offered-by-the-cli-when-running-\"},{\"title\":\"skillselion.com\",\"url\":\"https://skillselion.com/skills/oakoss/agent-skills/changesets\"},{\"title\":\"relizy.pages.dev\",\"url\":\"https://relizy.pages.dev/config/monorepo\"},{\"title\":\"RFC: Packages extensibility\",\"url\":\"https://lightrun.com/answers/changesets-changesets-rfc-packages-extensibility\"},{\"title\":\"github-redirect.dependabot.com\",\"url\":\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/changesets/bot/issues/39\"},{\"title\":\"lerna lerna changelog how to ignore private packages\",\"url\":\"https://lightrun.com/answers/lerna-lerna-changelog-how-to-ignore-private-packages\"},{\"title\":\"Presentations03.04.25 • Changesets\",\"url\":\"https://alteos-gmbh.github.io/tip-of-the-week/presentations/250403-Changesets\"},{\"title\":\"release workflows changesets\",\"url\":\"https://blog.openreplay.com/release-workflows-changesets/\"},{\"title\":\"github-redirect.dependabot.com\",\"url\":\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/changesets/changesets/discussions/1215\"},{\"title\":\"glama.ai\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@Monsoft-Solutions/model-context-protocols/blob/5c53eb4624032d9a7e7bd8b8bc2e15cb6c7ccf0a/.changeset/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"socket.dev\",\"url\":\"https://socket.dev/npm/package/@changesets/types/diff/5.2.0\"},{\"title\":\"🎩 You're Invited:Meet the Socket team at Black Hat in Las Vegas, August 3-6.RSVP\",\"url\":\"https://socket.dev/npm/package/@changesets/config/diff/4.0.0-next.9\"},{\"title\":\"nodejs monorepo en\",\"url\":\"https://www.owenyoung.com/blog/nodejs-monorepo-en\"},{\"title\":\"# @changesets/cli\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/changesets-cli-custom@1.1.0/CHANGELOG.md\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing Changesets for Package Versioning in Polyglot Monorepos\",\"url\":\"https://feedbagel.com/post/implementing-changesets-for-package-versioning-in-polyglot-monorepos\"},{\"title\":\"tomevault.io\",\"url\":\"https://tomevault.io/tome/dashersw/gea/changesets\"}]\n\nThe search turned up useful material on `privatePackages`, but nothing that directly addresses the workspace root package being left out of versioning.\n\n- **Default and common setup:** Running `changeset init` creates a config with `privatePackages` set to version and tag true. These settings allow publishing releases to private GitHub repositories.\n- **Opting out:** You can also now opt private packages out of versioning entirely by setting `privatePackages: false`. A changesets issue notes that with this setting, it will ignore private packages (whether they have a version or not).\n- **Type definition:** The `@changesets/types` package describes `privatePackages` as an opt-in for tracking non-npm or private packages, with optional `version` and `tag` booleans. (Socket.dev diff, index 13-3 to 13-5.)\n- **Defaults in the config reader:** A diff of `@changesets/config` 4.0.0-next.9 shows the defaults changing: the `version` default went from true to false, and an object form defaults `version` and `tag` to false if unset. (Socket.dev diff, index 14-1 onward, and 115–129 of the schema diff.) This could explain behavior changes between versions, but I haven't confirmed it.\n- **Bot limitation:** A changesets/bot issue reports that the bot handles single packages and fully published monorepos well, but struggles when only some packages in a monorepo are published. But it does not work well with the case where one has a monorepo where only some of the packages under the monorepo are actually published to npm.\n\n**Gaps:** None of the results explain how a workspace root package (the one with `private: true` at the repo root) is handled. Searching the Changesets docs or GitHub issues for \"root package\" with `privatePackages` and `ignore` would be the next step, and checking the installed `@changesets/config` version's defaults would confirm whether the default change is the cause.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"746df9f7-5008-4ace-81c3-9f648fca3eba","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:45:17.331Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Changesets monorepo private packages version workspace root package not included; privatePackages config","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0145TPLbpFW98QbjpuhpNoYv","content":[{"title":"🦋 Changesets is a game changer","url":"https://levelup.gitconnected.com/changesets-is-a-game-changer-fe752af6a8cc"},{"title":"github-redirect.dependabot.com","url":"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/changesets/changesets/issues/1325"},{"title":"Stuck on an issue?","url":"https://lightrun.com/answers/changesets-changesets-omit-private-packages-from-lists-of-changed-and-unchanged-packages-offered-by-the-cli-when-running-"},{"title":"skillselion.com","url":"https://skillselion.com/skills/oakoss/agent-skills/changesets"},{"title":"relizy.pages.dev","url":"https://relizy.pages.dev/config/monorepo"},{"title":"RFC: Packages extensibility","url":"https://lightrun.com/answers/changesets-changesets-rfc-packages-extensibility"},{"title":"github-redirect.dependabot.com","url":"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/changesets/bot/issues/39"},{"title":"lerna lerna changelog how to ignore private packages","url":"https://lightrun.com/answers/lerna-lerna-changelog-how-to-ignore-private-packages"},{"title":"Presentations03.04.25 • Changesets","url":"https://alteos-gmbh.github.io/tip-of-the-week/presentations/250403-Changesets"},{"title":"release workflows changesets","url":"https://blog.openreplay.com/release-workflows-changesets/"},{"title":"github-redirect.dependabot.com","url":"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/changesets/changesets/discussions/1215"},{"title":"glama.ai","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@Monsoft-Solutions/model-context-protocols/blob/5c53eb4624032d9a7e7bd8b8bc2e15cb6c7ccf0a/.changeset/README.md"},{"title":"socket.dev","url":"https://socket.dev/npm/package/@changesets/types/diff/5.2.0"},{"title":"🎩 You're Invited:Meet the Socket team at Black Hat in Las Vegas, August 3-6.RSVP","url":"https://socket.dev/npm/package/@changesets/config/diff/4.0.0-next.9"},{"title":"nodejs monorepo en","url":"https://www.owenyoung.com/blog/nodejs-monorepo-en"},{"title":"# @changesets/cli","url":"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/changesets-cli-custom@1.1.0/CHANGELOG.md"},{"title":"Implementing Changesets for Package Versioning in Polyglot Monorepos","url":"https://feedbagel.com/post/implementing-changesets-for-package-versioning-in-polyglot-monorepos"},{"title":"tomevault.io","url":"https://tomevault.io/tome/dashersw/gea/changesets"}]},"The search turned up useful material on `privatePackages`, but nothing that directly addresses the workspace root package being left out of versioning.\n\n- **Default and common setup:** Running `changeset init` creates a config with `privatePackages` set to version and tag true. These settings allow publishing releases to private GitHub repositories.\n- **Opting out:** You can also now opt private packages out of versioning entirely by setting `privatePackages: false`. A changesets issue notes that with this setting, it will ignore private packages (whether they have a version or not).\n- **Type definition:** The `@changesets/types` package describes `privatePackages` as an opt-in for tracking non-npm or private packages, with optional `version` and `tag` booleans. (Socket.dev diff, index 13-3 to 13-5.)\n- **Defaults in the config reader:** A diff of `@changesets/config` 4.0.0-next.9 shows the defaults changing: the `version` default went from true to false, and an object form defaults `version` and `tag` to false if unset. (Socket.dev diff, index 14-1 onward, and 115–129 of the schema diff.) This could explain behavior changes between versions, but I haven't confirmed it.\n- **Bot limitation:** A changesets/bot issue reports that the bot handles single packages and fully published monorepos well, but struggles when only some packages in a monorepo are published. But it does not work well with the case where one has a monorepo where only some of the packages under the monorepo are actually published to npm.\n\n**Gaps:** None of the results explain how a workspace root package (the one with `private: true` at the repo root) is handled. Searching the Changesets docs or GitHub issues for \"root package\" with `privatePackages` and `ignore` would be the next step, and checking the installed `@changesets/config` version's defaults would confirm whether the default change is the cause."],"durationSeconds":5.348773957997561,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f87d275e-ef9d-4bcf-aaac-3e70dac1faca","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","branch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","r