{"parentUuid":"8cd6be0d-ffb4-4e4b-b75b-2473d8efb1d9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguWNSomuRMoReQaKZ9FV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. Today the release PR doesn't say it, and a reader has to infer it from what's missing. In 0.19.0, `callisto-fixtures` appears in the summary table next to the four crates that publish, and nothing says it goes nowhere.\n\n**What I'd show**\n- **Release PR, publish section.** After \"Merging will publish\", one line: \"Versioned, not published: `callisto-fixtures` (no publish target).\" The reader then knows the omission is deliberate.\n- **Summary table.** Optionally mark those rows as \"not published\" so the table and the publish section agree. I'd start with the publish-section line and add the marker only if it still reads ambiguously.\n- **GitHub release and changelog.** No change. They describe what users get, and a private package has no users.\n\n**How it works.** The data already exists. `publish_outlook_in` picks the bumped packages that have a publish target, so the bumped packages it leaves out are exactly the versioned-only ones. The change:\n- Carry that list in the preview as an optional field, so old preview files still load and the schema version stays the same.\n- Render it in the PR body.\n- Test it with the private-member case from #480.\n\n**Where it sits.** It's one small PR, in the same area as the 0.19 work. My order: did-you-mean first (no decision needed), then this one and the root rule. Since you want to limit open PRs, one at a time.\n\nWhen I write the changeset I'll route it through the courier agent once the plugin update lands. If it isn't ready I'll draft it in the agreed layered shape and have a fresh reader check it.\n\nneeds input: a go on this change and on the root rule, and a go on closing the stale trails."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":410546,"output_tokens":1208,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":670},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":654,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1208,"cache_read_input_tokens":410546,"cache_creation_input_tokens":654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":654},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f3b05005-9003-4e48-b521-42698f823d2b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CguWNSVRVRfmNzEoZQqPc","requestRef":"43c6118c-f096-4136-b768-0f111730202d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e5393f75-5061-4bb5-9dcd-623d7cdb5c45","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:46:06.241Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
