{"parentUuid":"d397556b-e61b-4621-8ff2-0a0d4c419f93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguWPMDD9sPiFHjogkasL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the plan: three small PRs in sequence, plus trail housekeeping, all run the way we agreed.\n\n**How each piece gets done**\n\n| # | Work | Approach | Done when |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | Did-you-mean for a mistyped package name | Where E102 is raised, rank the workspace's package names by edit distance and add \"did you mean `cargo/lib`?\" to the help line. No new config. | A typo such as `cargo/libb` suggests `cargo/lib`, and a name far from any package suggests nothing. Tested for both. |\n| 2 | Private workspace root skipped unless named | Spec first: extend WS-DISC-08 so a private root that declares `workspaces` isn't discovered, whether versioned or not, unless a `[[package]]` block names it. Then the code, plus the one-line `status` note. | The spec, a failing test, then the fix. A private versioned root disappears from `status` with the note, and naming it brings it back. |\n| 3 | Show versioned-but-not-published packages | Carry the \"bumped, no publish target\" list as an optional field in the preview, and render a \"Versioned, not published\" line under the publish section. | The #480 private-member case shows `callisto-fixtures` on that line, and old preview files still load. |\n| 4 | Close stale trails | Check each outcome trail's done-when against merged PRs, then close the bookkeeping ones: old auto-trails, release PRs, Dependabot. | The list of what was closed and why, and the few left open are the real work. |\n\n**How every PR is run**\n- **One PR open at a time.** Each starts in a new worktree off `origin/main`, and I check overlap with open PRs before pushing.\n- **Test first, then a mutation check.** Remove the fix, confirm the new test fails, then restore it.\n- **Real run before pushing.** I run the built binary in a scratch worktree, so the working tree is never touched.\n- **Checks by exit code.** Pre-push, lint, doc-check, test and the full `just workflow-contracts`.\n- **Changeset written as the user would read it.** What changed, why it helps, what to do. I'll route it through the courier agent once the plugin update lands, then have a fresh reader check it.\n- **Signed commits, and finding resolution.** Each PR gets linked to its trail, and I resolve any review findings with a test.\n\n**Order:** 1, then 2, then 3, with 4 running alongside since it creates no PRs.\n\nI can also write this into the local plan file in `.claude/plans/`, which stays out of git, so it survives a context reset.\n\nneeds input: a go on the order and the four pieces, and a yes to close the stale trails after the check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180,"cache_read_input_tokens":412408,"output_tokens":1082,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":189},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":180,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1082,"cache_read_input_tokens":412408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":180},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"08d68273-1c76-431b-8d71-d8beb2c299e8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CguWPLsd5cjMVsVQ5i7NV","requestRef":"1727c3f8-3888-419d-8ce3-11b7e1a73440","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6600e32e-7fd8-4b10-8e4a-e680e54d5d62","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:46:16.386Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6