{"parentUuid":"780e48b3-b3fb-4786-9506-beae282424f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguWv1Wu2x55aErZiB2qJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DquYsV7beibNF3LVKvXEiE","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"did-you-mean","description":"Did-you-mean for E102","prompt":"Task: when a user names a package that does not exist, the error should suggest the closest real package name. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First run `git switch -c feat/did-you-mean origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). Work only here.\n\nCurrent behavior: `callisto add --package cargo/libb:minor --summary x` in a workspace with `cargo/lib` prints `E102 package \\`cargo/libb\\` was not found in the workspace` with help \"Check the package's name and ecosystem, or that its directory has a manifest callisto discovers.\" It does not say what the user probably meant. In a monorepo with dozens of packages a typo costs a rerun plus a `status` call.\n\nCriteria (each must have a test that fails before your change and passes after):\n1. When the missing name is close to one or more real packages (edit distance small relative to length; case-insensitive; also catch a name that matches after dropping the ecosystem prefix, e.g. `lib` vs `cargo/lib` is a different error E317, do not change that), the E102 help line names the closest one to three, as `did you mean \\`cargo/lib\\`?`, using ecosystem-qualified display names.\n2. When nothing is close, the help text is unchanged (no suggestion line, no listing of everything).\n3. Suggestions come only from packages that exist in the discovered workspace.\n4. Every place that raises E102 with the workspace's package list at hand gets the suggestion; find them with grep (error.rs, identity.rs, add.rs and any other). Where the list is not available, do not restructure code to get it: report those sites instead.\n5. docs/errors.md describes the new help text for E102 if it documents the help line.\n\nConstraints: prefer an edit-distance helper already in the dependency tree; add no new crate unless one is already a workspace dependency. Keep it small and simple; no config, no new flags. Match the surrounding code's comment density and naming; one short comment line only where the why is non-obvious. Do NOT add a changeset file (the maintainer writes it); instead return, in plain words, what a user now sees and why it helps.\n\nVerify: run `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli` and `just lint`, `just doc-check` and judge each by exit code. Do a mutation check: temporarily break the suggestion logic and confirm your new test fails, then restore. Do NOT commit, push, or sign; leave changes uncommitted in your worktree. Final report: files changed, new test names, the exact commands you ran with exit codes, the E102 sites you did and did not cover, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3045,"cache_read_input_tokens":413775,"output_tokens":4620,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":974},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3045,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4620,"cache_read_input_tokens":413775,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3045,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3045},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DquYsV7beibNF3LVKvXEiE":{"subagent_type":"sm