{"parentUuid":"184ad3f1-851b-44b1-acf8-63393c2d8a68","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguWv1Wu2x55aErZiB2qJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xaqjf7Li7y7yasCdtd7JGQ","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"private-root","description":"Skip private workspace root","prompt":"Task: a private npm workspace root should not be discovered as a package unless the user names it. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First run `git switch -c feat/skip-private-root origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). Work only here.\n\nContext: docs/specs/workspace.json WS-DISC-08 already says \"A root package.json that is both `private` and versionless is never discovered as an npm package (it only holds `workspaces`), regardless of admission.\" A root that is private, declares `workspaces`, and has a name AND a version (e.g. `{\"name\":\"monorepo\",\"private\":true,\"version\":\"0.0.0\",\"workspaces\":[\"packages/*\"]}`) is currently listed in `status` as `npm/monorepo 0.0.0`, and `[[package]] match = \"npm/monorepo\"` with `publish-to = [\"none\"]` does not hide it. Code to read: crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs (around line 141 and the tests near 640-730) and locate/root.rs. \"Private\" means never published to any registry, so such a root is a container for scripts and dev tooling, not a release unit, and nothing depends on it by version.\n\nRequired behavior:\n1. SPEC FIRST: edit WS-DISC-08 in docs/specs/workspace.json (keep it valid JSON) so a root package.json that is `private` and declares `workspaces` is not discovered as an npm package whether or not it has a version, unless a `[[package]]` block names it (then it is discovered as today). Write the spec text before the code, and keep the rest of the criterion intact.\n2. Tests first (fail before, pass after): private+workspaces+versioned root is not discovered; the same root named by a `[[package]]` block is discovered; a non-private root with workspaces is unaffected; a private root WITHOUT `workspaces` is unaffected (still discovered if it has a name and version); a private non-root workspace member is unaffected.\n3. `callisto status` (and any command that already prints discovery notes, like the existing note for a Cargo crate with no version) prints one note when it skips such a root: `ignored private workspace root \\`npm/monorepo\\` (name it in [[package]] to version it)`. Reuse the existing note mechanism; do not invent a new one. Add a test that the note appears.\n4. Update docs/config.md or docs/architecture/* only where they describe root discovery and would now be wrong.\n\nConstraints: no new config keys or flags. Smallest complete change. Match surrounding comment density; one short line only for a non-obvious why. Do NOT add a changeset file; instead return, in plain words, what a user now sees, why it helps and what to do if they did want the root versioned.\n\nVerify: `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, each judged by exit code. Mutation check: weaken the new rule and confirm a new test fails, then restore. Do NOT commit, push, or sign; leave changes uncommitted in your worktree. Final report: files changed, new test names, exact commands run with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3045,"cache_read_input_tokens":413775,"output_tokens":4620,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":974},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3045,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_ge