ess a `[[package]]` block names it (then it is discovered as today). Write the spec text before the code, and keep the rest of the criterion intact.\n2. Tests first (fail before, pass after): private+workspaces+versioned root is not discovered; the same root named by a `[[package]]` block is discovered; a non-private root with workspaces is unaffected; a private root WITHOUT `workspaces` is unaffected (still discovered if it has a name and version); a private non-root workspace member is unaffected.\n3. `callisto status` (and any command that already prints discovery notes, like the existing note for a Cargo crate with no version) prints one note when it skips such a root: `ignored private workspace root \\`npm/monorepo\\` (name it in [[package]] to version it)`. Reuse the existing note mechanism; do not invent a new one. Add a test that the note appears.\n4. Update docs/config.md or docs/architecture/* only where they describe root discovery and would now be wrong.\n\nConstraints: no new config keys or flags. Smallest complete change. Match surrounding comment density; one short line only for a non-obvious why. Do NOT add a changeset file; instead return, in plain words, what a user now sees, why it helps and what to do if they did want the root versioned.\n\nVerify: `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, each judged by exit code. Mutation check: weaken the new rule and confirm a new test fails, then restore. Do NOT commit, push, or sign; leave changes uncommitted in your worktree. Final report: files changed, new test names, exact commands run with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4d96d84d-f790-4840-a80d-a35379c7ad95","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CguWv1C4MhwbzfaeMWbVS","requestRef":"79102d97-45da-4a3a-bb00-e1ffc8d275b8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"73fa11f3-186b-4444-93c4-5357214ef5b0","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:53:27.781Z","advisorModel":"c