{"parentUuid":"bfbe76a5-016a-4d2f-8738-98d26e8afb28","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguYdePSzPmcm2oyPbb35","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fyy8J637CcBATtcoEcn9K7","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr490-body","description":"PR body for 490","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr490.diff. Feature: a private npm workspace root (private, lists `workspaces`) is no longer discovered as a package, with or without a version, unless a `[[package]]` block names it; `status` prints one note when it skips such a root. Reason: it only holds scripts and tooling, is never published, nothing depends on it by version; before, a versioned root like `monorepo 0.0.0` showed as a phantom package that `publish-to = [\"none\"]` could not hide. Spec WS-DISC-08 was updated first.\nVerified facts you may state: five new tests drive the real binary (not discovered, named block brings it back, public root unchanged, private root without workspaces unchanged, private member unchanged); a mutation that disables the rule fails the main test; two existing fixtures asserted the root was a package and one init test's scripted answers depended on it, so they were updated (the root is incidental to what they test); the full checks (`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test`, `just workflow-contracts`) exit 0. Known limit to state: the skip note prints on every command that loads the workspace (init prints it more than once), like the existing note for a Cargo crate with no version. Not run: CI.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; keep it under 170 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":493473,"output_tokens":1948,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1948,"cache_read_input_tokens":493473,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Fyy8J637CcBATtcoEcn9K7":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr490-body","description":"PR body for 490","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr490.diff. Feature: a private npm workspace root (private, lists `workspaces`) is no longer discovered as a package, with or without a version, unless a `[[package]]` block names it; `status` prints one note when it skips such a root. Reason: it only holds scripts and tooling, is never published, nothing depends on it by version; before, a versioned root like `monorepo 0.0.0` showed as a phantom package that `publish-to = [\"none\"]` could not hide. Spec WS-DISC-08 was updated first.\nVerified facts you may state: five new tests drive the real binary (not discovered, named block brings it back, public root unchanged, private root without workspaces unchanged, private member unchanged); a mutation that disables the rule fails the main test; two existing fixtures asserted the root was a p