{"parentUuid":"6f2e654b-1a7d-4673-b90f-5777a6a1b1fb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"edb16cc5-01b7-4736-aa02-29059b4901ca","timestamp":"2026-11-10T16:15:54.583Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-adba22f5917d499fe","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"feat/did-you-mean","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"4098891b36d36f30aac8937820a310b8f7cc3078f1621c625d992716c516063f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The three PR-body agents are running. Meanwhile I'm queuing the fresh-reader check on the three new changesets, with only their text, so I can fix vagueness before reviewers see it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VA81UoXiDjhnvGvsvbw9Up","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/cold_set3.md","content":"# callisto-cli 0.20.0 (draft changelog)\n\n### Minor Changes\n\n- A private npm workspace root is no longer treated as a package.\n\n  - A root `package.json` that is `private` and lists `workspaces` is skipped even when it has a version such as `0.0.0`, so it stops appearing in `status` and in release plans. It only holds scripts and tooling, is never published, and nothing depends on it by version.\n  - `status` prints one line when it skips a root, so it never disappears silently.\n  - To version the root anyway, name it in `callisto.toml` with a `[[package]]` block, for example `match = \"npm/monorepo\"`.\n\n### Patch Changes\n\n- The release PR says which packages are versioned but not published.\n\n  - Under \"Merging will publish\", a line such as ``Versioned, not published: `callisto-fixtures` (no publish target).`` names each package that is bumped but has nowhere to publish, such as a private package that moves with its fixed group.\n  - Before, that package sat in the package table next to the ones that publish, with nothing saying it goes nowhere.\n  - For scripts: the `--emit-preview` file lists these packages as `versionedOnly` under `publish`.\n- A mistyped package name now gets a suggestion, so you can fix it from the error alone.\n\n  - `callisto add --package cargo/libb:minor` adds ``did you mean `cargo/lib`?`` to the E102 error, with up to three close matches.\n  - A wrong ecosystem is caught too: `npm/lib` suggests `cargo/lib`.\n  - When nothing is close, the error is unchanged.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KFaYNseSUFtsgigH5imXWU","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"haiku","description":"Cold-read of three changesets","prompt":"You are a developer who uses a release tool called Callisto. Read only the file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/cold_set3.md and nothing else. Answer in under 180 words: (1) For each of the three entries, what is new or changed, in your own words? (2) Why would you care? (3) Do you need to do anything when upgrading, and what? (4) Quote anything vague, confusing or missing, and say what you would want to know. Be blunt."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
