{"parentUuid":"193dcf34-40d9-458c-a6ea-2d8f0dd0fbc5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Write","toolUseID":"toolu_01HoeETt1LcNiMkhypyvAJRy","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-adba22f5917d499fe\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"agent-adba22f5917d499fe\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":90},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4c231c58-98cf-49b3-910d-e3a59d78fa42","timestamp":"2026-11-10T16:16:07.697Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-adba22f5917d499fe","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"feat/did-you-mean","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"4c231c58-98cf-49b3-910d-e3a59d78fa42","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguYfakURhXJjhLKB655k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BQyjuu44nQDY7j8NAQe3WW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr491_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\nA mistyped package name in a selector now gets a `did you mean` hint on the E102 error. `callisto add --package cargo/libb:minor` suggests `cargo/lib`, and a wrong ecosystem is caught too (`npm/lib` suggests `cargo/lib`). Up to three close workspace packages are listed. When nothing is close, the error is unchanged. The edit distance is a small local helper, so there is no new dependency. The one internal E102 site in toposort has no hint, because user input cannot reach it.\n\n## Verify\n\nNew unit and CLI tests cover a typo, a wrong ecosystem and a far miss. A mutation that empties the suggestion fails the positive tests. I ran the built binary on a scratch workspace with the four cases and saw the expected output. `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2092,"cache_read_input_tokens":497950,"output_tokens":1653,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":78},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2092,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1653,"cache_read_input_tokens":497950,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2092},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"c