{"parentUuid":"396bf757-8be6-4e18-9f69-4f7f55fb78fa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgueU82GzqpgCiB56SpaC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**How and when we make changesets.** This is what I'd write into AGENTS.md and follow from now on:\n\n| When | Who | What |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **In the PR that makes the user-visible change** | The author | One changeset, written before asking for review, so the reviewer reads it with the code. The PR template carries a \"Changelog\" line with \"no changeset needed\" as an explicit choice. |\n| **For a feature spanning several PRs** | The PR that completes it | One entry per outcome. Earlier PRs add none, and the last one writes or updates it. |\n| **For a fix to something not yet released** | Nobody | No changeset. It's folded into the feature's entry. |\n| **For internal, test-only or docs-only work** | Nobody | No changeset. |\n\n**How the text gets written**\n1. **Draft with the courier agent** once your plugin update lands, giving it the diff and the shape: a lead line, then bullets and sub-bullets in audience sections (what you see, scripting, upgrading) when there's enough to say. Until then I draft it in that shape myself.\n2. **Fresh-reader check.** An agent with no context reads only the changeset and says what's new, why it matters and what to do. That caught the vague phrases in #490 and #487.\n3. **Read the rendered release PR before merging it.** It's the first place the whole 0.19-style changelog appears together, so it's the last chance to catch redundant or unclear entries.\n\n**What's next on the work**\n- **Waiting on reviews:** #487, #490 and #491 (and #492, which you own).\n- **Plugin update:** yours, in progress. Once it lands I'll try the courier changeset agent on the next change and compare.\n- **Ready for me, no decisions needed:**\n  - Dedupe the repeated \"ignored private root\" and \"no version\" notes.\n  - Check the done-when on the remaining outcome trails (#173, #176 to #178, #233, #237, #245, #246, #198) and close the finished ones.\n  - Read the 0.18 and 0.19 release timings for #247.\n- **Needs your call:**\n  - Whether to rename `short_sha` to camelCase in the preview file.\n  - Closing #152, the changeset-lint trail, with \"no lint, process and plugin instead\" recorded as the decision.\n  - Whether the PR template gets the \"Changelog\" line.\n\nI'd start with the trail done-when check, since it needs no decision and trims the backlog.\n\nneeds input: a yes or no on the three calls above, and which of the ready items to take first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59,"cache_read_input_tokens":535820,"output_tokens":1165,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":330},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1165,"cache_read_input_tokens":535820,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5240647d-bc01-43ee-a9b1-873071d1548c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgueU7fgyZfUJEFujAnwa","requestRef":"a4c6a308-339a-48b6-8d10-f2c8987292ca","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"182a73ce-d398-41b1-b3ee-10ebf42d417a","timestamp":"2026-11-10T17:32:17.140Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a68476f02ef165