ranch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nMeasured problem (debug build, synthetic workspace of 300 cargo crates + 100 npm packages, all tagged on one commit, N crates changed since the tags and not covered by a changeset): `callisto version --emit-preview` runs `git diff` once per changed uncovered package: N=4 -> 7 diffs, N=40 -> 42, N=150 -> 151 diffs and 3.8 s wall. Everything else is flat in package count. The code is `changed_source_files_of_uncovered` in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs (called from `unreleased_changes` in release_preview.rs). It already skips covered packages and does a tree-id pass; the remaining cost is a separate `git diff --name-only <base> -- <package paths> <excludes>` per package (see the loop around the `args` construction in changed.rs).\n\nRequired change: group the packages that need a file list by their base commit (the commit of each package's last tag; packages with no tag are already excluded upstream) and run ONE `git diff --no-renames --relative --name-only -z <base> -- <all those packages' paths> <excludes>` per distinct base, then assign each returned path to the package whose directory contains it (longest matching package path wins, so nested package directories attribute correctly). The result must be identical to today's for every package: same files, same sort order, same exclusion of ignored paths and DEFAULT_IGNORED_PATHS, same handling of packages that share a directory or are nested, same behavior for uncommitted changes. Where today's code has an edge case (a package whose path is the repository root, a path containing spaces or non-UTF-8, a package with no tag using `git ls-files`), keep the behavior and keep per-package handling for the cases that cannot be batched; report which.\n\nAcceptance (each needs a test that fails before and passes after, using the existing `RecordingGit` runner in changed.rs tests to count git calls):\n1. N changed uncovered packages sharing one base commit cause exactly one `git diff` call, not N.\n2. Packages with two distinct base commits cause two diffs.\n3. Output equals the old per-package output: add a differential test that builds several packages (including nested directories and a root-level package) and compares the batched result with a straightforward per-package reference implementation kept only in the test.\n4. Nested package directories attribute a file to the innermost package.\n5. A package with no changed files is absent or empty exactly as before.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies; match surrounding comment density, one short line only for a non-obvious why. Do NOT add a changeset (internal performance change; I will decide). Verify: `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, judged by exit code; do a mutation check (revert to per-package calls and confirm the call-count test fails, then restore). Do NOT commit, push or sign; leave changes uncommitted. Final report: files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/aad7b373863f1de3f.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"68dcac6e-26c4-4d4f-b6aa-36856dcb4b99","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a68476f02ef165c79","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a68476f02ef165c79","branch":"feat/versioned-not-published","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-