{"parentUuid":"94c92f53-3520-4bb5-a7c6-22a82244bae5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgufbe76BoSq9p4GGBiJu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bigger graph is fine. At 1,800 packages (4.5 times larger) the git process count stays at 8 to 23, and wall time grows only about 2.5 times: `status` 1.4 s, `version` 1.6 s, `--emit-preview` 2.6 s, all on a debug build. Cascading a change through a 1,500-deep dependency chain costs nothing noticeable.\n\n**So the picture is:**\n- **Flat in package count:** `status`, `version` and the publish plan.\n- **One hotspot:** the per-changed-package `git diff` in the unreleased-changes check, linear in the number of changed-but-uncovered packages (151 diffs and 3.8 s at 150). The implementer is fixing it.\n\n**How I'll hold it to the bar when it reports**\n1. Review the diff against the five criteria, especially the differential test against a per-package reference.\n2. Rerun this benchmark before and after at 4, 40 and 150 changed packages and require roughly 1 diff for all three.\n3. Run the full checks, then push, link the trail and write the PR with the courier agent.\n\nI'll report when the implementer finishes.\n\nneeds input: none now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":550573,"output_tokens":536,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":153},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":550573,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformatio