nested_package_gets_its_own_files_and_not_its_parents_other_files`\n  - `a_package_without_changes_has_an_empty_listing` (the package stays in the map with an empty list, as before)\n  \n  **Commands and exit codes**\n  - `cargo test -p callisto-graph changed::`: exit 0, 32 passed.\n  - Mutation check: I temporarily forced per-package diffs with `if false &&` on the batching guard. `a_package_without_changes_has_an_empty_listing`, `batched_listing_equals_the_per_package_listing`, `packages_sharing_a_base_commit_are_listed_by_one_diff` and `two_base_commits_cost_two_diffs` all failed. I then restored the guard and the tests pass again.\n  - `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli --no-fail-fast`: exit 101. All callisto-graph tests pass. In callisto-cli, 3 tests fail: `test_full_polyglot_workspace_release_lifecycle`, `pnpm_and_uv_workspace_resolves_natively_after_version` and `pnpm_and_uv_workspace_resolves_natively_after_snapshot`. The sandbox blocked github.com, index.crates.io and registry.npmjs.org, and the polyglot failure is a crates.io publish command failing, so they look network-caused. I did not confirm that on a clean main. The classifier denied my retry with the sandbox disabled, so these 3 need a run on your side.\n  - `just lint`: exit 0.\n  - `just doc-check`: exit 0.\n  - I did not run `just pre-push`, `just ci`, `just bench` or `just test`.\n  \n  **Unsure**\n  - A package directory containing pathspec glob characters could be attributed differently in the batch, because the union pathspec is glob-interpreted for all packages together. Today's per-package pathspec has the same glob interpretation. A path git returns that no directory claims is dropped. I judged this negligible and did not test it.\n  - I did not rerun the 300 crate / 100 npm synthetic workspace, so the 151 to 1 diff reduction is shown only by the new call-count tests.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"Batched the per-package `git diff` in `changed_source_files_since_last_tag`: one diff per distinct tag commit instead of one per package. `just lint` and `just doc-check` pass. `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli` exits 101 because 3 callisto-cli tests need the network (details below); all the new and changed-module tests pass.\n\n**File changed (uncommitted, no changeset):** `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aad7b373863f1de3f/crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs`. `changed_source_files_of_uncovered` calls this function, so it picks up the change with no edit.\n\n**Branch:** `perf/batch-changed-files` already existed at origin/main (87cf95e4e), so I switched to it. My `git switch -c` failed on the upstream-config write because the sandbox denies the shared `.git/config`, so the branch has no upstream. Nothing was committed or pushed.\n\n**Behaviour**\n- Packages with a tag commit and at least one directory are grouped by that commit and listed with one `git diff --no-renames --relative --name-only -z <base> -- <all dirs> <excludes>`. Each returned path goes to every package whose directory contains it, using the existing `SpecIndex` ancestor lookup, then is sorted by `BTreeSet<PathBuf>` as before.\n- Still one process per package for two cases that cannot be batched:\n  - An untagged package, or one whose tag is not a commit, still runs `git ls-files`.\n  - A tagged package with no directories still gets its own diff, because an empty pathspec would match everything.\n- I pulled the shared run, failure message and NUL-split into a `list_files` helper (plus `diff_command`) so the batched and per-package paths use the same code.\n- A root-level package (`.`), a directory with spaces, and uncommitted and staged changes behave as before. Non-UTF-8 paths are unchanged: lossy conversion both before and after.\n\n**Spec conflict, please decide:** your requirement says the result must be identical to today's, but acceptance 4 says a nested file goes to the innermost package only. Today the per-package pathspec of the outer package also covers the inner package's files, so the outer package gets them too. I kept today's behaviour (both packages get the file), because narrowing it could make an outer package look unchanged and drop it from release proposals. The test asserts the inner package gets its own files and the outer one still does too. If you want innermost-only, it is a small change in the attribution loop, but it alters results.\n\n**New tests** (all in `changed.rs`):\n- `packages_sharing_a_base_commit_are_listed_by_one_diff` (5 packages, exactly 1 diff)\n- `two_base_commits_cost_two_diffs`\n- `batched_listing_equals_the_per_package_listing` (differential test against a per-package reference kept in the test; covers a root package, nested `pkg-a/inner`, a directory with a space, an untagged package, ignored paths and an uncommitted staged file, and asserts 1 diff)\n- `a_nested_package_gets_its_own_files_and_not_its_parents_other_files`\n- `a_package_without_changes_has_an_empty_listing` (the package stays in the map with an empty list, as before)\n\n**Commands and exit codes**\n- `cargo test -p callisto-graph changed::`: exit 0, 32 passed.\n- Mutation check: I temporarily forced per-package diffs with `if false &&` on the batching guard. `a_package_without_changes_has_an_empty_listing`, `batched_listing_equals_the_per_package_listing`, `packages_sharing_a_base_commit_are_listed_by_one_diff` and `two_base_commits_cost_two_diffs` all failed. I then restored the guard and the tests pass again.\n- `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli --no-fail-fast`: exit 101. All callisto-graph tests pass. In callisto-cli, 3 tests fail: `test_full_polyglot_workspace_release_lifecycle`, `pnpm_and_uv_workspace_resolves_natively_after_version` and `pnpm_and_uv_workspace_resolves_natively_after_snapshot`. The sandbox blocked github.com, index.crates.io and registry.npmjs.org, and the polyglot failure is a crates.io publish command failing, so they look network-caused. I did not confirm that on a clean main. The classifier denied my retry with the sandbox disabled, so these 3 need a run on your side.\n- `just lint`: exit 0.\n- `just doc-check`: exit 0.\n- I did not run `just pre-push`, `just ci`, `just bench` or `just test`.\n\n**Unsure**\n- A package directory containing pathspec glob characters could be attributed differently in the batch, because the union pathspec is glob-interpreted for all packages together. Today's per-package pathspec has the same glob interpretation. A path git returns that no directory claims is dropped. I judged this negligible and did not test it.\n- I did not rerun the 300 crate / 100 npm synthetic workspace, so the 151 to 1 diff reduction is shown only by the new call-count tests."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":184,"turnIndex":220},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a68476f02ef165c79","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"feat/versioned-not-published","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
