{"parentUuid":"15ac7836-e4ca-492a-8f80-c144efdac9ad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgugmcx31CLpq4nSyV8ra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QSbELGBFkk2KdZoJitBNqX","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr494-body","description":"PR body for 494","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr494.diff. Change: `changed_source_files_since_last_tag` now lists changed files with one `git diff` per distinct last-tag commit instead of one per package, attributing each returned path to every package whose directory contains it (same as before, including nested directories). Packages with no tag or no directory still use one git call each. Pathspecs are split across several diffs past a 24,000-byte budget so a huge workspace stays under command-line limits (Windows is 32 KB).\nMeasured on a synthetic workspace (debug build, `version --emit-preview`, all packages tagged at one commit, N changed and not covered by a changeset): 150 changed packages went from 151 git diffs and 3.8 s to 4 diffs and 1.0 s; 40 changed stayed at 4 diffs (was 42); 1,800 packages with 150 changed took 2.6 s and 20 git processes. status, version --dry-run and the publish plan were already flat in package count (8 to 23 git processes, under 2.6 s at 1,800 packages), so this was the one linear spot. It enforces the AGENTS.md rule of no git process per package.\nVerified: new tests count git calls (5 packages, 1 diff; two base commits, 2 diffs), a differential test compares the batched result with a per-package reference (root package, nested directories, a directory with a space, an untagged package, ignored paths, an uncommitted staged file), a small-budget test shows chunking changes nothing, and mutations (force per-package diffs, ignore the budget) fail those tests; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Behavior note: a nested package's files still also belong to its parent package, as before.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 170 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1160,"cache_read_input_tokens":572874,"output_tokens":1189,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":91},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1160,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1189,"cache_read_input_tokens":572874,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1160},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QSbELGBFkk2KdZoJitBNqX":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr494-body","description":"PR body for 494","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr494.diff. Change: `changed_source_files_since_last_tag` now lists changed files with one `git diff` per distinct last-tag commit instead of one per package, attributing each returned path to every package whose directory contains it (same as before, including nested directories). Packages with no tag or no directory still use one git call each. Pathspecs are split across several diffs past a 24,000-byte budget so a huge workspace stays under command-line limits (Windows is 32 KB).\nMeasured on a synthetic workspace (debug build, `version --emit-preview`, all packages tagged at one commit, N changed and not covered by a changeset): 150 changed packages went from 151 git diffs and 3.8 s to 4 diffs and 1.0 s; 40 changed stayed at 4 diffs (was 42); 1,800 packages with 150 changed took 2.6 s and 20 git processes. status, version --dry-run and the publish plan were already flat in package count (8 to 23 git processes, under 2.6 s at 1,800 packages), so this was the one linear spot. It enforces the AGENTS.md rule of no git process per package.\nVerified: new tests count git calls (5 packages, 1 diff; two base commits, 2 diffs), a differential test compares the batched result with a per-package reference (root package, nested directories, a directory with a space, an untagged package, ignored paths, an uncommitted staged file), a small-budget test shows chunking changes nothing, and mutations (force per-package diffs, ignore the budget) fail those tests; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Behavior note: a nested package's files still also belong to its parent package, as before.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 170 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e918b3dc-0cb6-424a-a403-eb79296a30df","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgugmcaTEk8tZV8eKC85T","requestRef":"513fe3b5-8254-4d85-968e-83e63d5c4bf0","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aad6c4a6-4a36-48fb-bbb5-22c7e9b72860","timestamp":"2026-11-10T18:02:26.293Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-