{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytxL4nYq1T7cJBdRjiu","lastSequenceNum":8710,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"ad5e5ddf-90da-45a4-9aa1-c1ecf130fde4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgugnLni6XtM3e38pfWSc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PR body agent is running. Here's where the performance work stands.\n\n**Measured, not guessed.** I built a synthetic monorepo (up to 1,500 Cargo crates in a dependency chain plus 300 npm packages) and counted git processes and wall time. Before this change:\n- `status`, `version --dry-run` and the publish plan were flat in package count: 8 to 23 git processes and under 2.6 s at 1,800 packages, on a debug build.\n- `version --emit-preview` had one linear hotspot, one `git diff` per changed-but-uncovered package.\n\n**What #494 does.** It runs one diff per release instead of one per package, and I added a pathspec size budget so very large workspaces can't hit a command-line length limit.\n\n| Case | Before | After |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 150 changed packages | 151 diffs, 3.8 s | 4 diffs, 1.0 s |\n| 40 changed packages | 42 diffs | 4 diffs |\n| 1,800 packages, 150 changed | n/a | 20 processes, 2.6 s |\n\n**Quality bar**\n- **Differential test:** it compares the batched result with a per-package reference, covering a root package, nested directories, a directory with a space, an untagged package, ignored paths and an uncommitted staged file.\n- **Budget test:** shrinking the budget to one byte splits the listing into six diffs with identical results.\n- **Mutations:** removing the batching or the budget each fails its tests.\n- **Checks:** all five run outside the sandbox and pass. The implementer's three \"network\" failures were the sandbox, as before.\n\n**Decision I made for you.** The nested-package spec conflict in my own brief: the implementer kept today's behavior, where an outer package also owns an inner package's files. I agreed, because narrowing it could drop an outer package from release proposals.\n\n**Open as PR #494**, linked to trail 250, with a patch changeset saying what a large-monorepo user gets. CI has not run.\n\nneeds input: none now. I'll apply the PR body when the narrator returns."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_read_input_tokens":574034,"output_tokens":687,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1417,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":687,"cache_read_input_tokens":574034,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1417},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"79ae2077-7d53-4c79-a899-66cc5f227644","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgugnLFyDe3ycQYTUJXXU","requestRef":"eccbd3c0-21ef-436e-9bb7-d8e5d8bf0ccc","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f90b6e8a-e8c0-4f71-8088-6a9af5634c43","timestamp":"2026-11-10T18:02:32.967Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aad7b373863f1de3f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/batch-changed-files-pr","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
