{"parentUuid":"1ef80c7d-51cb-401f-89c9-64bf10fff0c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgugnx7ySg9tnYaCntUN4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FYV6BSX8vzCuU1JZ52vh9v","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr494_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\n`changed_source_files_since_last_tag` ran one `git diff` per package. That made `version --emit-preview` scale linearly with package count, against the AGENTS.md rule of no git process per package. It now runs one diff per distinct last-tag commit and attributes each path to every package whose directory contains it, nested directories included. Untagged or directory-less packages still use one call each. Pathspecs split across several diffs past 24,000 bytes to stay under the Windows 32 KB command-line limit.\n\nWith 150 changed packages tagged at one commit, a synthetic workspace went from 151 diffs and 3.8 s to 4 diffs and 1.0 s.\n\n## Verify\n\nNew tests count git calls and compare the batched result with a per-package reference (root package, nested and spaced directories, untagged package, ignored paths, staged file). A small-budget test shows chunking changes nothing. Forcing per-package diffs or ignoring the budget fails these tests. `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI not run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1347,"cache_read_input_tokens":575451,"output_tokens":671,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1347,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":575451,"cach