{"parentUuid":"bdfd9f17-d2a3-43de-b1bb-1325f4447d60","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguiARLYFicnDw5qJEdoj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0135VQciCYuABBisM82zG7YU","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"note-once","description":"Print discovery notes once","prompt":"Task: discovery notes print more than once per run; print each once. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First run `git switch -c fix/note-once origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nProblem: two `eprintln!(\"note: ...\")` sites run once per workspace load, and some commands load the workspace several times (`callisto init` prints the private-workspace-root note three times): (1) crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs, in `discover`, `note: ignored private workspace root ...`; (2) crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs around line 156, `note: skipping ... it declares no version ...`. Find any other `eprintln!(\"note:` discovery notes and handle them the same way.\n\nRequired: add one small helper in the graph crate, for example `fn note_once(message: String)`, that prints the note to stderr the first time that exact message is seen in the process and never again, using a process-wide `OnceLock<Mutex<BTreeSet<String>>>` (or equivalent std-only structure). It must return or expose whether it printed so it can be unit tested. Route the notes through it. No new dependency, no new flags, no behavior change except the repeat.\n\nAcceptance (tests fail before, pass after):\n1. Unit test on the helper: the same message twice reports printed then not printed; a different message prints.\n2. A CLI test driving the real built binary (see crates/callisto-cli/tests/private_workspace_root_tests.rs for the pattern): `callisto init --yes` in a workspace with a private versioned npm root prints the ignored-root note exactly once on stderr.\n3. Existing tests that assert a note appears (private_workspace_root_tests.rs, any for the no-version Cargo crate) still pass.\nConstraints: smallest complete change; one short comment line only where the why is non-obvious. Do NOT add a changeset (I will decide). Verify: `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, each judged by exit code; mutation check (make the helper always print and confirm the new tests fail, then restore). Do NOT commit, push or sign; leave changes uncommitted. Final report: files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1407,"cache_read_input_tokens":578479,"output_tokens":1240,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":249},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1407,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1240,"cache_read_input_tokens":578479,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1407},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0135VQciCYuABBisM82zG7YU":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"note-once","description":"Print discovery notes once","prompt":"Task: discovery notes print more than once per run; print each once. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First run `git switch -c fix/note-once origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nProblem: two `eprintln!(\"note: ...\")` sites run once per workspace load, and some commands load the workspace several times (`callisto init` prints the private-workspace-root note three times): (1) crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs, in `discover`, `note: ignored private workspace root ...`; (2) crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs around line 156, `note: skipping ... it declares no version ...`. Find any other `eprintln!(\"note:` discovery notes and handle them the same way.\n\nRequired: add one small helper in the graph crate, for example `fn note_once(message: String)`, that prints the note to stderr the first time that exact message is seen in the process and never again, using a process-wide `OnceLock<Mutex<BTreeSet<String>>>` (or equivalent std-only structure). It must return or expose whether it printed so it can be unit tested. Route the notes through it. No new dependency, no new flags, no behavior change except the repeat.\n\nAcceptance (tests fail before, pass after):\n1. Unit test on the helper: the same message twice reports printed then not printed; a different message prints.\n2. A CLI test driving the real built binary (see crates/callisto-cli/tests/private_workspace_root_tests.rs for the pattern): `callisto init --yes` in a workspace with a private versioned npm root prints the ignored-root note exactly once on stderr.\n3. Existing tests that assert a note appears (private_workspace_root_tests.rs, any for the no-version Cargo crate) still pass.\nConstraints: smallest complete change; one short comment line only where the why is non-obvious. Do NOT add a changeset (I will decide). Verify: `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, each judged by exit code; mutation check (make the helper always print and confirm the new tests fail, then restore). Do