fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-process","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/note-once","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"7519959c-19a4-44fc-888c-5600d03c8f5c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"742a1b36-e83f-484b-a2b0-adb3fe2a079e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LB3NhxCTDzW8anvYNriH91","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-process/AGENTS.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"91161958-eda5-493a-bff1-7acac6f52400","timestamp":"2026-11-10T18:21:32.242Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-process/AGENTS.md","oldString":"One changeset per user-visible topic. Lead with what the user sees now and say why it matters to them; add an action or limit when it matters. A fix to something not yet released has no changeset. Use a short sentence for a simple change, or a short lead and bullets for related details. No internal names, mechanism or filler.","newString":"One changeset per user-visible outcome, written in the PR that makes it visible; a feature spanning several PRs gets its entry from the last one, and earlier PRs add none. Lead with what the user sees now and say why it matters to them; add an action or limit when it matters. Use a short sentence for a simple change, or a short lead with bullets and sub-bullets, in sections for upgrading, scripting or setup when there is enough to say. A fix to something not yet released, an internal change, and test-only or docs-only work have no changeset. Before review, have a reader with no context see only the changeset and say what changed, why it matters and what to do; read the rendered release PR before merging it. No internal names, mechanism or filler.","originalFile":"# Agent guide\n\nRules for AI agents working in this repo.\n\n## Crates\n\n| Crate | License | Depends on |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| callisto-model | MIT | none (external: `michi-graph`, MIT) |\n| callisto-manifests | FSL-1.1-MIT | model |\n| callisto-graph | FSL-1.1-MIT | model, manifests |\n| callisto-cli | FSL-1.1-MIT | model, manifests, graph |\n| callisto-fixtures | FSL-1.1-MIT | model (dev-only) |\n\n- `callisto-model` (MIT) must never depend on an FSL crate. It depends on `michi-graph` (MIT, no dependencies of its own) for dependency-graph validation and ordering. `just license-boundary` fails if anything it builds with is FSL.\n- Check with `grep -H \"^license\" crates/*/Cargo.toml` after adding or moving a crate.\n\n## Commands\n\n- Full pipeline: `just ci` (includes the 90% coverage gate). `just test`, `just lint`, `just fmt`.\n- Before every push or PR: `just pre-push && just lint && just doc-check && just test`, and `just ci` before marking a PR ready. Judge each by its exit code. Never tail or grep the output for success (a compile error prints no \"failed\" line), and never report a check as passed that was not run.\n- Commits must be signed: the ruleset requires it. Never pass `-c commit.gpgsign=false`. After pushing, `gh api repos/orin-dx/callisto/commits/<sha> --jq .commit.verification.reason` must say `valid`.\n- Performance: `just bench` times `status`, `version --dry-run` and `release --dry-run` over generated workspaces and counts the git processes each starts (`CALLISTO_BENCH_SHAPES=1` lists which). A change that adds a git process per package fails review.\n- Scoped iteration: one `cargo test -p <crate>` or `cargo clippy -p <crate> --all-targets -- -D warnings` at a time.\n  - Not `moon run <project>:test`: its per-project fan-out serializes on `target/`'s build lock.\n  - Never run cargo builds in parallel.\n- Changesets: `callisto add --package cargo/callisto-cli:<bump> --summary \"...\"` (non-interactive). Target `callisto-cli`: its changelog is the one users read. One changeset per user-visible topic. Lead with what the user sees now and say why it matters to them; add an action or limit when it matters. A fix to something not yet released has no changeset. Use a short sentence for a simple change, or a short lead and bullets for related details. No internal names, mechanism or filler.\n- Never `git checkout -- Cargo.lock` as cleanup. A lockfile diff means investigate, not discard.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. Safe Rust only: `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`.\n2. Manifest edits preserve format: `toml_edit` for TOML; JSON changes that only replace string values are written into the original text by span (`json_text`), anything else keeps key order and fingerprinted indentation. No regex or line edits.\n3. File writes go through `callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write`.\n4. User-facing errors derive `miette::Diagnostic` with a code and a fix.\n5. No emojis in docs or code.\n6. No cargo features in shipped crates; behaviour is chosen at runtime (#143). The dev-only `callisto-model/test-util` feature is the exception.\n7. No `unwrap()` outside tests (`just lint` denies it). An `expect` names the invariant that makes it unreachable.\n\n## Fixing bugs\n\n- Grep for structurally identical code (same algorithm, other file, ecosystem or mode). A sibling with the same defect is in scope now.\n- N copies of one logic: unify to one implementation rather than patching each.\n- A deliberately deferred sibling gets an explicit record: changeset note, tracked follow-up or code comment.\n- A new shared helper migrates every call site in the same change, or the rest are tracked.\n\n## Specs and plans\n\n- Specs (`spec@1`) live in `docs/specs/`, one per area, current behavior only. Change the spec in the same PR as the behavior. No history, rationale or revision notes.\n- This repo's release workflow has no GitHub Environment or reviewer gate and only `execute` gets registry secrets (owner policy, enforced by `.github/tests/verify-release-workflow-policy.sh`). Never add one.\n- Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` and the matching `docs/architecture/` topic before changing behavior in an area.\n- Read `docs/adr/README.md` before changing release flow, Git access, publishing, distribution, platform packages or manifest writes. Reversing an ADR needs a new ADR the owner accepts.\n- Plans (`plan@1`) live in `docs/projects/`. Delete a plan once its work ships.\n- Code never cites specs: no spec IDs, criterion IDs, section numbers or track names in comments, test names or messages. Describe the behavior instead.\n- A requirement the owner didn't state is a judgment call. Get owner confirmation before it gates anything.\n\n## Writing\n\n- Succinct: short sentences, bullets, tables. No backstory, hedging or filler.\n- Never hard-wrap Markdown or PR bodies: one line per paragraph.\n- Code comments: one short line, only for a non-obvious why. Wrap at 120 columns (`rustfmt.toml`). No history (\"used to\", \"previously\"): git records it.\n- No claude.ai session links in commits, PRs or files.\n\n<!-- entire-agent:begin -->\nRead .entire/agent-guide.md for this repository's workflow, source inspection, and verification guidance.\n@.entire/agent-guide.md\n<!-- entire-agent:end -->\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":24,"oldLines":7,"newStart":24,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Scoped iteration: one `cargo test -p <crate>` or `cargo clippy -p <crate> --all-targets -- -D warnings` at a time.","   - Not `moon run <project>:test`: its per-project fan-out serializes on `target/`'s build lock.","   - Never run cargo builds in parallel.","-- Changesets: `callisto add --package cargo/callisto-cli:<bump> --summary \"...\"` (non-interactive). Target `callisto-cli`: its changelog is the one users read. One changeset per user-visible topic. Lead with what the user sees now and say why it matters to them; add an action or limit when it matters. A fix to something not yet released has no changeset. Use a short sentence for a simple change, or a short lead and bullets for related details. No internal names, mechanism or filler.","+- Changesets: `callisto add --package cargo/callisto-cli:<bump> --summary \"...\"` (non-interactive). Target `callisto-cli`: its changelog is the one users read. One changeset per user-visible outcome, written in the PR that makes it visible; a feature spanning several PRs gets its entry from the last one, and earlier PRs add none. Lead with what the user sees now and say why it matters to them; add an action or limit when it matters. Use a short sentence for a simple change, or a short lead with bullets and sub-bullets, in sections for upgrading, scripting or setup when there is enough to say. A fix to something not yet released, an internal change, and test-only or docs-only work have no changeset. Before review, have a reader with no context see only the changeset and say what changed, why it matters and what to do; read the rendered release PR before merging it. No internal names, mechanism or filler."," - Never `git checkout -- Cargo.lock` as cleanup. A lockfile diff means investigate, not discard."," "," ## Invariants"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7519959c-19a4-44fc-888c-5600d03c8f5c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/changeset-process","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/note-once","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
