{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"07a7170e03350f4c9664e0e67f3d03a71fd586d7d443fc4bab2cfcc840f5c770","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YWDfTFsHyj8cyXBXbUPZ2G","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr495_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\nThe 0.19.0 release had 13 changelog entries, many describing fixes to unreleased features or mechanism rather than user outcomes; they were rewritten into 3 layered entries. AGENTS.md and the PR template now say when to write a changeset: one per user-visible outcome, in the PR that makes it visible, with a feature spanning several PRs getting its entry from the last one. Fixes to unreleased features, internal changes, and test-only or docs-only work have none.\n\n## Verify\n\n`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cdmqi3mMd9D2u1fTDiGfw7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 495 --title \"docs: clarify changeset authoring scope and timing\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr495_final.md","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
