{"parentUuid":"8aee0bee-0de6-4d23-be4d-64f2b3fcb6ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguiyZDNEP9CLYdJZBtzs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019wBfZkKbbiM4weJ9JqUGzf","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"haiku","name":"pr496-body","description":"PR body for 496","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr496.diff. Change: the discovery notes (`note: ignored private workspace root ...` and `note: skipping ... declares no version ...`) print at most once per process through a small `note_once` helper (a process-wide set of seen messages), because commands that load the workspace several times, such as `callisto init`, printed the same note up to three times. Left alone on purpose: the release-preview note TAGS_UNBOUND_NOTE, which is a different kind of note in the cli crate.\nVerified: a unit test on the helper; a CLI test runs the built binary with `callisto init --yes` and asserts the ignored-root note appears exactly once; a mutation making the helper always print fails both tests (the init test then shows 3 copies); `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Limit: the guard is process-wide, so in-process tests that load the same fixture twice see a note once.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 120 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":249,"cache_read_input_tokens":618