{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"ad29eafcf9d611606c0f7a0f0d0fecc8115daab30507c8e11940ddc58dc1fa4f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The narrator's body is accurate but vague on checks, and it omits the CI caveat. I'm tightening it with the exact commands and the known limit."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UvVfrC3xY74p2vM9kHzj1k","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr496_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\nDiscovery notes about skipped packages, an ignored private workspace root and a crate with no version, now print at most once per run. Before, `callisto init` and other commands that load the workspace more than once printed the same note up to three times.\n\nThe guard is process-wide, so in-process tests that load the same fixture twice see a note once. The release-preview note `TAGS_UNBOUND_NOTE` is a different kind of note and is unchanged.\n\n## Verify\n\nA unit test covers the helper, and a CLI test runs the built binary with `callisto init --yes` and asserts the ignored-root note appears exactly once. Making the helper always print fails both tests, and the init test then shows three copies.\n\n`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015WsBLS6MfkLjtMP5JB75WY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 496 --title \"fix(graph): print each discovery note once per run\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr496_final.md","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
