{"parentUuid":"b3dfd050-77a4-4ae9-8dce-a65ffff3b919","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01UcYDCV8qaz5TVdLbyGuRtw","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"cat docs/stability.md | head -60; rtk grep -rn -i \\\"1\\\\.0\\\\|v1\\\" docs/how-callisto-works.md README.md 2>/dev/null | head -8\",\"dangerouslyDisableSandbox\":true}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":19},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cb45810f-114b-44bb-b634-dc0b4aa22dc3","timestamp":"2026-11-10T18:51:49.031Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae5865da7dc4349e3","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/note-once","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"b3dfd050-77a4-4ae9-8dce-a65ffff3b919","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c1b14e46-db41-43a6-8854-46862dcdca27","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UcYDCV8qaz5TVdLbyGuRtw","type":"tool_result","content":"# Stability\n\nWhat Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. A breaking change to anything in the first table needs a major version.\n\n## Stable\n\n| Surface | The promise |\n| --- | --- |\n| The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error. |\n| `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. |\n| `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |\n| Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli` for npm names; other ecosystems use `ecosystem/name` keys. |\n| Error codes | A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused. New codes may appear. |\n| Tag names | `{name}@{version}` by default, `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name. Pin a name with `tag-template` if a stable tag matters to your tooling. |\n| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version. |\n\n## CI plumbing\n\nThe generated workflows use `release plan`, `release inspect`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work only with the same Callisto version that generated them: the intent, decision, receipt and run envelope carry versions, and a reader rejects any other. Keep the action and the binary on one version, and regenerate with `callisto init` after an upgrade.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Text output, stderr, warnings and the wording of error messages.\n- The library crates (`callisto-model`, `-manifests`, `-graph`). They are internal and version in lockstep with the CLI.\n- The order of keys in JSON output, and timing or performance.\n- Platforms without a published binary. Windows is not supported.\ndocs/how-callisto-works.md:63:Callisto is pre-v1. These rows describe current behavior rather than planned adapters.\nREADME.md:66:Callisto is pre-v1. The [guide](docs/how-callisto-works.md) covers current support, known limits, and when another tool may be a better fit, and [stability](docs/stability.md) says what will and will not change.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"15c6b7b6-2c57-4f54-aa5e-1b18bc96257a","timestamp":"2026-11-10T18:51:51.358Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Stability\n\nWhat Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. A breaking change to anything in the first table needs a major version.\n\n## Stable\n\n| Surface | The promise |\n| --- | --- |\n| The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |\n| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error. |\n| `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. |\n| `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |\n| Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli` for npm names; other ecosystems use `ecosystem/name` keys. |\n| Error codes | A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused. New codes may appear. |\n| Tag names | `{name}@{version}` by default, `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name. Pin a name with `tag-template` if a stable tag matters to your tooling. |\n| The GitHub Actions | The inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto`. The floating `v1` tag moves only on stable releases; pin a commit for a fixed version. |\n\n## CI plumbing\n\nThe generated workflows use `release plan`, `release inspect`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release build-python`, `release-pr`, `matrix`, `compose-pr-body` and `schema`. They are hidden from `--help` and work only with the same Callisto version that generated them: the intent, decision, receipt and run envelope carry versions, and a reader rejects any other. Keep the action and the binary on one version, and regenerate with `callisto init` after an upgrade.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Text output, stderr, warnings and the wording of error messages.\n- The library crates (`callisto-model`, `-manifests`, `-graph`). They are internal and version in lockstep with the CLI.\n- The order of keys in JSON output, and timing or performance.\n- Platforms without a published binary. Windows is not supported.\ndocs/how-callisto-works.md:63:Callisto is pre-v1. These rows describe current behavior rather than planned adapters.\nREADME.md:66:Callisto is pre-v1. The [guide](docs/how-callisto-works.md) covers current support, known limits, and when another tool may be a better fit, and [stability](docs/stability.md) says what will and will not change.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"bd189401-7e99-497c-862e-8fd5bc14a037","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae5865da7dc4349e3","root":"