{"parentUuid":"7b2916db-0e10-468e-bf4c-08386c481339","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgukYoinXwagM1T1zEpDE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KA7TVgKiaE9Q3LjPiFJY9K","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"error-envelope","description":"Consistent JSON error envelope","prompt":"Task: make every failing command's `--format json` error output use the same envelope its success report uses (trail #177; part of the 1.0 stability promise in docs/stability.md: \"--format json reports carry schemaVersion\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/error-envelope origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nContext: docs/specs/release.json REL-CMD-12 and REL-PR-07 already say a failing release command's JSON error carries its own `command` (the subcommand path, e.g. `release plan`, `release-pr verify`) and the `dryRun` flag. The trail says the code may not do this: `release plan` reportedly reports `\"command\": \"release\"`, and the release-pr subcommands report `\"command\": \"release-pr\"` with no `dryRun` (see crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs near the error path and cli.rs near the command-name function). FIRST build the binary and reproduce, with real runs, what each of these prints on failure with `--format json` (run outside a workspace or with a bad argument to force an error): `release plan`, `release execute`, `release artifact-manifest`, `release inspect`, `release build-python`, `release pending`, each `release-pr` subcommand (verify, decide, commit-plan), `matrix`, `compose-pr-body`, and plain `version`/`status`/`add`. Record the actual envelope keys for each in your report.\n\nThen fix every command whose error envelope differs from its success envelope in `command`, `dryRun` or `schemaVersion`, so a failing `release plan` reports `command: \"release plan\"` and so on (match exactly how REL-CMD-12 and REL-PR-07 word it; if the specs and code disagree about the exact string, follow the specs and tell me). If everything already conforms, say so with the evidence and add only the missing tests.\n\nAcceptance (tests fail before, pass after, or exist because they were missing): one test per command family (release, release-pr, matrix/compose-pr-body, core commands) asserting the error envelope has `schemaVersion`, the right `command`, and `dryRun`, by running the real binary. Update the specs only if a criterion is wrong or missing; keep JSON valid.\n\nThis changes user-visible JSON on failure, so do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words: what a script that parses errors sees now versus before, and whether any value changed that an existing script could depend on (that decides whether it needs an upgrade note). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on your main test. Final report: findings per command, files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_read_input_tokens":623288,"output_tokens":4395,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":969},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1555,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4395,"cache_read_input_tokens":623288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1