ling `release plan` reports `command: \"release plan\"` and so on (match exactly how REL-CMD-12 and REL-PR-07 word it; if the specs and code disagree about the exact string, follow the specs and tell me). If everything already conforms, say so with the evidence and add only the missing tests.\n\nAcceptance (tests fail before, pass after, or exist because they were missing): one test per command family (release, release-pr, matrix/compose-pr-body, core commands) asserting the error envelope has `schemaVersion`, the right `command`, and `dryRun`, by running the real binary. Update the specs only if a criterion is wrong or missing; keep JSON valid.\n\nThis changes user-visible JSON on failure, so do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words: what a script that parses errors sees now versus before, and whether any value changed that an existing script could depend on (that decides whether it needs an upgrade note). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on your main test. Final report: findings per command, files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c6ef4b3e-de88-410d-a00f-4022ddbd8c5d","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgukYoLU8hh8BsDGuAj1G","requestRef":"79b74ffb-56e8-4d7f-8e7f-b49e900ad6d4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e638018-dce2-40b6-af26-21644e352de8","timestamp":"2026-11-10T18:52:07.673Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae5865da7dc4349e3","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/note-once","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"9e638018-dce2-40b6-af26-21644e352de8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgukYoinXwagM1T1zEpDE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014Y4N4PKPkUpAhVbDHZ82FZ","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"spec-test-gaps","description":"Tests for untested spec criteria","prompt":"Task: add tests for spec criteria that have none (trail #178). Test-only: no code or spec change unless a test reveals the code is wrong (then stop and report). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c test/spec-gaps origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nThe seven gaps, from a spec re-check (criteria are in docs/specs/*.json; first check each: it may already be covered by a test added since, in which case say so and skip it):\n1. MX-OUT-02 (matrix): two cargo artifacts on the same triple sort by `artifactName`.\n2. MX-ERR-06: a non-string entry in a target list is rejected; the CLI test should check exit code 1 and that the path appears in the message for `engines.node` and `requires-python` (today it checks only non-zero).\n3. MX-ERR-07: the CLI test checks the package name but not the error code E102.\n4. MX-DISC-02: \"neither field means no entry\" is asserted only at helper level; add an end-to-end CLI test.\n5. WS-ID-08: E101 (two packages resolving to one tag) has no test.\n6. WS-ID-09: E007 has only unit tests; none for the `dynamic = [\"version\"]` case, or for failing before `version` and `init` write anything.\n7. VER-CS-03: byte-order mark and lone carriage return handling in changesets has no test.\n\nRules: each test must fail if the behavior regresses, so for each, make a temporary mutation of the behavior it pins (or the assertion's subject) and confirm the test fails, then restore. Drive the real built binary for CLI behavior (patterns in crates/callisto-cli/tests). Use real fixtures, not mocks. Name tests after the behavior, not the criterion id. Match surrounding style; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset (tests only). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code. Final report: for each of the seven, the test name and file (or why skipped), the mutation you used and that it failed, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_read_input_tokens":623288,"output_tokens":4395,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":969},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1555,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4395,"cache_read_input_tokens":623288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1555},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014Y4N4PKPkUpAhVbDHZ82FZ":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"spec-test-gaps","description":"Tests for untested spec criteria","prompt":"Task: add tests for spec criteria that have none (trail #178). Test-only: no code or spec change unless a test reveals the code is wrong (then stop and report). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c test/spec-gaps origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nThe seven gaps, from a spec re-check (criteria are in docs/specs/*.json; first check each: it may already be covered by a test added since, in which case say so and skip it):\n1. MX-OUT-02 (matrix): two cargo artifacts on the same triple sort by `artifactName`.\n2. MX-ERR-06: a non-string entry in a target list is rejected; the CLI test should check exit code 1 and that the path appears in the message for `engines.node` and `requires-python` (today it checks only non-zero).\n3. MX-ERR-07: the CLI test checks the package name but not the error code E102.\n4. MX-DISC-02: \"neither field means no entry\" is asserted only at helper level; add an end-to-end CLI test.\n5. WS-ID-08: E101 (two packages resolving to one tag) has no test.\n6. WS-ID-09: E007 has only unit tests; none for the `dynamic = [\"version\"]` case, or for failing before `version` and `init` write anything.\n7. VER-CS-03: byte-order mark and lone carriage return handling in changesets has no test.\n\nRules: each test must fail if the behavior regresses, so for each, make a temporary mutation of the behavior it pins (or the assertion's subject) and confirm the test fails, then restore. Drive the real built binary for CLI behavior (patterns in crates/callisto-cli/tests). Use real fixtures, not mocks. Name tests after the behavior, not the criterion id. Match surrounding style; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset (tests only). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code. Final report: for each of the seven, the test name and file (or why skipped), the mutation you used and that it failed, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c6ef4b3e-de88-410d-a00f-4022ddbd8c5d","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgukYoLU8hh8BsDGuAj1G","requestRef":"79b74ffb-56e8-4d7f-8e7f-