{"parentUuid":"d692b6e4-850a-4099-abf8-ce5479670c47","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgukbFnkJXhibaU8sMFoc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Four agents are running in parallel, all aimed at the 1.0 promises in `docs/stability.md`.\n\n| Agent | Type and model | Does what |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `error-envelope` | implementer, Sonnet | Reproduces every command's JSON failure output with the real binary, then fixes any that differ from the specs. That's trail #177. |\n| `spec-test-gaps` | implementer, Sonnet | Adds tests for the seven untested spec criteria, each checked by a mutation. That's trail #178. |\n| `v1-stability-audit` | bug-hunter, Sonnet, read-only | Checks each row of the Stable table against the code and tests: flags, exit codes 0/1/2, `schemaVersion`, unknown config keys, error-code reuse, and tags and action inputs. |\n| `json-naming-inventory` | Explore, Haiku, read-only | Lists every serialized field that isn't camelCase, such as `short_sha`, and whether it sits in a versioned file. |\n\n**Why this order.** Once 1.0 ships, a frozen surface like JSON field names or error shapes needs a major version to change. These are the cheapest things to fix now.\n\nI'll review each result against its criteria, run the full checks outside the sandbox, do the overlap check, and write the changesets in the layered shape. The audit and inventory results will decide the next implementation batch, so I'll fold their findings into a ranked list for you.\n\nneeds input: none now. I'll report as each agent finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8768,"cache_read_input_tokens":624843,"output_tokens":504,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tok