{"parentUuid":"27552dd3-005a-4da7-95f3-14fea2ad9491","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgukouFawBWihN3wV9rWS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"My scanner and the agent both miss `ChangeKind::Commit { short_sha }`, so I'm adding a test that serializes every public JSON type and fails on any underscore key, and launching a fifth agent for it.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":637012,"output_tokens":2557,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1162},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2557,"cache_read_input_tokens":637012,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"c939dffa-0015-48d8-8687-14564f39336a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgukotuz9Mcv8K2wNV7N1","requestRef":"ad8dcf46-5d47-42a0-96f6-0e0d56d5c956","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"963f9503-00e1-4d37-9862-80c892f1704f","timestamp":"2026-11-10T18:55:26.722Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae5865da7dc4349e3","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/note-once","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"963f9503-00e1-4d37-9862-80c892f1704f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgukouFawBWihN3wV9rWS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018wHqP73h2goxnwW7dgszHo","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"camel-case-fields","description":"camelCase for all JSON fields","prompt":"Task: make every serialized JSON field name camelCase before 1.0, and add a test that keeps it that way. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them (the --format json reports and versioned files are a 1.0 stability surface; the CI-plumbing envelopes are tied to the exact Callisto version, so their keys may change pre-1.0).\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/camel-case-fields origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nProblem: serde's `rename_all = \"camelCase\"` on an ENUM renames only variants, not the fields inside struct variants. Use `rename_all_fields = \"camelCase\"` too (serde 1.0.185 or newer; check the workspace's serde version) or an explicit `#[serde(rename = ...)]` on the field. Known misses (an audit agent and my scan, both incomplete, so find the rest yourself): crates/callisto-graph/src/release_preview.rs `ChangeKind::Commit { short_sha }` (serializes `short_sha`); crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs `BumpReason::Cascade { dep_kind, dependency_to }`; crates/callisto-model/src/release_observation.rs `ProviderEvidenceV1` (`peeled_commit`, `tag_name`, `byte_length`) and its `...Wire` twin; crates/callisto-model/src/release/operation.rs `ReleaseOperationRoleWire` (`binding_digest`, `registry_key`). Look for every other `Serialize` enum or struct whose multi-word field has no camelCase rename, including types that appear inside versioned reports and files. Do not rename fields of types that are never serialized to JSON for users or CI, and do not touch Deserialize-only input formats whose snake_case keys come from external tools (Cargo.toml, package.json, pyproject.toml, changeset frontmatter).\n\nRequired:\n1. Fix every such field. Where a reader accepts older files (e.g. a `Wire` twin that reads stored JSON), check what must still parse and keep a `#[serde(alias = \"old_name\")]` only if a stored file written by a released Callisto would otherwise stop loading; report each place you did or did not add an alias and why.\n2. Add one guard test (or a small helper plus a test per public report/file type family) that serializes a representative value of each user-facing or CI JSON type and asserts that no key at any depth contains an underscore. It must fail on the current code for the known misses and pass after the fix. Cover at least: the release preview (all ChangeKind variants, PublishOutlook, Findings), the BumpReason variants inside version/status reports, the release receipt provider evidence variants, and operation role wire types.\n3. Update docs/specs and docs/architecture only where they name one of the old keys; keep spec JSON valid.\n4. Update the stored-file fixtures and tests that assert old keys.\n\nDo NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words, which JSON keys changed (old to new, and in which report or file) so I can judge whether it needs an upgrade note. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-model`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, and a mutation check on the guard test (remove one rename and confirm it fails). Final report: the full list of fields changed, aliases decision, files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":637012,"output_tokens":2557,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1162},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2557,"cache_read_input_tokens":637012,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018wHqP73h2goxnwW7dgszHo":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"camel-case-fields","description":"camelCase for all JSON fields","prompt":"Task: make every serialized JSON field name camelCase before 1.0, and add a test that keeps it that way. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them (the --format json reports and versioned files are a 1.0 stability surface; the CI-plumbing envelopes are tied to the exact Callisto version, so their keys may change pre-1.0).\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/camel-case-fields origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nProblem: serde's `rename_all = \"camelCase\"` on an ENUM renames only variants, not the fields inside struct variants. Use `rename_all_fields = \"camelCase\"` too (serde 1.0.185 or newer; check the workspace's serde version) or an explicit `#[serde(rename = ...)]` on the field. Known misses (an audit agent and my scan, both incomplete, so find the rest yourself): crates/callisto-graph/src/release_preview.rs `ChangeKind::Commit { short_sha }` (serializes `short_sha`); crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs `BumpReason::Casca