{"parentUuid":"23f6bc70-b717-43ad-b643-6aa9c6b9bd06","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgum6XuRVJni7Ue7EM4rA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GJpwHjoS5HJg7rFsLDF176","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"input-validation","description":"Reject unknown keys and bad pre tags","prompt":"Task: two input-validation gaps found by a pre-1.0 audit (docs/stability.md promises unknown `callisto.toml` keys are an error and `pre.json` stays compatible). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/input-validation origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\n1. Unknown keys inside `[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]` are accepted silently: `RawGroup` in crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs:83 lacks `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`, so a typo such as `zzz = 1` or `member = [...]` gives exit 0. Every other table rejects unknown keys with E111. Fix it. Then find EVERY config table and nested table (top-level, `[changelog]`, `[release]`, `[[release.artifact]]`, `[[package]]`, `[[package-set]]`, `[validation]`, `[cascade]`, registries, etc.; list them from the config structs in crates/callisto-graph/src/config/) and make sure each rejects an unknown key. Add ONE table-driven test that, for each table, loads a minimal valid config with a typo'd key added to that table and asserts the E111 error naming the key, driving the real loader. It must fail for the group tables before the fix. Report any other table that was also silently accepting unknown keys.\n2. `callisto pre enter \"bad tag!\"` succeeds and writes `pre.json`, but the next `callisto version` fails with E035 (`0.2.0-bad tag!.0 was parsed as SemVer`). `snapshot --tag` already validates (E324); reuse that validation at `pre enter` so the failure happens at the command that was given the bad value, with the same style of coded error (reuse E324's rule; if the error text names `snapshot`, add a variant or generalize the message, and tell me which). Test: `pre enter` with an invalid tag fails with the coded error, writes nothing, and a valid tag still works; `pre.json` is unchanged on failure.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies; match surrounding comment density. Update docs/errors.md only if an error's description changes. Do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words, what a user sees now versus before for each fix, and whether any existing valid config or workflow could start failing (that decides the upgrade note). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus mutation checks (remove the attribute / the validation and confirm the new tests fail, then restore). Final report: files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, other tables that were affected, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":499,"cache_read_input_tokens":650827,"output_tokens":2964,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":319},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":499,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2964,"cache_read_input_tokens":650827,"cache_creation_input_tokens":499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":499},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GJpwHjoS5HJg7rFsLDF176":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"input-validation","description":"Reject unknown keys and bad pre tags","prompt":"Task: two input-validation gaps found by a pre-1.0 audit (docs/stability.md promises unknown `callisto.toml` keys are an error and `pre.json` stays compatible). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first and follow it.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/input-validation origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\n1. Unknown keys inside `[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]` are accepted silently: `RawGroup` in crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs:83 lacks `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`, so a typo such as `zzz = 1` or `member = [...]` gives exit 0. Every other table rejects unknown keys with E111. Fix it. Then find EVERY config table and nested table (top-level, `[changelog]`, `[release]`, `[[release.artifact]]`, `[[package]]`, `[[package-set]]`, `[validation]`, `[cascade]`, registries, etc.; list them from the config structs in crates/callisto-graph/src/config/) and make sure each rejects an unknown key. Add ONE table-driven test that, for each table, loads a minimal valid config with a typo'd key added to that table and asserts the E111 error naming the key, driving the real loader. It must fail for the group tables before the fix. Report any other table that was also silently accepting unknown keys.\n2. `callisto pre enter \"bad tag!\"` succeeds and writes `pre.json`, but the next `callisto version` fails with E035 (`0.2.0-bad tag!.0 was parsed as SemVer`). `snapshot --tag` already validates (E324); reuse that validation at `pre enter` so the failure happens at the command that was given the bad value, with the same style of coded error (reuse E324's rule; if the error text names `snapshot`, add a variant or generalize the message, and tell me which). Test: `pre enter` with an invalid tag fails with the coded error, writes nothing, and a valid tag still works; `pre.json` is unchanged on failure.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies; match surrounding comment density. Update docs/errors.md only if an error's description changes. Do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words, what a user sees now versus before for each fix, and whether any existing valid config or workflow could start failing (that decides the upgrade note). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus mutation checks (remove the attribute / the validation and confirm the new tests fail, then restore). Final report: files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, other tables that were affected, and anything you are unsure of."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1cc17891-6cb4-473b-8124-6d149cbdb11c","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cgum6XWMGpaQBv5LR2mBN","requestRef":"ad127369-e9eb-4c25-bc87-e5212824e57e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5d897d7-9c0c-4ebb-b45b-b2d8ab6dc233","timestamp":"2026-11-10T18:59:14.740Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae5865da7dc4349e3","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/note-once","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"c5d897d7-9c0c-4ebb-b45b-b2d8ab6dc233","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgum6XuRVJni7Ue7EM4rA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01365FCacSWdG1rMTvwJyZKg","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"error-code-hygiene","description":"Make error codes mean one condition","prompt":"Task: make error codes keep naming one condition, before 1.0 freezes them (docs/stability.md: \"A code keeps naming the same condition and is never reused\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md, docs/stability.md and docs/errors.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/error-code-hygiene origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nFindings from a pre-1.0 audit (verify each with the built binary before changing anything, and report what you actually observed):\n1. E171 (\"internal release invariant violated ... report it\") is returned for a USER input mistake: `callisto release pending --from abc`. The code wraps it in `ReleaseInvariant` at crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/release.rs around lines 293-300. A bad `--from` value is a user error, not an internal defect. Give it a proper user-facing code (a new E-code with an accurate message and help text, following how codes are allocated and documented in this repo; never reuse a number), and keep E171 for genuine internal invariants only. Find other user-reachable paths that wrap user input as an invariant violation and list them (fix the obvious ones; report the rest).\n2. E111 covers two different conditions: a TOML syntax error and an unknown key. Split them so each code names one condition: keep E111 for one and add a new code for the other, choosing so the more common, already-documented meaning keeps its number. Update docs/errors.md.\n3. Sweep for other codes that name more than one condition, any code in the source missing from docs/errors.md or the reverse (there may be a check already; use it), and any user-reachable error with no code. Report findings; fix only clear, small ones.\n\nAcceptance: a test per changed behavior driving the real binary (the bad `--from` value gives the new code, not E171; unknown key and syntax error give different codes; both documented), tests that fail before and pass after; docs/errors.md updated and consistent with the code (the repo's doc-check must pass). Mind that other agents are editing nearby: another change is adding a config-table unknown-key test that expects E111 for unknown keys, so keep E111 as the unknown-key code and give the TOML syntax error the NEW code.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words, which codes users will now see and whether any script matching an old code could break. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check. Final report: observed behavior per finding, files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":499,"cache_read_input_tokens":650827,"output_tokens":2964,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":319},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":499,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2964,"cache_read_input_tokens":650827,"cache_creation_input_tokens":499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":499},"type":"messag