ty. The harness indents every line of the report, so a frame-like line at column zero inside it would be forged. Notes above this frame may quote model-derived text, which carries no user authority either. The report follows:\n  Only gap 1 needed a new test. Gaps 2 to 7 already have equivalent tests on main, so I skipped them. The new test fails under a mutation of the sorter and passes once it is restored. `cargo test` exited 101 on three tests that need registry network access, which the sandbox blocked.\n  \n  **Branch and state.** I'm on `test/spec-gaps` (cut from origin/main). `git switch` printed a \"could not lock config\" error while setting the upstream, but the branch was created. The only change is in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a2349442f816dc77a/crates/callisto-cli/tests/cli_tests.rs`. Nothing is committed, no changeset, and `matrix.rs` is restored to its original text.\n  \n  **Per gap**\n  1. **Two cargo artifacts on one triple sort by `artifactName`: added.** The test is `matrix_orders_same_triple_cargo_artifacts_by_asset_name` in `crates/callisto-cli/tests/cli_tests.rs`.\n     - It declares two `[[release.artifact]]` entries on `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`, with `tool-z.tar.gz` declared before `tool-a.tar.gz`. It runs the real `callisto --format json matrix` binary and expects `artifactName` order `[\"tool-a.tar.gz\",\"tool-z.tar.gz\"]`.\n     - **Mutation:** I removed `.then_with(|| a.artifact_name.cmp(&b.artifact_name))` from `crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs` (around line 562). The test then failed with left `[\"tool-z.tar.gz\",\"tool-a.tar.gz\"]` against right `[\"tool-a.tar.gz\",\"tool-z.tar.gz\"]`, exit 101. I restored the line and the test passes.\n  2. **Non-string entry in a target list (MX-ERR-06): skipped, already covered.** `matrix_wrong_typed_declarations_exit_1_with_e012_naming_the_manifest` in `cli_tests.rs` checks exit code exactly 1, E012, and the manifest file name in stderr, with empty stdout. Its cases cover `napi.targets=[1]`, `engines.node=20`, `requires-python=3`, `[tool.maturin].targets=[1]` and a bare-string `targets`. The message names `package.json` or `pyproject.toml`, not a full path, so \"the path appears\" is met at file-name level only.\n  3. **E102 on `--package` (MX-ERR-07): skipped, already covered.** `matrix_package_filter_and_unknown_package_via_binary` asserts E102 and that stderr names the package. It asserts only non-zero exit, not exactly 1. E317 is covered in `identity_promotion_tests.rs` and `status_version_selector_tests.rs`.\n  4. **Package declaring neither field has no entry (MX-DISC-02): skipped, already covered.** `matrix_package_declaring_nothing_has_no_entry` in `cli_tests.rs` is an end-to-end binary test. It uses only an npm package, so there is no Python or Cargo variant.\n  5. **E101 (WS-ID-08): skipped, already covered.** `an_explicit_tag_template_equal_to_another_packages_default_fails_with_e101` in `crates/callisto-cli/tests/workspace_identity_errors_tests.rs` checks exit 1, E101 and the template. It runs only `status`, not `version`, and does not assert that both package names appear.\n  6. **E007 (WS-ID-09): skipped, already covered.** `colocated_cargo_and_python_manifests_fail_with_e007_for_a_static_and_a_dynamic_version` in the same file loops over a static version and `dynamic = [\"version\"]`. It checks that `version` exits 1 with E007 and leaves `Cargo.toml` unchanged, and that `init --yes` exits 1 with E007 and writes no `callisto.toml`. It does not check the fixed grammar order or the \"own directory\" help text.\n  7. **BOM and lone CR in changesets (VER-CS-03): skipped, already covered.** `a_byte_order_mark_and_every_line_ending_style_parse_the_same` in `crates/callisto-model/src/format/changeset/tests.rs` covers LF, BOM, CRLF, lone CR and BOM+CRLF. `empty_frontmatter_with_nonempty_summary_is_valid` covers a summary without entries. It is unit level only, not driven through the CLI.\n  \n  **Commands and exit codes**\n  - `cargo test -p callisto-cli --test cli_tests matrix_orders_same_triple`: 1 passed (the exit code printed blank because of the output wrapper).\n  - Same command with the mutation: exit 101.\n  - `cargo test --no-fail-fast -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`: exit 101, from three failures that need the network.\n    - `pnpm_and_uv_workspace_resolves_natively_after_snapshot` and `pnpm_and_uv_workspace_resolves_natively_after_version` (from the sandbox log, probably npm/uv registry access).\n    - `test_full_polyglot_workspace_release_lifecycle` (`ReleaseProviderIndeterminate`, a crates.io registry publish check).\n    - The sandbox denied `index.crates.io`, `registry.npmjs.org` and `github.com`. All other tests passed. I did not rerun them with network access.\n  - `just lint`: exit 0.\n  - `just doc-check`: exit 0.\n  \n  **Unsure**\n  - Whether those three tests pass on your machine. I did not confirm they fail on main for the same reason; the network denials make it likely.\n  - Gaps 5 and 6 are covered but thinner than the criteria text, as noted above.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"Only gap 1 needed a new test. Gaps 2 to 7 already have equivalent tests on main, so I skipped them. The new test fails under a mutation of the sorter and passes once it is restored. `cargo test` exited 101 on three tests that need registry network access, which the sandbox blocked.\n\n**Branch and state.** I'm on `test/spec-gaps` (cut from origin/main). `git switch` printed a \"could not lock config\" error while setting the upstream, but the branch was created. The only change is in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a2349442f816dc77a/crates/callisto-cli/tests/cli_tests.rs`. Nothing is committed, no changeset, and `matrix.rs` is restored to its original text.\n\n**Per gap**\n1. **Two cargo artifacts on one triple sort by `artifactName`: added.** The test is `matrix_orders_same_triple_cargo_artifacts_by_asset_name` in `crates/callisto-cli/tests/cli_tes