{"parentUuid":"8c891281-8e2e-419d-b23c-21bb5022a604","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgumMQ44K7ZKf16euYhpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1783,"cache_read_input_tokens":668425,"output_tokens":1960,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1118},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1783,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1960,"cache_read_input_tokens":668425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1783,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1783},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9366,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"70831a7a-4aec-4ec1-9f7b-de122fa92d90","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgumMPgE7dkLtpn1kWJeW","requestRef":"157ffb72-8aa2-4bfa-b22b-b6a43fdc6f71","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e49c0bbd-849a-47d4-9a30-4843050520f4","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:02:33.796Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a2349442f816dc77a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/error-code-hygiene","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"e49c0bbd-849a-47d4-9a30-4843050520f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgumMQ44K7ZKf16euYhpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The audit's remaining findings are in, and five of its top fixes are already in flight. Here's how every finding maps to work:\n\n| Audit finding | Status |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| 1. `release pending` and `release build-python` have no `schemaVersion` | `error-envelope`, scope extended |\n| 2. Report fields not camelCase, plus a guard test | `camel-case-fields` |\n| 3. Unknown keys silently accepted in `[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]` | `input-validation` |\n| 5. `pre enter` accepts invalid tags | `input-validation` |\n| 6. E171 and E111 each name two conditions | `error-code-hygiene` |\n| 4. Usage errors exit 1, not the promised 2 | held until `error-envelope` lands (same `main.rs` path) |\n| `add` writes a changeset its own reader rejects (a duplicate package) | next batch |\n| `snapshot --strict` help text is wrong | next batch |\n| `status` prints `lastReleasedVersion: null` but omits `lastTag` | next batch |\n| `version_command` can't take quoted arguments (undocumented) | next batch, as a documentation note |\n\nI'm holding the \"next batch\" until the camelCase and envelope agents land, since they touch the same report and CLI files and I don't want to repeat the overlap mistake.\n\n**Two decisions for you, with my recommendations**\n1. **Exit code 2 for usage errors.** Clap-level mistakes exit 2, but every runtime check of a value you passed (a bad severity, a missing `--summary`, a bad tag) exits 1. **Recommend:** map the usage-class error codes to exit 2, so the promise in `docs/stability.md` is true. The alternative is to reword the promise to \"clap-level errors only\", which is cheaper but weaker for script authors. Pre-1.0 is the only cheap moment.\n2. **Bare names in changeset keys.** `add cargo/a` writes `a: minor`, and a later `npm/a` package makes that ambiguous. `stability.md` says other ecosystems use `ecosystem/name` keys, which isn't what the code does. **Recommend:** keep the behavior, since it stays compatible with `@changesets/cli`, and reword the promise to \"bare name unless ambiguous, then qualified\". The ambiguity already fails loudly with a coded error.\n\nneeds input: a yes or no on both recommendations, and I'll queue exit-2 behind `error-envelope` on a yes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1783,"cache_read_input_tokens":668425,"output_tokens":1960,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1118},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1783,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1960,"cache_read_input_tokens":668425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1783,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1783},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"70831a7a-4aec-4ec1-9f7b-de122fa92d90","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgumMPgE7dkLtpn1kWJeW","requestRef":"157ffb72-8aa2-4bfa-b22b-b6a43fdc6f71","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e056fd4-e421-409a-b8e1-abb20c8e9987","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:02:39.591Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a2349442f816dc77a","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/error-code-hygiene","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
