{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"d2104fb83ea82a1cbe444cf1c12d9a0b3667a27f640adf53e771f32af352eacc","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The camelCase fix is solid in design. It uses `rename_all_fields`, adds a guard test that walks every key at every depth, and its mutation proof is clear. Two things I want to check myself: the agent mutated all three enums together, so I'll confirm one alone is caught, and it never got a clean full-suite exit code. Reviewing the diff, then running everything outside the sandbox."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HZvx1Ker9dQpuvZVEYuQMr","name":"EnterWorktree","input":{"path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a70a2dcb75857e08c"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
