{"parentUuid":"a3a5d019-b019-4aa4-9f01-b20996c95938","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgumvMWvYqMKGhegPo7V8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EVYJxdqHn1xTxJFrCTaNbF","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"error-code-hygiene","summary":"Keep E111 as TOML syntax, new codes for the rest","message":"Correction to my earlier instruction: E111's already-documented meaning is \"callisto.toml is not valid TOML\", and docs/stability.md says a code keeps naming the same condition. So do NOT move that meaning. Swap your allocation: E111 stays the TOML syntax error; the NEW codes go to the other conditions: unknown key becomes E325 (ConfigError::UnknownField), wrong-type or missing-required-key stays E326 (ConfigError::InvalidValue). Update crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs code() mapping, docs/errors.md (E111 keeps its original wording; add E325 and E326 as unknown key and wrong-type value), and your tests accordingly (config_syntax_error_reports_e111, config_unknown_key_reports_e325, config_value_of_the_wrong_type_reports_e326). Keep E327 and E328 for release pending --from. Another branch (fix/input-validation) has a test expecting E111 for an unknown key; I will update that one, you do not need to. Re-run the new tests, lint and doc-check, redo your mutation check, and report only the delta plus exit codes. Still do not commit, push or sign.","type":"message","recipient":"error-code-hygiene","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Correction to my earlier instruction: E111's alre…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8408,"cache_read_input_tokens":692096,"output_tokens":2004,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":884},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8408,"e