{"parentUuid":"657b4de0-5133-4a75-88c4-7dd55fe70c2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgumvMWvYqMKGhegPo7V8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E95TomdkzJRwG4HbSTXCAY","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"input-validation","summary":"Keep dotted pre tags working at pre enter","message":"Decision on your dotted-tag finding: `pre enter beta.1` and `rc.2` worked before and must keep working (0.2.0-beta.1.0 is valid SemVer), so do not break them. Make `pre enter` use a pre-release-specific rule: one or more dot-separated identifiers, each non-empty and made only of letters, digits and `-` (SemVer pre-release identifier syntax), while `snapshot --tag` keeps its stricter single-identifier rule. Keep one shared validator function with the two rules expressed in one place (for example a parameter or two small wrappers), keep E324 for both and keep its message/help accurate for both rules, and update docs/errors.md E324 wording. Tests: `beta.1`, `rc.2` and `pr-42` succeed at pre enter; `bad tag!`, `x/y`, `` (empty), `a..b`, `.a` and `a.` fail at pre enter with E324 and write nothing; `snapshot --tag a.b` still fails. Also, the unknown-key code is changing on another branch: unknown keys in callisto.toml will report a NEW code E325 and E111 stays TOML-syntax only, so make your every_config_table_rejects_an_unknown_key test assert on the error message naming the key and on the variant for unknown-field, not on the literal E111; if that variant does not exist on your base, assert on the message text only and tell me which. Re-run tests, lint, doc-check and your mutation checks, and report only the delta with exit codes. Do not commit, push or sign.","type":"message","recipient":"input-validation","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Decision on your dotted-tag finding: `pre enter b…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"us