{"parentUuid":"ee2c2fc4-44d3-4f2d-955f-b6a25ea9f753","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a21ef840-835b-4486-82aa-11c814c1e089","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:10:05.948Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a70a2dcb75857e08c","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/camel-case-fields","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"aa867e79c166b153170c75b41b590e830eeda2fd556f23baf345611f2c783e60","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Four of five implementers have reported, and the camelCase change is pushed. I'm correcting my E111 instruction: it keeps its documented \"not valid TOML\" meaning, and the new codes go to the other conditions, with both corrections sent to the owning agents.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EVYJxdqHn1xTxJFrCTaNbF","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"error-code-hygiene","summary":"Keep E111 as TOML syntax, new codes for the rest","message":"Correction to my earlier instruction: E111's already-documented meaning is \"callisto.toml is not valid TOML\", and docs/stability.md says a code keeps naming the same condition. So do NOT move that meaning. Swap your allocation: E111 stays the TOML syntax error; the NEW codes go to the other conditions: unknown key becomes E325 (ConfigError::UnknownField), wrong-type or missing-required-key stays E326 (ConfigError::InvalidValue). Update crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs code() mapping, docs/errors.md (E111 keeps its original wording; add E325 and E326 as unknown key and wrong-type value), and your tests accordingly (config_syntax_error_reports_e111, config_unknown_key_reports_e325, config_value_of_the_wrong_type_reports_e326). Keep E327 and E328 for release pending --from. Another branch (fix/input-validation) has a test expecting E111 for an unknown key; I will update that one, you do not need to. Re-run the new tests, lint and doc-check, redo your mutation check, and report only the delta plus exit codes. Still do not commit, push or sign."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E95TomdkzJRwG4HbSTXCAY","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"input-validation","summary":"Keep dotted pre tags working at pre enter","message":"Decision on your dotted-tag finding: `pre enter beta.1` and `rc.2` worked before and must keep working (0.2.0-beta.1.0 is valid SemVer), so do not break them. Make `pre enter` use a pre-release-specific rule: one or more dot-separated identifiers, each non-empty and made only of letters, digits and `-` (SemVer pre-release identifier syntax), while `snapshot --tag` keeps its stricter single-identifier rule. Keep one shared validator function with the two rules expressed in one place (for example a parameter or two small wrappers), keep E324 for both and keep its message/help accurate for both rules, and update docs/errors.md E324 wording. Tests: `beta.1`, `rc.2` and `pr-42` succeed at pre enter; `bad tag!`, `x/y`, `` (empty), `a..b`, `.a` and `a.` fail at pre enter with E324 and write nothing; `snapshot --tag a.b` still fails. Also, the unknown-key code is changing on another branch: unknown keys in callisto.toml will report a NEW code E325 and E111 stays TOML-syntax only, so make your every_config_table_rejects_an_unknown_key test assert on the error message naming the key and on the variant for unknown-field, not on the literal E111; if that variant does not exist on your base, assert on the message text only and tell me which. Re-run tests, lint, doc-check and your mutation checks, and report only the delta with exit codes. Do not commit, push or sign."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
