{"parentUuid":"49a6f638-47f6-4bd3-ba24-2d63ce7c3a1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgunYonVUH6DXa3tjBJQ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TtPXhQtGoHgy6z3UCdkg2N","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr499-body","description":"PR body for 499","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr499.diff. Change: `callisto release pending --format json` and hidden `release build-python --format json` now use the standard report envelope (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`) with their payloads (`pending`, `built`) unchanged; a failing run reports `command: \"release pending\"` / `\"release build-python\"` instead of `\"release\"`. New tests run the real binary and assert the error envelope (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`, with and without `--dry-run`) for every command family: core commands, matrix and compose-pr-body, release, release pending, release build-python, release plan and release-pr verify. Finding: the trail's main complaint (release plan and release-pr subcommands reporting the wrong `command`) was already fixed on main; these tests lock it. REL-CMD-12 in docs/specs/release.json now lists the two commands. Left alone: `release inspect` success prints the raw input document with no envelope (by design). Why now: docs/stability.md says every `--format json` report carries `schemaVersion` from 1.0.\nVerified: a mutation passing `false` instead of the real `--dry-run` flag fails the new tests; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Gap: no success-path test for build-python (needs a Python toolchain).\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 170 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":738103,"output_tokens":3021,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":145},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3021,"cache_read_input_tokens":738103,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TtPXhQtGoHgy6z3UCdkg2N":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr499-body","description":"PR body for 499","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr499.diff. Change: `callisto release pending --format json` and hidden `release build-python --format json` now use the standard report envelope (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`) with their payloads (`pending`, `built`) unchanged; a failing run reports `command: \"release pending\"` / `\"release build-python\"` instead of `\"release\"`. New tests run the real binary and assert the error envelope (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`, with and without `--dry-run`) for every command family: core commands, matrix and compose-pr-body, release, release pending, release build-python, release plan and release-pr verify. Finding: the trail's main complaint (release plan and release-pr subcommands reporting the wrong `command`) was already fixed on main; these tests lock it. REL-CMD-12 in docs/specs/release.json now lists the two commands. Left alone: `release inspect` success prints the raw input document with no envelope (by design). Why now: docs/stability.md says every `--format json` report carries `schemaVersion` from 1.0.\nVerified: a mutation passing `false` instead of the real `--dry-run` flag fails the new tests; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Gap: no success-path test for build-python (needs a Python toolchain).\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 170 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8e8f2f41-d928-40fd-9570-69790c0c1f93","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgunYoFjWrKZvN2diDz3b","requestRef":"57b12ee8-6912-45dc-8b9f-7892302abee0","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2c49a4b2-7da0-4424-90aa-3bb31da238e8","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:18:13.322Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"2c49a4b2-7da0-4424-90aa-3bb31da238e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgunYonVUH6DXa3tjBJQ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01695vH8BsjGZ5RMu6ZZFyzY","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr500-body","description":"PR body for 500","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr500.diff. Change: each error code now names one condition, because docs/stability.md says from 1.0 a code keeps its meaning. `callisto.toml`: E111 stays \"not valid TOML\" (syntax); an unknown key is now E325; a wrong-typed value or a missing required key is now E326 (a shared `parse_raw` in config/resolve.rs is used by both `config::load` and `init`). `release pending --from`: a value that is not a full 40-character SHA is E327 and a valid SHA that is not a release commit on this branch is E328; both used to report E171, which means \"internal release invariant violated, report it\". docs/errors.md updated. Compatibility cost: a script that matched E111 for an unknown key or wrong-type value, or E171 for a bad `--from`, stops matching; exit codes are unchanged. Not fixed, found by the sweep: E254 (\"unknown callisto key\") is a catch-all for several config conditions, and a few E171 sites in release/binding.rs and release/derive.rs look user-reachable through config but were not verified; both are follow-ups.\nVerified: six new tests drive the real binary (bad --from gives E327 or E328 not E171, syntax error E111, unknown key E325, wrong type E326, and every new code is documented); a mutation of the unknown-field detection fails the unknown-key test; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Note: this conflicts with the input-validation PR only in adjacent rows of docs/errors.md.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 200 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":738103,"output_tokens":3021,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":145},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3021,"cache_read_input_tokens":738103,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01695vH8BsjGZ5RMu6ZZFyzY":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr500-body","description":"PR body for 500","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr500.diff. Change: each error code now names one condition, because docs/stability.md says from 1.0 a code keeps its meaning. `callisto.toml`: E111 stays \"not valid TOML\" (syntax); an unknown key is now E325; a wrong-typed value or a missing required key is now E326 (a shared `parse_raw` in config/resolve.rs is used by both `config::load` and `init`). `release pending --from`: a value that is not a full 40-character SHA is E327 and a valid SHA that is not a release commit on this branch is E328; both used to report E171, which means \"internal release invariant violated, report it\". docs/errors.md updated. Compatibility cost: a script that matched E111 for an unknown key or wrong-type value, or E171 for a bad `--from`, stops matching; exit codes are unchanged. Not fixed, found by the sweep: E254 (\"unknown callisto key\") is a catch-all for several config conditions, and a few E171 sites in release/binding.rs and release/derive.rs look user-reachable through config but were not verified; both are follow-ups.\nVerified: six new tests drive the real binary (bad --from gives E327 or E328 not E171, syntax error E111, unknown key E325, wrong type E326, and every new code is documented); a mutation of the unknown-field detection fails the unknown-key test; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Note: this conflicts with the input-validation PR only in adjacent rows of docs/errors.md.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 200 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8e8f2f41-d928-40fd-9570-69790c0c1f93","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgunYoFjWrKZvN2diDz3b","requestRef":"57b12ee8-6912-45dc-8b9f-7892302abee0","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d8f3f12c-8384-47ca-aa88-6cd07c6ff4f6","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:18:18.044Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stre