{"parentUuid":"2c49a4b2-7da0-4424-90aa-3bb31da238e8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dbb1916f-3ada-4200-99b2-5de90a6bbb44","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TtPXhQtGoHgy6z3UCdkg2N","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawned successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the ID below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagent_id: apr499-body-dea93db07bd52f19\nname: pr499-body\nThe agent is now running and will receive instructions via mailbox."}]}]},"uuid":"2160f6d8-c73d-44d1-8c8c-537d36b3b5e9","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:18:26.218Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"teammate_spawned","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr499.diff. Change: `callisto release pending --format json` and hidden `release build-python --format json` now use the standard report envelope (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`) with their payloads (`pending`, `built`) unchanged; a failing run reports `command: \"release pending\"` / `\"release build-python\"` instead of `\"release\"`. New tests run the real binary and assert the error envelope (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`, with and without `--dry-run`) for every command family: core commands, matrix and compose-pr-body, release, release pending, release build-python, release plan and release-pr verify. Finding: the trail's main complaint (release plan and release-pr subcommands reporting the wrong `command`) was already fixed on main; these tests lock it. REL-CMD-12 in docs/specs/release.json now lists the two commands. Left alone: `release inspect` success prints the raw input document with no envelope (by design). Why now: docs/stability.md says every `--format json` report carries `schemaVersion` from 1.0.\nVerified: a mutation passing `false` instead of the real `--dry-run` flag fails the new tests; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Gap: no success-path test for build-python (needs a Python toolchain).\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 170 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body.","agentId":"apr499-body-dea93db07bd52f19","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","teammate_id":"pr499-body@session-6cc3e47b","agent_id":"apr499-body-dea93db07bd52f19","agent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr499-body","color":"yellow","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-6cc3e47b","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8e8f2f41-d928-40fd-9570-69790c0c1f93","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","branch":"fix/input-validation","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2c49a4b2-7da0-4424-90aa-3bb31da238e8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionK