{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"e429afbd-7528-4029-b7ef-e30e50569af3","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:18:26.303Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"a5d78a38c3b33787e5b5d9b7008e9de2db1c7b9a9ca69bf894342b554f4e1149","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"57b12ee8-6912-45dc-8b9f-7892302abee0","keep":1201,"tail":["143cc39420e9e8e5836830b70f60fb62dd47313817899d821c990944c4f2dac6","85e3fd19413d18c52307cbf143c19dd69ac4d07eb5f38cfae78ca55731df5b82","41d93bbfb52011e0642c79c34afc54c3cc4c2007798d6922697df613e3d63011"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1203,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"df8eab89174cb5056aaf3c0da069a6fff69ab5b88af04f65f3a28dacb60f10ab"}
{"parentUuid":"53b83821-b239-4d02-b4de-3afc85da2656","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgunaNgSKoKhky8DqhLDf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Four 1.0-readiness PRs are open, and four agents are writing their descriptions in parallel. All four were reviewed and run through the full checks outside the sandbox, with signed commits and trails linked. CI has not run on any of them.\n\n| PR | What it fixes before 1.0 | Evidence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **#498** | Six JSON keys were snake_case (`short_sha`, `dep_kind` and others), because `rename_all` on an enum doesn't rename its fields. | A guard test walks every key at every depth. Removing each of the three attributes alone fails it. |\n| **#499** | `release pending` and `release build-python` JSON had no `schemaVersion` envelope, and their failure `command` was wrong. | New tests assert the error envelope for every command family, with and without `--dry-run`. The trail's original complaint was already fixed on main, and the tests now lock that in. |\n| **#500** | E111 named three conditions and E171 (\"internal defect\") fired on user input. | E111 keeps its documented TOML-syntax meaning. New codes: E325 (unknown key), E326 (wrong value), E327 and E328 (`--from`). |\n| **#501** | Unknown keys in group tables were silently accepted, and `pre enter` accepted tags that failed later. | A table-driven test covers 12 config tables, and dotted tags like `beta.1` keep working. |\n\n**Merge order.** #500 and #501 conflict only in adjacent rows of `docs/errors.md`. Merge #500 first, and I'll resolve the one-line doc conflict on #501. The other branches are clean against each other.\n\n**Corrections I made to the agents' work**\n- **E111:** I'd told the agent to move its meaning, which would break the stability promise. It now keeps its documented meaning.\n- **Dotted tags:** the agent had made `pre enter beta.1` fail. I had it keep them working.\n\n**Changesets.** Each is in the layered shape. #498, #500 and #501 are minor with `Breaking:` or `Action:` notes, and #499 is a patch with an `Action:`.\n\n**Not done yet:** exit code 2 for usage errors, the next batch (duplicate packages in `add`, the `--strict` help text, the `lastTag` null) and `ChangeKind`'s remaining items. They wait on your two decisions and on these merging.\n\nneeds input: review #498 to #501, and your yes or no on the exit-2 and bare-names recommendations."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3744,"cache_read_input_tokens":738906,"output_tokens":825,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3744,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":738906,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3744},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fdb90a0b-e32b-44c4-84f4-f3f19a6ff9fa","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgunaNKr2GR5QdAq1zfHL","requestRef":"e429afbd-7528-4029-b7ef-e30e50569af3","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad9979ea-5827-4c43-9602-ca5097249edc","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:18:33.053Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
