{"parentUuid":"8f14ffb7-9122-4050-b80f-fcb0c6b6c52c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"95244cbd-e378-4c54-8b85-fd98cef6051e","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:18:49.388Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"28ed102fcc7609ac45f5c444567fe74056c0e24f9e921c4297cf8f7df5c24d20","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Applying the two bodies that came back, #498 and #501. #499 and #500 are still being written."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SUAinSfSMZorja7UixCs5y","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr498_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\n`rename_all = \"camelCase\"` on an enum renames only variants, not the fields inside struct variants, so six JSON keys shipped as snake_case. The three affected enums now also carry `rename_all_fields = \"camelCase\"`. This lands before 1.0 because `docs/stability.md` freezes `--format json` report shapes from 1.0, and a later rename would need a major version.\n\n## Breaking\n\nSix keys are renamed:\n\n- `reason.dep_kind` and `reason.dependency_to` in `version` and `snapshot` reports become `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n- `short_sha` in the release preview file becomes `shortSha`.\n- `peeled_commit`, `tag_name` and `byte_length` in the release receipt become `peeledCommit`, `tagName` and `byteLength`.\n\nNo serde aliases were added. The preview and receipt are CI-plumbing files tied to the exact Callisto version, and `BumpReason` is output-only. The changeset is minor, with Breaking and Action notes.\n\n## Verify\n\n- A new guard test fails on any snake_case key in the release preview, `BumpReason` inside version and snapshot reports, the release receipt, and operation roles. Removing each of the three attributes on its own makes it fail.\n- `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0.\n- Not run: CI.\n- Not covered by the guard: `MatrixReport`, `ReleasePr*`, and the decision and intent types. These were checked only by a derive scan.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GBahqXqdScCmX73edNiacz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr501_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\nTwo input-validation gaps found by the pre-1.0 audit of `docs/stability.md`.\n\n`[[fixed-group]]` and `[[linked-group]]` silently accepted unknown keys, so a typo'd key was ignored. Every other table already rejected them. Both group tables now reject unknown keys.\n\n`callisto pre enter \"bad tag!\"` succeeded and wrote `pre.json`, and the next `version` failed with a confusing SemVer error. `pre enter` now validates its tag with the same validator as `snapshot --tag` (one `validate_tag`, E324, variant renamed `TagInvalid`) and writes nothing on failure. `pre enter` still allows dotted identifiers such as `beta.1` and `rc.2`, which are valid SemVer, while `snapshot --tag` stays single-identifier. An empty tag keeps its existing E279.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nA config with a stray key in a group block now fails to load. No previously valid pre tag is rejected.\n\n## Verify\n\nA table-driven test puts a typo'd key in each of the 12 config tables and asserts each is rejected naming the key. Removing `deny_unknown_fields` fails it, and so does applying the strict single-identifier rule at `pre enter`. `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n\nThis touches adjacent rows of `docs/errors.md` with the error-code PR (#500), so expect a trivial conflict.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PqwNxqffsEz174E3fLD2ea","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 498 --title \"fix(model): serialize every JSON field in camelCase\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr498_final.md && gh pr edit 501 --title \"fix(config): reject unknown group keys and invalid pre tags\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr501_final.md","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
