{"parentUuid":"4e2fd0bb-cc04-458d-9c3c-92acbf2b7c42","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0cc45ce1-ea7c-4682-bd8e-824395cb240d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:19:06.894Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"c9646b16f73fd97a6927f2f51c691761dfaeee867e3db772223baa08e284206a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CMVDRzAxqpsN77tmYpYqFg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr499_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\n`callisto release pending --format json` and the hidden `release build-python --format json` now carry the standard envelope (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`), with `pending` and `built` unchanged. A failing run reports `command: \"release pending\"` or `\"release build-python\"` instead of `\"release\"`. `docs/stability.md` promises `schemaVersion` on every `--format json` report from 1.0.\n\nNew tests run the real binary and assert the error envelope, with and without `--dry-run`, for every command family. They also lock in the earlier fix to `release plan` and `release-pr` subcommands, which already report the right `command` on main. `release inspect` success still prints the raw input document by design. REL-CMD-12 in `docs/specs/release.json` now lists both commands.\n\n## Verify\n\n`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Passing `false` instead of the real `--dry-run` flag makes the new tests fail. CI has not run. There is no `build-python` success-path test because it needs a Python toolchain.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014C2pDcWQ73aJWyTVHKPXj1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr500_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\n`docs/stability.md` says that from 1.0 an error code keeps its meaning, so each code has to name a single condition.\n\n- `callisto.toml`: E111 now means only \"not valid TOML\". An unknown key is E325. A wrong-typed value or a missing required key is E326. `config::load` and `init` share one `parse_raw` in `config/resolve.rs`.\n- `release pending --from`: a value that is not a full 40-character SHA is E327. A valid SHA that is not a release commit on this branch is E328. Both used to report E171, which means \"internal release invariant violated, report it\".\n- `docs/errors.md` documents the new codes.\n\n## Breaking\n\nScripts that match E111 for an unknown key or wrong-type value, or E171 for a bad `--from`, stop matching and must use E325, E326, E327 or E328. Exit codes are unchanged.\n\n## Verify\n\nSix new tests in `error_code_hygiene_tests.rs` run the real binary:\n- A bad `--from` gives E327 or E328, never E171.\n- A syntax error gives E111.\n- An unknown key gives E325.\n- A wrong type gives E326.\n- Every new code is documented.\n\nBreaking the unknown-field detection makes the unknown-key test fail. `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\nE254 (\"unknown callisto key\") still covers several config conditions. A few E171 sites in `release/binding.rs` and `release/derive.rs` look reachable through config but were not verified.\n\nThis overlaps the input-validation PR (#501) only in adjacent rows of `docs/errors.md`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NDm3Q1MxgbB8fbLHr15fu1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 499 --title \"fix(cli): give release pending and build-python the report envelope\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr499_final.md && gh pr edit 500 --title \"fix(errors): give each error code one meaning\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr500_final.md","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
