{"parentUuid":"171b1840-4cba-4e2d-acd8-e31e62e6a5a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguoDJe8MHDdoYkvggWLd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BSRCj5mvLCRkLcLywWjP3t","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"exit-code-2","description":"Exit 2 for usage-class errors","prompt":"Task: make usage errors exit 2, as docs/stability.md promises (\"Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/usage-exit-code origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nProblem (found by an audit, reproduced with the built binary): clap-level mistakes already exit 2, but every runtime check of a user-supplied value exits 1, because crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs (around line 48) maps every `Err` to `ExitCode::FAILURE`. Examples that should be usage errors (exit 2): `add --package a:patch` (E317, no ecosystem), `add --package cargo/a:bogus` (E271, bad severity), `add --package x` with no `--summary` (E274), `add` with no TTY and no `--package` (E214), `init` without `--yes` when stdin is not a terminal (E240), `snapshot --tag \"a/b c\"` and `pre enter \"bad tag!\"` (E324, if that exists on your base; it may not), `init --workflow --no-workflow` (E242), `--summary \"\"` (E275), a malformed `--package` selector, bad `--from` value, conflicting flags checked in code.\n\nRequired:\n1. Decide the classification by error CODE, in ONE place: a single function (for example `fn is_usage_error(code) -> bool` or a method on the CLI error type) listing the codes that mean \"the user passed a bad value or a bad combination of flags\". Walk docs/errors.md and the error enums to classify every code: usage-class means the command line input was wrong or incomplete; everything about workspace state, config content, git, registries, network, release preconditions stays exit 1. Be conservative: when unsure, leave exit 1 and list the code in your report. Put the classification where a new code forces a decision (for example an exhaustive match on the error enums, or a test that fails when a code in docs/errors.md is neither classified usage nor explicitly listed as runtime).\n2. main.rs exits 2 for those and 1 for the rest, for text and JSON output alike. The JSON error envelope is unchanged.\n3. docs/stability.md: reword the exit-code row only if needed so it says what is true (for example \"2 usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing\"). docs/errors.md: add a column or note only if the repo already documents exit codes per code; otherwise do not.\n4. Tests (fail before, pass after) driving the real binary: at least one case per example above that exists on your base (E317, E271, E274, E214, E240, E242, E275) exits 2, a representative runtime failure (an unknown package E102, an invalid config) still exits 1, and the classification test described in 1.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words, which commands now exit 2 instead of 1 and what a script that checks `$? -eq 1` sees (that is a behavior change; I will write the changeset with an upgrade note). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check (classify nothing as usage and confirm the tests fail). Final report: the full classification (usage vs runtime, per code), files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":750684,"output_tokens":3292,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":401},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3292,"cache_read_input_tokens":750684,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BSRCj5mvLCRkLcLywWjP3t":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"exit-code-2","description":"Exit 2 for usage-class errors","prompt":"Task: make usage errors exit 2, as docs/stability.md promises (\"Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/usage-exit-code origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nProblem (found by an audit, reproduced with the built binary): clap-level mistakes already exit 2, but every runtime check of a user-supplied value exits 1, because crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs (around line 48) maps every `Err` to `ExitCode::FAILURE`. Examples that should be usage errors (exit 2): `add --package a:patch` (E317, no ecosystem), `add --package cargo/a:bogus` (E271, bad severity), `add --package x` with no `--summary` (E274), `add` with no TTY and no `--package` (E214), `init` without `--yes` when stdin is not a terminal (E240), `snapshot --tag \"a/b c\"` and `pre enter \"bad tag!\"` (E324, if that exists on your base; it may not), `init --workflow --no-workflow` (E242), `--summary \"\"` (E275), a malformed `--package` selector, bad `--from` value, conflicting flags checked in code.\n\nRequired:\n1. Decide the classification by error CODE, in ONE place: a single function (for example `fn is_usage_error(code) -> bool` or a method on the CLI error type) listing the codes that mean \"the user passed a bad value or a bad combination of flags\". Walk docs/errors.md and the error enums to classify every code: usage-class means the command line input was wrong or incomplete; everything about workspace state, config content, git, registries, network, release preconditions stays exit 1. Be conservative: when unsure, leave exit 1 and list the code in your report. Put the classification where a new code forces a decision (for example an exhaustive match on the error enums, or a test that fails when a code in docs/errors.md is neither classified usage nor explicitly listed as runtime).\n2. main.rs exits 2 for those and 1 for the rest, for text and JSON output alike. The JSON error envelope is unchanged.\n3. docs/stability.md: reword the exit-code row only if needed so it says what is true (for example \"2 usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing\"). docs/errors.md: add a column or note only if the repo already documents exit codes per code; otherwise do not.\n4. Tests (fail before, pass after) driving the real binary: at least one case per example above that exists on your base (E317, E271, E274, E214, E240, E242, E275) exits 2, a representative runtime failure (an unknown package E102, an invalid config) still exits 1, and the classification test described in 1.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words, which commands now exit 2 instead of 1 and what a script that checks `$? -eq 1` sees (that is a behavior change; I will write the changeset with an upgrade note). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check (classify nothing as usage and confirm the tests fail). Final report: the full classification (usage vs runtime, per code), files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8df9345a-06cb-4c30-8f52-f9296963d999","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CguoDJGoSLNSP5taCpHCp","requestRef":"9c739072-f918-49c3-9c7f-52ddc4517d0e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e3f5533f-1abb-4daa-b2d5-53054271b33b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:27:01.875Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"e3f5533f-1abb-4daa-b2d5-53054271b33b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguoDJe8MHDdoYkvggWLd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0167nFStiwsmbDqGdMhyQVjN","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"cli-polish","description":"Pre-1.0 CLI consistency fixes","prompt":"Task: four small pre-1.0 consistency fixes found by an audit, plus one doc rewording. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/cli-polish origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\n1. `callisto add --package cargo/a:patch --package cargo/a:major` writes `a: patch` and `a: major` into one changeset file, which Callisto's own reader then rejects (`status` shows an error diagnostic and `status --check` exits 1). Reject a duplicate package in `add` with a coded error naming the package (follow how errors and codes are allocated and documented here; use the next free number and document it in docs/errors.md; also covers the interactive wizard path if it can produce duplicates). Test with the real binary: duplicate (same severity and different severity) is rejected, nothing is written, and a normal multi-package add still works.\n2. `snapshot --strict` help text says \"abort on error diagnostics\", but graph errors always abort (`abort_on_graph_errors`, crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/mod.rs around line 23); `--strict` only escalates warnings, as it does on `status` and `version`. Fix the help text on every command that documents `--strict` so each describes what it really does; check `callisto <cmd> --help` output with the built binary for status, version and snapshot. There may be a help-text exactness test (cli.rs has one for status); update it.\n3. `status --format json` prints `lastReleasedVersion: null` but omits `lastTag` when there is none. Make the field set stable: print `lastTag: null` the same way. Check the other optional fields of the status, version and snapshot reports for the same inconsistency and fix only the obvious ones; list the rest. Keep the report's `schemaVersion` as is (adding a null field is additive). Update the spec criterion if one describes the field.\n4. The Action input `version_command` (callisto-action) is word-split with `read -ra` in .github/actions/callisto-action/scripts/create-or-update-release-pr.sh (around line 100), so it cannot take quoted arguments, and Callisto appends --emit-decision to it. Document that in the input's description in .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml (one or two sentences). Do not change the script. The repo runs workflow contract checks (`just workflow-contracts`); run it, and note that policy forbids new secrets or write permissions, which this does not need.\n5. docs/stability.md says changesets for other ecosystems use `ecosystem/name` keys, but the code writes the bare name (`a: minor`) and qualifies only when the name is ambiguous across ecosystems. Reword the Changesets row to say that: compatible with `@changesets/cli`; the bare package name is the key unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, in which case the key is `ecosystem/name`. Check docs/architecture and docs/specs for a statement that contradicts the wording and fix it to match, listing what you changed.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change per item; no new dependencies; match surrounding comment density. Do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words, what a user sees now versus before for items 1 to 3. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just workflow-contracts` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on the item 1 and item 3 tests. Final report: per item what changed, files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":750684,"output_tokens":3292,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":401},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3292,"cache_read_input_tokens":750684,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0167nFStiwsmbDqGdMhyQVjN":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"cli-polish","description":"Pre-1.0 CLI consistency fixes","prompt":"Task: four small pre-1.0 consistency fixes found by an audit, plus one doc rewording. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/cli-polish origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\n1. `callisto add --package cargo/a:patch --package cargo/a:major` writes `a: patch` and `a: major` into one changeset file, which Callisto's own reader then rejects (`status` shows an error diagnostic and `status --check` exits 1). Reject a duplicate package in `add` with a coded error naming the package (follow how errors and codes are allocated and documented here; use the next free number and document it in docs/errors.md; also covers the interactive wizard path if