{"parentUuid":"e3f5533f-1abb-4daa-b2d5-53054271b33b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"21f07cf6-a1a1-4b2f-b072-8ee55568efb0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BSRCj5mvLCRkLcLywWjP3t","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a24178b2c45873db7 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a24178b2c45873db7', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a24178b2c45873db7.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"db1abde8-1d0e-4cae-a7b4-792e870feef2","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:27:11.314Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a24178b2c45873db7","description":"Exit 2 for usage-class errors","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Task: make usage errors exit 2, as docs/stability.md promises (\"Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: your worktree starts on an unrelated branch. First `git switch -c fix/usage-exit-code origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nProblem (found by an audit, reproduced with the built binary): clap-level mistakes already exit 2, but every runtime check of a user-supplied value exits 1, because crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs (around line 48) maps every `Err` to `ExitCode::FAILURE`. Examples that should be usage errors (exit 2): `add --package a:patch` (E317, no ecosystem), `add --package cargo/a:bogus` (E271, bad severity), `add --package x` with no `--summary` (E274), `add` with no TTY and no `--package` (E214), `init` without `--yes` when stdin is not a terminal (E240), `snapshot --tag \"a/b c\"` and `pre enter \"bad tag!\"` (E324, if that exists on your base; it may not), `init --workflow --no-workflow` (E242), `--summary \"\"` (E275), a malformed `--package` selector, bad `--from` value, conflicting flags checked in code.\n\nRequired:\n1. Decide the classification by error CODE, in ONE place: a single function (for example `fn is_usage_error(code) -> bool` or a method on the CLI error type) listing the codes that mean \"the user passed a bad value or a bad combination of flags\". Walk docs/errors.md and the error enums to classify every code: usage-class means the command line input was wrong or incomplete; everything about workspace state, config content, git, registries, network, release preconditions stays exit 1. Be conservative: when unsure, leave exit 1 and list the code in your report. Put the classification where a new code forces a decision (for example an exhaustive match on the error enums, or a test that fails when a code in docs/errors.md is neither classified usage nor explicitly listed as runtime).\n2. main.rs exits 2 for those and 1 for the rest, for text and JSON output alike. The JSON error envelope is unchanged.\n3. docs/stability.md: reword the exit-code row only if needed so it says what is true (for example \"2 usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing\"). docs/errors.md: add a column or note only if the repo already documents exit codes per code; otherwise do not.\n4. Tests (fail before, pass after) driving the real binary: at least one case per example above that exists on your base (E317, E271, E274, E214, E240, E242, E275) exits 2, a representative runtime failure (an unknown package E102, an invalid config) still exits 1, and the classification test described in 1.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset; instead return, in plain words, which commands now exit 2 instead of 1 and what a script that checks `$? -eq 1` sees (that is a behavior change; I will write the changeset with an upgrade note). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check (classify nothing as usage and confirm the tests fail). Final report: the full classification (usage vs runtime, per code), files changed, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a24178b2c45873db7.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8df9345a-06cb-4c30-8f52-f9296963d999","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","branch":"fix/input-validation","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e3f5533f-1abb-4daa-b2d5-53054271b33b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"db1abde8-1d0e-4cae-a7b4-792e870feef2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","toolUseID":"toolu_01BSRCj5mvLCRkLcLywWjP3t","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"agent-a99fea3d03893e29f\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Agent\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":66},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bc03cdba-a9a2-4198-aed4-3229b8d6eb4f","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:27:11.313Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"bc03cdba-a9a2-4198-aed4-3229b8d6eb4f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"sandbox_instructions","content":"## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for them. If the task cannot be finished with what you were given, do what you can and tell the user plainly what is missing instead of finding another way to it; that report is a complete answer.\n\nHow the sandbox is configured in this session:\nFilesystem: {\"read\":{\"denyOnly\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/ide\",\"~/.config/orin-dx\",\"~/.cache/orin-dx\",\"~/Library/Application Support/OrinDX-PR-Bot\",\"~/Library/Caches/OrinDX-PR-Bot\"],\"allowWithinDeny\":[]},\"write\":{\"allowOnly\":[\"/dev/stdout\",\"/dev/stderr\",\"/dev/null\",\"/dev/tty\",\"/dev/dtracehelper\",\"/dev/autofs_nowait\",\"/tmp/claude\",\"/private/tmp/claude\",\"/Users/gabe/.npm/_logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/debug\",\".\",\"$TMPDIR\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.git\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a24178b2c45873db7\"],\"denyWithinAllow\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.d\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/local\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/daemon\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/shell-snapshots\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/session-env\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/workflows\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/commands\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/agents\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/routines\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/rules\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/output-styles\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/launch.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/CLAUDE.md\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/daemon.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature-iat.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.stamp.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/backups\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/loop.md\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/cowork_plugins\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/dev-mods\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/mcp-skill-archives\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/mcp-discovery-cache\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/shares\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/todos\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/statsig\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/access-audit\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/remote-settings-helper-consent\",\"... and 145 more (truncated for prompt size)\"]}}\n\n - You should always default to running commands within the sandbox. Do NOT attempt to set `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` unless:\n  - The user *explicitly* asks you to bypass sandbox\n  - A specific command just failed and you see evidence of sandbox restrictions causing the failure. Note that commands can fail for many reasons unrelated to the sandbox (missing files, wrong arguments, network issues, etc.).\n - Evidence of sandbox-caused failures includes:\n  - \"Operation not permitted\" errors for file/network operations\n  - Access denied to specific paths outside allowed directories\n  - Network connection failures to non-whitelisted hosts\n  - Unix socket connection errors\n - When you see evidence of sandbox-caused failure:\n  - If the `<sandbox_violations>` block names a denied host, re-run the command with that host in its `allowed_domains` (auto mode); otherwise retry with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` directly rather than asking in prose first — the retry itself goes through the permission gate (a user prompt, or the auto-mode classifier when auto mode is active)\n  - Briefly explain what sandbox restriction likely caused the failure. Be sure to mention that the user can use the `/sandbox` command to manage restrictions.\n - A sandbox denial on a credential, a file or a host that the task does not involve is the boundary above at work: tell the user rather than retrying with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`.\n - Treat each command you execute with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` individually. Even if you have recently run a command with this setting, you should default to running future commands within the sandbox.\n - Do not suggest adding sensitive paths like ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, ~/.ssh/*, or credential files to the sandbox allowlist.\n - Network egress goes through a filtering proxy. Attempt requests and read the error rather than predicting whether a host is reachable; denied connections are reported in a `<sandbox_violations>` block explaining the reason. In auto mode, list the hosts a command needs beyond that in its `allowed_domains` — a denied host named in the block goes there on the re-run.\n - If a command fails to bind or listen on a local port with \"Operation not permitted\" (EPERM), local port binding is off in this sandbox. Treat it as the sandbox-caused failure described above, and tell the user that `sandbox.network.allowLocalBinding: true` in their settings (it applies without a restart) allows it without leaving the sandbox.\n - Opening an app, file or URL with `open`, or scripting another app with `osascript`, is blocked inside this sandbox (macOS Launch Services and Apple Events are off) and fails with errors such as -10822 (kLSServerCommunicationErr), -54, -600 or \"LSOpenURLsWithRole() failed\". That failure is the sandbox, not a problem with what you built; do not retry it with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`. Tell the user the sandbox blocked it and give them the exact command to run themselves.\n - For temporary files, always use the `$TMPDIR` environment variable. TMPDIR is automatically set to the correct sandbox-writable directory in sandbox mode. Do NOT use `/tmp` directly - use `$TMPDIR` instead.\n - If a clipboard utility such as `pbcopy`, `xclip`, or `wl-copy` fails inside the sandbox and the user wants the text on their clipboard, put the text in a fenced code block in your response and tell them to run `/copy` (it copies from outside the sandbox; when the picker appears they can select just that block), rather than writing a file for them to copy manually."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"de14e339-bf8b-4f4b-b93b-b3c2a3bc56f9","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:27:11.362Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for them. If the task cannot be finished with what you were given, do what you can and tell the user plainly what is missing instead of finding another way to it; that report is a complete answer.\n\nHow the sandbox is configured in this session:\nFilesystem: {\"read\":{\"denyOnly\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/ide\",\"~/.config/orin-dx\",\"~/.cache/orin-dx\",\"~/Library/Application Support/OrinDX-PR-Bot\",\"~/Library/Caches/OrinDX-PR-Bot\"],\"allowWithinDeny\":[]},\"write\":{\"allowOnly\":[\"/dev/stdout\",\"/dev/stderr\",\"/dev/null\",\"/dev/tty\",\"/dev/dtracehelper\",\"/dev/autofs_nowait\",\"/tmp/claude\",\"/private/tmp/claude\",\"/Users/gabe/.npm/_logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/debug\",\".\",\"$TMPDIR\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.git\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a24178