s 1.\n- **Runtime (exit 1):** every other code in docs/errors.md, 233 in total. The full list is the `RUNTIME_CODES` string in `crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs`.\n\nLeft at exit 1 on purpose:\n- **E102, E103:** unknown or ambiguous package.\n- **E169, E189, E188:** valid values depend on workspace contents.\n- **E230, E232, E233, E308:** depend on the intent file or config. E232 and E233 are the `--artifact-manifest`/`--artifact-dir` checks.\n- **E272, E273:** the interactive `add` wizard.\n- **E281:** the `release-pr` JSON argument, which is input content rather than a flag value.\n- **E299:** init with no `origin` remote.\n- **E004:** an invalid SHA from the model crate.\n- **E259–E264:** tag-template config content.\n- **E277:** `--strict` escalation.\n- **E243, E244, E280:** pre-mode state.\n\nThe classification itself is a judgment, so the ones I am least sure of are E169, E189, E230, E232, E233, E281, E299, E216-E218 and E309. If you want any of them reclassified, the change is moving one code between the two lists.\n\n## Files changed\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs`: `USAGE_CODES`, `USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES` and `CliError::is_usage_error()`.\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/main.rs`: exits 2 when `is_usage_error()`, otherwise 1; header comment updated.\n- `docs/stability.md`: exit-code row now reads \"`2` usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing.\"\n- `crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs` (new).\n- `crates/callisto-cli/tests/release_artifact_owner_tests.rs`: the E231 test now expects exit 2 and is renamed `plan_with_only_the_artifact_repository_fails_with_e231`.\n- docs/errors.md is untouched; it has no per-code exit-code documentation.\n\n## New tests (all in `usage_exit_codes_tests.rs`, driving the real binary)\n- `every_documented_code_is_classified_usage_or_runtime_exactly_once`: fails when a code in docs/errors.md is in neither list, is in both, or is listed but not documented. This is what forces a decision for a new code.\n- `bad_or_missing_flag_values_checked_after_parsing_exit_2`: E317, E271, E274, E275, E214, E240, E242, E324 and E279 each exit 2 in JSON and text mode, and the JSON envelope code is checked.\n- `runtime_failures_still_exit_1`: E102 and E111.\n- `a_bare_package_in_config_exits_1_though_the_same_code_on_a_flag_exits_2`: a bare `match = \"a\"` in `callisto.toml` gives E317 with exit 1.\n\n## Checks\n- **Mutation check:** I made `is_usage_error` always return false, and `bad_or_missing_flag_values_checked_after_parsing_exit_2` failed. I then reverted it.\n- **`just lint`:** exit 0, re-run after the last edit.\n- **`just doc-check`:** exit 0.\n- **`cargo fmt --check`:** exit 0.\n- **`cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli --no-fail-fast`:** exit 101. The one failure caused by my change was the E231 test, which I fixed; that test file now passes. The other three failures are `test_full_polyglot_workspace_release_lifecycle`, `pnpm_and_uv_workspace_resolves_natively_after_snapshot` and `pnpm_and_uv_workspace_resolves_natively_after_version`. The sandbox denied network to npm, crates.io and github.com while they ran. I did not re-run them on the base to confirm they also fail there. The four tests in `usage_exit_codes_tests` pass.\n- Not run: `just ci`, `just pre-push` and `just test`.\n\n## Other\n- The base had no E324 problem; `snapshot --tag \"a/b c\"` is covered.\n- Run from a script, `init` prints a \"Detected:\" block to stderr before the JSON envelope, as it did before. The new test strips that prefix before parsing.\n- `package selector` E316 errors, raised from the identity resolver for selectors on other commands, still exit 1 because that context is not `--package`. This is the sibling gap I left; if you want it closed, it needs the resolver to say whether the selector came from a flag or from config."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPositio