both --orchestration-revision and --artifact-repository |\n| E195 | `--forge-repository` value is invalid | Use the GitHub `owner/repo` the product releases to. |\n| E196 | `--artifact-target` triple is invalid | Use distinct, non-empty Rust target triples. |\n| E216 | `release artifact-manifest` was run with `--dry-run`, but it needs an output file | re-run `callisto release artifact-manifest` without --dry-run |\n| E217 | `release plan` was run with `--dry-run`, but planning is already read-only and needs an output file | re-run `callisto release plan --out <file>` without --dry-run |\n| E218 | `release execute` was run with `--dry-run`, which it doesn't support | remove --dry-run; release execute has no read-only mode |\n| E309 | `release build-python` run with `--dry-run`, which cannot write build output | re-run `callisto release build-python` without --dry-run |\n| E283 | `help` named a subcommand that doesn't exist | run `callisto --help` to list commands |\n| E282 | `release-pr commit-plan` was run with both `--out` and `--dry-run` | re-run without --dry-run, or drop --out |\n| E298 | `init --forge-repository`/`--product-package` given without `--artifact-target` | Drop the flag, or pass --artifact-target to ship the product's binaries (flag named in the error). |\n| E281 | A `release-pr` `--decision`/`--snapshot` argument is not valid JSON | check the JSON is well-formed and matches the expected schema |\n| E232 | `--artifact-manifest`/`--artifact-dir` given, but the intent declares no artifact slots and the manifest seals no Python files | drop --artifact-manifest and --artifact-dir for an intent without artifact slots or sealed P\n| E233 | Intent declares artifact slots or the manifest seals Python files, but `--artifact-manifest`/`--artifact-dir` are missing | pass both --artifact-manifest and --artifact-dir |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"