{"parentUuid":"8e27bc83-c25d-464b-8d33-4b4dda5c4a49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgupAR1PhEfyMYxyUaRwy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AeA3Ax5jkJSGpQ2z1iB1zH","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr502-body","description":"PR body for 502","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr502.diff. Change: usage errors now exit 2, as docs/stability.md promises (\"0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error\"). Before, clap-level mistakes exited 2 but every runtime check of a flag value exited 1 because main.rs mapped every error to ExitCode::FAILURE. Now `CliError::is_usage_error()` classifies by error code: 27 codes (bad flag values and flag combinations, e.g. E317, E271, E274, E275, E214, E240, E242, E324, E279, and `--dry-run` misuse E216-E218, E282, E309, bad `release` flag values E195, E196, E224-E229, E231) exit 2; E316 and E317 exit 2 only when raised for a `--package` flag, so a bare name in callisto.toml still exits 1; every other documented code (233) exits 1, including workspace, config, git, registry and intent-file content errors. The JSON error envelope is unchanged. A test fails when a code in docs/errors.md is classified neither way, so a new code forces a decision. docs/stability.md exit-code row reworded to match.\nCompatibility: a script that checks `$? -eq 1` after a bad argument now sees 2; checking for non-zero is unaffected.\nVerified: new tests run the real binary (nine codes exit 2 in text and JSON mode; E102 and E111 still exit 1; a bare package in config exits 1 while the same code from a flag exits 2); a mutation making the classifier always return false fails them; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Follow-up: once the error-code PR (#500) merges, its new codes E325 to E328 must be classified (E327, a bad `--from` value, is a usage error) or the classification test fails.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 200 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1080,"cache_read_input_tokens":769539,"output_tokens":1610,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":514},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1080,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1610,"cache_read_input_tokens":769539,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1080},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AeA3Ax5jkJSGpQ2z1iB1zH":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr502-body","description":"PR body for 502","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr502.diff. Change: usage errors now exit 2, as docs/stability.md promises (\"0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error\"). Before, clap-level mistakes exited 2 but every runtime check of a flag value exited 1 because main.rs mapped every error to ExitCode::FAILURE. Now `CliError::is_usage_error()` classifies by error code: 27 codes (bad flag values and flag combinations, e.g. E317, E27