{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"99f72959-1de3-4267-8397-18f9a7cec5e4","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:39:28.948Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"a5d78a38c3b33787e5b5d9b7008e9de2db1c7b9a9ca69bf894342b554f4e1149","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"def1a097-4e7e-4266-8b21-7954b6d16b10","keep":1240,"tail":["7bb4c6b151e71908521351355f7eb3a8d077d0107e1faf56c0972884998eac23","379d6ec25315067b03aaf9c88e6f8a005f7514c63633e7cea20742e1c39a40b8","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1242,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"1ea9973361796163f22e4616c30f7c7732387806d76a48e7c6c4efb485dcb3ec"}
{"parentUuid":"e68cc9ca-ab17-4ebd-88e9-74075a32edb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgupBSzUm2xtZdUh36ixV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #502, exit 2 for usage errors, is open and linked to trail 177, and its description is being written. The full checks pass outside the sandbox, and CI hasn't run.\n\n- **Classification:** 27 codes exit 2 and 233 stay at exit 1. I checked each borderline code against `docs/errors.md`, and every code that moved to exit 2 describes a bad flag value or flag combination. E316 and E317 exit 2 only when raised for a `--package` flag, so a bare name in `callisto.toml` still exits 1. The codes tied to workspace or intent-file content (E232, E233, E281) stay at exit 1.\n- **Enforcement:** a test fails if any code in `docs/errors.md` is classified neither way, so a new error code forces someone to decide.\n- **Changeset:** minor, with an `Action:` note that a script checking `$? -eq 1` after a bad argument must also accept 2.\n\n**Semantic collision.** The five branches are textually conflict-free, but #500 adds codes E325 to E328, and #502's test requires every documented code to be classified. After #500 merges, #502 will fail that test until I classify them (E327, a bad `--from`, is a usage error). I'll do that right after #500 lands, so merge #500 first.\n\n**Merge order, then:** #500, then #501 (a one-line doc fix from me), then #502 (the classification update from me). #498 and #499 are independent.\n\n**Still running:** `cli-polish` (duplicate packages in `add`, the `--strict` help text, `lastTag: null`, the `version_command` doc, and the bare-names stability rewording).\n\nneeds input: review #498 to #502, merging #500 first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1841,"cache_read_input_tokens":770619,"output_tokens":556,"output_tokens_details":{"thin