{"parentUuid":"f60f38d9-37dc-4300-bfef-e55682fe92c0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4aeb4f90-1534-4532-b958-e3612a9fda02","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:39:48.025Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a24178b2c45873db7","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"f4d470a7db3d4b8e45d16460a357eda6539b64aa3077ebe69dadb1a2a580f7c7","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013DS7p1HaQSxKqZn7fCSdDc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr502_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\n`docs/stability.md` promises exit 2 for usage errors, but only clap-level mistakes did. Runtime checks of flag values exited 1 because `main.rs` mapped every error to `ExitCode::FAILURE`.\n\n`CliError::is_usage_error()` now classifies by error code. 27 codes exit 2: bad flag values and combinations, `--dry-run` misuse, and bad `release` flag values. E316 and E317 exit 2 only when raised for a `--package` flag, so a bare name in `callisto.toml` still exits 1. The other 233 documented codes exit 1, including workspace, config, git, registry and intent-file content errors. The JSON error envelope is unchanged.\n\nA test fails when a code in `docs/errors.md` is classified neither way, so a new code forces a decision. The `docs/stability.md` exit-code row is reworded to match.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nA script that checks `$? -eq 1` after a bad argument now sees 2. Checking for non-zero is unaffected.\n\n## Verify\n\nNew tests run the real binary: nine codes exit 2 in text and JSON mode, E102 and E111 still exit 1, and a bare package in config exits 1 while the same code from a flag exits 2. A mutation making the classifier always return false fails them.\n\n`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n\nFollow-up: once #500 merges, its new codes E325 to E328 must be classified (E327, a bad `--from` value, is a usage error) or the classification test fails.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0164U1u2deqp3bf59X44o33M","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 502 --title \"fix(cli): exit 2 for usage errors raised after argument parsing\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr502_final.md; gh pr list --state open --json number,headRefName --jq '.[]|\"\\(.number) \\(.headRefName)\"'","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
