 runs on the resolved package.\n  \n  **2. `--strict` help text**\n  - Before:\n    - `snapshot --strict` said \"Abort if the workspace graph contains error-severity diagnostics\". Graph errors abort with or without the flag, so that was wrong.\n    - `version --strict` said \"Treat warning-level diagnostics as errors\".\n  - Now:\n    - `snapshot --strict` says \"Treat warnings as errors (graph errors abort with or without it)\".\n    - `version --strict` says \"Treat warnings as errors, including finding no pending changesets\".\n    - `status` is unchanged (\"Treat warnings as errors (fails with --check)\"), and it was already accurate.\n  - Only status, version and snapshot document `--strict`.\n  \n  **3. `status --format json` fields**\n  - Before: a package with no tag had `lastReleasedVersion: null` but no `lastTag` key at all. The same happened for `pendingSeverity` when no bump was planned.\n  - Now: both print `null`, so every package record has the same keys. `schemaVersion` is unchanged. No other consumer needed changing; the one test that reads `pendingSeverity` already treats a missing key and null alike.\n  - I fixed `pendingSeverity` as well as `lastTag`, because it is the same kind of field in the same record. Say if you want only `lastTag`.\n  - The remaining optional fields that are omitted rather than null, which I left alone:\n    - `BumpRecord.governedBy` and `BumpRecord.reason`, in the version and snapshot reports.\n    - `VersionReport.lockfileRefreshResults`.\n    - `diagnostics` is omitted when empty on every report. This is a deliberate convention across all reports.\n    - I judged `governedBy`, `reason` and `lockfileRefreshResults` not obvious, because absence there carries meaning.\n  \n  ## Items 4 and 5 (docs only)\n  \n  - **Item 4:** the `version_command` input description in `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml` now adds \"The value is split on whitespace, so it cannot contain quoted arguments or a path with spaces.\" The script is untouched, and no new secrets or write permissions were needed.\n  - **Item 5:** the Changesets row in `docs/stability.md` now says it stays compatible with `@changesets/cli`, and that the bare package name is the key unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, in which case the key is `ecosystem/name`.\n    - Other docs: I found no contradicting statement in `docs/architecture` or `docs/specs`. `identity.md`, `polyglot-v1.md`, `workspace.json` and `errors.md` already say changeset entries keep native names and bare names resolve when unambiguous. Nothing needed changing there.\n  \n  ## Files changed\n  \n  **Code**\n  - `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/add.rs`\n  - `crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs` (new error `AddDuplicatePackage`, code E325, the next free number)\n  - `crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs`\n  - `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs`\n  \n  **Docs and spec**\n  - `docs/errors.md` (E325 row)\n  - `docs/specs/cli.json`: the `add` criterion gains the E325 sentence; the status criterion says `lastTag` and `pendingSeverity` are null; the snapshot error-condition text is corrected.\n  - `docs/stability.md`\n  \n  **Action**\n  - `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`\n  \n  **New test file**\n  - `crates/callisto-cli/tests/add_duplicate_package_tests.rs`\n  \n  ## New tests\n  \n  - `add_duplicate_package_tests::a_package_given_twice_is_rejected_and_nothing_is_written`. It runs the real binary on same-severity and different-severity duplicates, checks exit 1, E325 and the package name in stderr, and checks that `.changeset` holds no changeset.\n  - `add_duplicate_package_tests::distinct_packages_still_write_one_changeset`\n  - `callisto-model` `status_package_record_json_serializes_absent_options_as_null`\n  - `callisto-cli` `cli::tests::version_and_snapshot_strict_help_text_is_exact`. The existing status help-text test is unchanged.\n  - Another test, `retired_other_call_sites_now_carry_code_and_help`, now includes the new error variant.\n  \n  ## Commands and exit codes\n  \n  - `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-model --no-fail-fast`: exit 0.\n  - `just lint`: exit 0.\n  - `just doc-check`: exit 0.\n  - `just workflow-contracts`: exit 0.\n  - `just fmt` was also run.\n  \n  Inside the sandbox, `workflow-contracts` failed with exit 128 because gpg signing and github.com were blocked. The npm- and uv-based tests also failed there for lack of network. I re-ran with the sandbox disabled, and all passed. The final runs above were done that way.\n  \n  ## Mutation checks\n  \n  - I disabled the duplicate check in `add.rs`, and the new E325 test failed (exit 101).\n  - I restored `skip_serializing_if` on `last_tag`. My first version of the null test still passed, because indexing a missing key on a `serde_json` value returns null. I tightened it to `value.get(key) == Some(&Null)`, and it then failed (exit 101).\n  - Both mutations were reverted, and the final runs above are on the reverted code.\n  \n  ## Unsure about\n  \n  - Whether to also null-ify `pendingSeverity`, as noted above.\n  - E325 names the package as the user typed it (`cargo/a`). Internally the entry name is the display name (`a`).\n  - I did not add a changeset or commit, as instructed. Under the repo's changeset rule, this probably needs a short entry for items 1 and 3 before release.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"All five items are done on branch `fix/cli-polish`, uncommitted, with no changeset. All checks exit 0, and the mutation checks fail as expected.\n\nThe worktree started on an unrelated branch, so I ran `git switch -c fix/cli-polish origin/main`. The branch was created, but git could not write the upstream-tracking config (sandbox). It does not matter for this work.\n\n## What a user sees now versus before (items 1 to 3)\n\n**1. `add` with a repeated package**\n- Before: `callisto add --package cargo/a:patch --package cargo/a:major` wrote `a: patch` and `a: major` into one changeset. Callisto's own reader then rejected the file, `status` showed an error diagnostic, and `status --check` exited 1.\n- Now: `add` exits 1 with E325 (\"package `cargo/a` is listed more than once in `--package`\"). The help says to pass each package once, with the one severity the change needs. Nothing is written. The same applies when both severities match. A normal multi-package add (`cargo/a:patch`, `cargo/b:major`) still writes one changeset.\n- The interactive wizard cannot produce duplicates, because it picks from a unique list, so I left it alone.\n- Bare and qualified spellings of the same package (`a` and `cargo/a`) are caught too, since the check runs on the resolved package.\n\n**2. `--strict` help text**\n- Before:\n  - `snapshot --strict` said \"Abort if the workspace graph contains error-severity diagnostics\". Graph errors abort with or without the flag, so that was wrong.\n  - `version --strict` said \"Treat warning-level diagnostics as errors\".\n- Now:\n  - `snapshot --strict` says \"Treat warnings as errors (graph errors abort with or without it)\".\n  - `version --strict` says \"Treat warnings as errors, including finding no pending changesets\".\n  - `status` is unchanged (\"Treat warnings as errors (fails with --check)\"), and it was already accurate.\n- Only status, version and snapshot document `--strict`.\n\n**3. `status --format json` fields**\n- Before: a package with no tag had `lastReleasedVersion: null` but no `lastTag` key at all. The same happened for `pendingSeverity` when no bump was planned.\n- Now: both print `null`, so every package record has the same keys. `schemaVersion` is unchanged. No other consumer needed changing; the one test that reads `pendingSeverity` already treats a missing key and null alike.\n- I fixed `pendingSeverity` as well as `lastTag`, because it is the same kind of field in the same record. Say if you want only `lastTag`.\n- The remaining optional fields that are omitted rather than null, which I left alone:\n  - `BumpRecord.governedBy` and `BumpRecord.reason`, in the version and snapshot reports.\n  - `VersionReport.lockfileRefreshResults`.\n  - `diagnostics` is omitted when empty on every report. This is a deliberate convention across all reports.\n  - I judged `governedBy`, `reason` and `lockfileRefreshResults` not obvious, because absence there carries meaning.\n\n## Items 4 and 5 (docs only)\n\n- **Item 4:** the `version_command` input description in `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml` now adds \"The value is split on whitespace, so it cannot contain quoted arguments or a path with spaces.\" The script is untouched, and no new secrets or write permissions were needed.\n- **Item 5:** the Changesets row in `docs/stability.md` now says it stays compatible with `@changesets/cli`, and that the bare package name is the key unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, in which case the key is `ecosystem/name`.\n  - Other docs: I found no contradicting statement in `docs/architecture` or `docs/specs`. `identity.md`, `polyglot-v1.md`, `workspace.json` and `errors.md` already say changeset entries keep native names and bare names resolve when unambiguous. Nothing needed changing there.\n\n## Files changed\n\n**Code**\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/add.rs`\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs` (new error `AddDuplicatePackage`, code E325, the next free number)\n- `crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs`\n- `crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs`\n\n**Docs and spec**\n- `docs/errors.md` (E325 row)\n- `docs/specs/cli.json`: the `add` criterion gains the E325 sentence; the status criterion says `lastTag` and `pendingSeverity` are null; the snapshot error-condition text is corrected.\n- `docs/stability.md`\n\n**Action**\n- `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`\n\n**New test file**\n- `crates/callisto-cli/tests/add_duplicate_package_tests.rs`\n\n## New tests\n\n- `add_duplicate_package_tests::a_package_given_twice_is_rejected_and_nothing_is_written`. It runs the real binary on same-severity and different-severity duplicates, checks exit 1, E325 and the package name in stderr, and checks that `.changeset` holds no changeset.\n- `add_duplicate_package_tests::distinct_packages_still_write_one_changeset`\n- `callisto-model` `status_package_record_json_serializes_absent_options_as_null`\n- `callisto-cli` `cli::tests::version_and_snapshot_strict_help_text_is_exact`. The existing status help-text test is unchanged.\n- Another test, `retired_other_call_sites_now_carry_code_and_help`, now includes the new error variant.\n\n## Commands and exit codes\n\n- `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-model --no-fail-fast`: exit 0.\n- `just lint`: exit 0.\n- `just doc-check`: exit 0.\n- `just workflow-contracts`: exit 0.\n- `just fmt` was also run.\n\nInside the sandbox, `workflow-contracts` failed with exit 128 because gpg signing and github.com were blocked. The npm- and uv-based tests also failed there for lack of network. I re-ran with the sandbox disabled, and all passed. The final runs above were done that way.\n\n## Mutation checks\n\n- I disabled the duplicate check in `add.rs`, and the new E325 test failed (exit 101).\n- I restored `skip_serializing_if` on `last_tag`. My first version of the null test still passed, because indexing a missing key on a `serde_json` value returns null. I tightened it to `value.get(key) == Some(&Null)`, and it then failed (exit 101).\n- Both mutations were reverted, and the final runs above are on the reverted code.\n\n## Unsure about\n\n- Whether to also null-ify `pendingSeverity`, as noted above.\n- E325 names the package as the user typed it (`cargo/a`). Internally the entry name is the display name (`a`).\n- I did not add a changeset or commit, as instructed. Under the repo's changeset rule, this probably needs a short entry for items 1 and 3 before release."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":187,"turnIndex":236},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a24178b2c45873db7","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
