{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"935494fcde8582cdb3354d9e53005b4e4536ba82449f2d9504fe128d3b776efe","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The cli-polish result has a collision. It allocated E325 for the duplicate-package error, but #500 already uses E325 for unknown config keys. That's the same \"another agent may take the next number\" risk the error-code agent warned about. I'm having it move to E329, the next free number after #500's block."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016By9dj4GSCnYwFsBzc2yEH","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"cli-polish","summary":"Renumber duplicate-package error to E329","message":"Collision: PR #500 (branch fix/error-code-hygiene) already allocates E325 (unknown config key), E326, E327 and E328. Renumber your duplicate-package error from E325 to E329 everywhere: crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs, docs/errors.md (put the E329 row after E324 and keep the file's ordering convention), docs/specs/cli.json, your test assertions and any text that names the code. Do not touch E325 to E328 or reference them. Re-run the new tests, lint, doc-check and the error-registry architecture tests, and report only the delta plus exit codes (run the tests with the sandbox disabled if the sandbox blocks them). Still do not commit, push or sign."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
