{"parentUuid":"e610f92a-8ff0-4b77-9f0a-b511af4f8cb1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgupT9NH6pTFi631ur8wE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The agent is renumbering the duplicate-package error to E329. Here's where that leaves everything:\n\n**The code ordering across PRs**\n- **#500** takes E325 to E328.\n- **cli-polish** takes E329, for a duplicate `--package`. It's a bad flag combination, so it will be a usage error that exits 2, and I'll classify it when #502's classification test needs it.\n- **#502** needs E325 to E329 classified once #500 and cli-polish land: E327 and E329 are usage errors, and E325, E326 and E328 are runtime.\n\n**What cli-polish does (items from the audit)**\n- **`add`** rejects a package passed twice, instead of writing a changeset Callisto's own reader rejects.\n- **`--strict` help text** is corrected for `snapshot` and `version`.\n- **`status --format json`** prints `lastTag` and `pendingSeverity` as `null`, so every package record has the same keys.\n- **`version_command`** is documented as not taking quoted arguments.\n- **`docs/stability.md`** now says changeset keys are the bare name unless another ecosystem has a package of that name.\n\n**Merge order for the whole set**\n1. #500 (error codes), then I update #501 and #502 for it.\n2. cli-polish (once I open the PR), then I classify E329 in #502.\n3. #498, #499, #495 and #497 are independent.\n\nI'll open the cli-polish PR after the renumber, with its changeset covering the `add` rejection, the `status` fields and the corrected help text.\n\nneeds input: none now. I'll finish the cli-polish PR when the renumber lands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1761,"cache_read_input_tokens":778303,"output_tokens":533,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_